# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Adapter in front of the sidecar:** The ``gitea-mcp`` sidecar runs as compose service ``giteamcpupstream`` on the role’s own network only, so nothing but the adapter reaches it. It answers ``initialize`` and ``tools/list`` to any caller because it holds no credential of its own and expects each client to supply a Gitea token per request, which makes it unsafe to expose directly. The adapter is what authenticates: a client presents the ``mcp_bearer`` credential and is refused with 401 otherwise, and the adapter presents the minted Gitea token upstream via ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY``."
msgstr "**Adapteris blakusvāģa priekšā:** E ir o pa s ``gitea-mcp`` blakusvāģis darbojas kā komponēt pakalpojums ``giteamcpupstream`` par lomu tikai tīklā, tāpēc nekas, bet adapteris sasniedz to. Tā atbild ``initialize`` kā arī ``tools/list`` jebkuram zvanītājam, jo tam nav sava akreditācijas, un sagaida, ka katrs klients sniegs Gitea marķieris pēc pieprasījuma, kas padara to nedrošu pakļaut tieši. adapteris ir tas, kas autentificē: klients piedāvā ``mcp_bearer`` credential un atsaka ar 401 citādi, un adapteris piedāvā kalti Gitea augšpusē caur ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Adapter in front of the sidecar:** The `gitea-mcp` sidecar runs as compose service `giteamcpupstream` on the role's own network only, so nothing but the adapter reaches it. It answers `initialize` and `tools/list` to any caller because it holds no credential of its own and expects each client to supply a Gitea token per request, which makes it unsafe to expose directly. The adapter is what authenticates: a client presents the `mcp_bearer` credential and is refused with 401 otherwise, and the adapter presents the minted Gitea token upstream via `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY`."
