# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO authentication:** Access is protected by Keycloak via oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "**SSO autentifikācija:** Piekļuvi aizsargā Keycloak caur oautu2- proksi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO flavor is `oauth2`** (oauth2-proxy sidecar → Keycloak), NOT native OIDC — because Checkmk Raw has no OIDC. The oauth2-proxy authenticates against Keycloak and passes `X-Remote-User`; Checkmk's site Apache trusts it via `auth_by_http_header`. This mirrors [`web-app-openproject`](../../roles/web-app-openproject/)'s header-SSO bridge (`OPENPROJECT_AUTH__SOURCE__SSO_HEADER` + LDAP-gated header trust)."
msgstr "**SSO aromāts `oauth2`** (oauts2- proksimāls blakusvāģis → Keycloak), NAV dzimtā OIDC – jo Checkmk Ravai nav OIDC. Zvaigzne2- proxy autentifikācijas pret Keycloak un iet `X-Remote-User`; Checkmk vietne Apache uzticas tai, izmantojot `auth_by_http_header`. Šis spogulis [`web-app-openproject`](../../roles/web-app-openproject/)galvenes- SSO tilts (`OPENPROJECT_AUTH__SOURCE__SSO_HEADER` + LDAP-ged header trust)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO round-trip test:** ``test-oidc-login.js`` drives ``/sso/key/generate`` through the Keycloak login form and asserts the UI no longer falls back to its own password gate."
msgstr "**SSO tests turp un atpakaļ:** ``test-oidc-login.js`` diskus ``/sso/key/generate`` caur Keycloak pieteikšanās formu un apgalvo, ka UI vairs nekrīt atpakaļ uz savu paroli vārtiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO round-trip test:** `test-oidc-login.js` drives `/sso/key/generate` through the Keycloak login form and asserts the UI no longer falls back to its own password gate."
msgstr "**SSO tests turp un atpakaļ:** `test-oidc-login.js` diskus `/sso/key/generate` caur Keycloak pieteikšanās formu un apgalvo, ka UI vairs nekrīt atpakaļ uz savu paroli vārtiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via Keycloak:** configured automatically on first deploy."
msgstr "**SSO caur Keycloak:** Automātiski konfigurēts pirmajā atrašanās vietā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted `Remote-Email` header (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); an `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, adapted from [PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n's own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via oauth2- starpniekserveri ar automātisku piegādi:** V1 vārti visu piekļuvi caur koplietošanas Keycloak OIDC klients (oauts2- proksi mala). opresty pārsūta autentificēto identitāti uz n8n kā uzticams `Remote-Email` galvene (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` skripts (`files/hooks.js`, pielāgots no [PavelSozonov/n8n-community-so](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) lasīt, ka galvene, auto-noteikumi vietējā n8n lietotājs pirmajā pierakstīšanās, un jautājumi n8n ir paša sesijas cookie - tāpēc katrs Keycloak lietotājs nolaižas tieši darbplūsmas redaktorā, bez otra, n8n-lokāla pieteikšanās solis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted ``Remote-Email`` header (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); an ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, adapted from `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n’s own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via oauth2- starpniekserveri ar automātisku piegādi:** V1 vārti visu piekļuvi caur koplietošanas Keycloak OIDC klients (oauts2- proksi mala). opresty pārsūta autentificēto identitāti uz n8n kā uzticams ``Remote-Email`` galvene (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` skripts (``files/hooks.js``, pielāgots no `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) lasīt, ka galvene, auto-noteikumi vietējā n8n lietotājs pirmajā pierakstīšanās, un jautājumi n8n’s pašas sesijas sīkfails - tāpēc katru Keycloak lietotājs nolaižas tieši darbplūsmas redaktorā, bez otra, n8n-lokāla pieteikšanās solis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM's own SAML login against Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall's SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to `/saml/acs` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak's realm descriptor by [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a `.onion` issuer is unresolvable directly. `/auth` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** ir SuiteCRMpaša SAML pieteikšanās pret Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` skaits [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)), nevis starpnieks tā priekšā. Neautenticated pieprasījumi hit Symfony ugunsmūris ir SAML ieejas punkts, kas novirza uz Keycloak; apgalvojums nāk atpakaļ `/saml/acs` un izveido reālu SuiteCRM sesija, tāpēc lietotne padara savu autentificētu UI, tostarp tās atslēgšanās kontroli. Konti tiek izveidoti pirmo reizi piesakoties no apgalvojuma (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), un IdP parakstīšanas sertifikātu nolasa no KeycloakName [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) boot, pār Tor SOCKS starpniekserveri, ja emitents ir sīpols, jo `.onion` emitents ir tieši noregulējams. `/auth` paliek sasniedzams kā vietējā break-stikla pieteikšanās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** ir SuiteCRMpaša SAML pieteikšanās pret Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` skaits ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` paliek sasniedzams kā vietējā break-stikla pieteikšanās."

