# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Your tools reachable from your assistants.** About twenty applications now speak MCP. Gitea, GitLab, Mattermost, Nextcloud, n8n, Baserow, Jenkins, Home Assistant, Moodle, Snipe-IT and WordPress serve their own endpoints; ten more get one through a locked-down sidecar. Open WebUI, Flowise and the agents discover what the deployment offers and register it automatically. Access is bounded rather than assumed: blocked paths are declared, every served path is gated, tools a provider calls mutating are withheld, reader and writer roles are separate, and each provider authenticates callers as its own service account. See [svc-ai-mcp-adapter](roles/svc-ai-mcp-adapter/README.md)."
msgstr "**Jūsu rīki sasniedzami no jūsu palīgiem.** Aptuveni divdesmit pieteikumi tagad runā MCP. Gitea, GitLab, Mattermost, Nextcloud, n8n, Baserow, Jenkins, Home Assistant, Moodle, Snipe-IT un WordPress kalpo savus galapunktus; vēl desmit iegūt vienu caur bloķētu blakusvāģi. Atvērt WebUI, Flowise un aģenti atklāt, ko izvietošana piedāvā un reģistrēt to automātiski. Piekļuve ir ierobežota, nevis pieņemts: bloķēti ceļi tiek deklarēti, katrs apkalpotais ceļš ir gated, rīki pakalpojumu sniedzēja zvani mutatis mutandis tiek ieturēti, lasītāja un rakstītāja lomas ir atsevišķas, un katrs pakalpojumu sniedzējs autentificē zvanītājus kā savu pakalpojumu kontu. Skatīt [svc-ai-mcp-adapter](roles/svc-ai-mcp-adapter/README.md)."

