# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Anything else gets `return 404`, and finding that out was worth the deploy. With `mcp.enabled` false, Baserow's canonical vhost still answered `401 Endpoint not found.` on `/mcp/<key>/sse`, because the image mounts the MCP app on the ASGI root unconditionally and the flag only governs whether an endpoint record is provisioned. A refused credential is still a surface, which is what the disabled-state assertion says and why it failed. The same routing has a sharper edge while MCP is *on*: the adapter narrows fourteen upstream tools to four, and a publicly routed native path walks straight past it to all fourteen for anyone holding the endpoint key. `web-app-homeassistant` had the same shape, an `exposure: internal` surface reachable on its public vhost. Both now 404 there and stay reachable on the container network, which is what `internal` was always supposed to mean."
msgstr "Viss pārējais kļūst `return 404`, un atklājot, ka bija vērts izvietot. kur: `mcp.enabled` Aplams, Baserow's kanonisko vhost joprojām atbildēja `401 Endpoint not found.` par `/mcp/<key>/sse`, jo attēls mount MCP lietotni uz ASGI saknes bez nosacījumiem un karodziņs nosaka tikai to, vai beigu punkts ieraksts ir paredzēts. Atteikts pilnvarojums joprojām ir virsma, ko saka invalīds un kāpēc tas neizdevās. Tai pašai maršrutēšanai ir asāka mala, kamēr MCP ir *par*: adapteris sašaurina četrpadsmit augšpusējos rīkus līdz četriem, un publiski maršrutēts vietējais ceļš iet tieši garām tam līdz visiem četrpadsmit ikvienam, kam ir galapunkta atslēga. `web-app-homeassistant` bija tāda pati forma, `exposure: internal` virsmas sasniedzams uz tās publisko vhost. Abi tagad 404 tur un palikt sasniedzams konteineru tīklā, kas ir tas, ko `internal` vienmēr bija domāts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Anything else — restating code, section banners, \"Note that …\", step narration outside sequential test specs, untracked TODO/FIXME — **DELETE before the edit lands**. Applies to every language and file kind under version control. When in doubt, delete."
msgstr "Jebkas cits – atkārtot kodu, sekciju baneri, \"Ņemiet vērā, ka ...\", posms ārpus secīgā testa specs, atsekots TODO/FIXME – **DELETE pirms rediģēšanas nolaižas**. Attiecas uz katru valodu un failu veidu saskaņā ar versiju kontroli. Kad rodas šaubas, dzēst."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Anything that wants to materialise the development inventory MUST go through :func:`build_dev_inventory` (single folder) or :func:`build_dev_inventory_matrix` (one folder per matrix-deploy round). Both flow through :class:`~.spec.DevInventorySpec` and own:"
msgstr "Visam, kas vēlas īstenot attīstības inventarizāciju, ir jāiziet cauri :func:`build_dev_inventory` (viena mape) vai :func:`build_dev_inventory_matrix` (viena mape katrai matrices izlikšanas kārtai). Abi plūst caur :class:`~.spec.DevInventorySpec` un kam pieder:"

