# priviliģētais `pull_request_target` izveidot pārbaudes **bāzi apvienot ref**
# (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) no bāzes repozitorija: PR izmaiņas saplūda uz bāzes,
# visas darbplūsmas un būvē-orchestration skriptus nāk no bāzes, nekad no
# dakšas. Tā kā `actions/checkout` citādi atsakās atnest PR ref zem
# `pull_request_target`, avota izrakstīšanās komplekti
# `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. Neuzticamais būvē iet **bez organizācijas
# noslēpumiem** — `secrets: inherit` nav pagājis, un tas autentificējas GHCR
# ar vienu darbu `GITHUB_TOKEN` tikai, tāpēc ļaunprātīgu dakša nevar lasīt
# repozitorija / organizēšanas noslēpumus. (E ir o pa s `pull_request_target`
# žetonu nēsātāji `packages: write`, Tāpēc `🛡️ Trusted` Etiķete joprojām ir
# īstā uzticības robeža visam ārpus attēla publicēšanas.)
# translation-refused: libretranslate protected-span lost=[] gained=['0010',
# '0020', '0220']
# nocheck: url
# translation-rejected: C0010 – C0020/R0220 **neuzticams** dakšu PR –
msgid "By default — for an **untrusted** fork PR — the privileged `pull_request_target` build checks out the **base merge ref** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) from the base repository: the PR's changes merged onto base, with all workflow and build-orchestration scripts coming from base, never from the fork. Because `actions/checkout` otherwise refuses to fetch a PR ref under `pull_request_target`, the source checkout sets `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. The untrusted build runs **without organization secrets** — `secrets: inherit` is not passed and it authenticates to GHCR with the per-job `GITHUB_TOKEN` only, so a malicious fork cannot read repository/organization secrets. (The `pull_request_target` token still carries `packages: write`, so the `🛡️ Trusted` label remains the real trust boundary for anything beyond image publication.)"
msgstr ""

