# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The make target ultimately calls the same CLI, so any behaviour described here applies to both."
msgstr "Mērķis galu galā sauc to pašu CLI, tāpēc jebkura šeit aprakstītā rīcība attiecas uz abiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The manager legs of steps 2, 4 and 9 run only when the app's include closure contains `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` / `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`. `utils/tests/swarm/backup_repos.py` derives both the manager's inventory groups and the `remote-2-local` provider list from that closure; apps without those roles prove the chain through the nfs repository."
msgstr "Vadītāja soļi soļi 2, 4 kā arī 9 palaist tikai tad, ja lietotne ietver aizvēršanu satur `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` / `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`. `utils/tests/swarm/backup_repos.py` iegūst gan pārvaldnieka inventāra grupām un `remote-2-local` pakalpojumu sniedzēju sarakstu no šīs slēgšanas; lietotnes bez šīm lomām pierāda ķēdi caur nfs repozitoriju."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The manifest document, or None when the generation carries none."
msgstr "Saraksta dokuments, vai Nav, ja paaudzei nav."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The manual entry workflow (`entry-manual-steer.yml`) sets `cancel-in-progress: true` on its own group, and the orchestrator's group cancels for `workflow_dispatch` regardless of ref, so a manual sweep supersedes on both levels, `main` included."
msgstr "Manuālā ieraksta darbplūsma (`entry-manual-steer.yml`) komplekti `cancel-in-progress: true` par savu grupu, un orķestra grupa atceļ par `workflow_dispatch` neatkarīgi no ref, tāpēc manuālā slaucīšana aizstāj abos līmeņos, `main` iekļauti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The map itself is generated, never tracked, so no second copy of a hostname can drift; ``utils.cache.render.render_artifacts`` writes it once the value-set is built."
msgstr "Pati karte ir izveidota, tā nekad netiek izsekota, tāpēc neviena otra resursdatora kopija nevar dreifēt; ``utils.cache.render.render_artifacts`` raksta to, kad vērtību komplekts ir uzbūvēts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The marked row carries `instructions: <mode>` in the matrix JSON and a 📖 in its job title, between the variant number and the ⭐ of a priority row."
msgstr "Atzīmētā rinda nes `instructions: <mode>` matricā JSON un 📖 darba nosaukumā starp prioritārās rindas varianta numuru un ;."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The marker adds `web-app-docs` to that row's `apps`, so the documentation is deployed beside the role under test. Its own CLI test then reads the role's page, takes the Production block out of the rendered HTML, and runs it."
msgstr "Marķieris pievieno `web-app-docs` uz šo rindu `apps`, tādējādi dokumentācija tiek izmantota papildus testa lomai. Tā paša CLI tests tad lasa lomu lapu, ņem ražošanas bloku no renderēta HTML, un vada to."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The marker file carries the same name as the swarm drill's (`scripts/tests/deploy/swarm/routine/backup/base.sh`) — one name for one concept. The implementations stay apart on purpose: the swarm drill follows a single token across five hops on four machines from the controller, which has nothing in common with marking every subject of one host beyond the three lines that write a file and read it back."
msgstr "Marķiera fails satur tādu pašu nosaukumu kā bara urbis (`scripts/tests/deploy/swarm/routine/backup/base.sh`) — viens nosaukums vienam jēdzienam. Īstenojumi palikt atsevišķi uz mērķi: bars urbis seko vienu žetonu pāri pieciem apiņiem uz četrām mašīnām no kontrolieris, kas nav nekas kopīgs ar marķēšanu katru priekšmetu viena uzņēmēja aiz trim līnijām, kas raksta failu un lasīt to atpakaļ."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The match stream is built once per process by `_scan.iter_matches` and shared across the four test classes; the repo-derived context (application defaults, user defaults, per-role schemas, `application_id`-declaring role set) comes from `_scan.get_context`. Validation helpers live in `_validate.py`. Suppression is wired through the project's `noqa` / `nocheck` grammar; the rule key is `lookup-config-path` (see [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md))."
msgstr "Sērkociņu straumi izveido `_scan.iter_matches` un dalīti četrās testa klasēs; no repo atvasinātais konteksts (lietotnes noklusējuma, lietotāja noklusējuma, per-role shēmas, `application_id`- pienākumu noteikšana) ir no `_scan.get_context`. Validācijas palīgi dzīvo `_validate.py`. Apspiešana ir vadu caur projekta `noqa` / `nocheck` gramatika; noteikumu atslēga ir `lookup-config-path` (skatīt [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md))."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matcher itself lives in :mod:`utils.cache.gitignore` (single SPOT for ``.gitignore`` parsing and matching). :func:`iter_non_ignored_files` here composes the cached project walk with that matcher and is the recommended helper for lint tests that want the \"files git would track\" view without subprocessing."
msgstr "Pats mačeris dzīvo :mod:`utils.cache.gitignore` (vienu SPOT ``.gitignore`` parsēšana un saskaņošana). :func:`iter_non_ignored_files` šeit veido kešatmiņas projektu staigāt ar šo matricas un ir ieteicama palīgs lint testiem, kas vēlas \"atrastu failu git\" skats bez apakšapstrādes."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matching Pull Request template defines PR structure, required author input, and review context. You MUST use the guidance in [Pull Request Templates](../artefact/git/pull-request.md) and orient your Pull Request to it."
msgstr "Atbilstošā Pull pieprasījuma veidne definē PR struktūru, nepieciešamo autora ievadi un pārskatīšanas kontekstu. Jums jāizmanto [Pull pieprasījuma sagataves](../artefact/git/pull-request.md) un orientējiet savu Pull pieprasījumu uz to."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The materialised application payload exposes services under the bare ``services`` key (no ``compose.services`` wrapper). The function name is preserved for backwards compatibility with existing call sites."
msgstr "Materializētā lietojumprogrammas lietderīgā krava pakļauj pakalpojumus zem kaila ``services`` atslēga (nav ``compose.services`` Apvalks). Funkcijas nosaukumu saglabā atpakaļsavietojamībai ar esošajām zvanu vietām."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix hands every row exactly one filesystem, so the value a deploy job sees is always narrow. Reading that narrowness as a demand would turn every condition the applying step is built to tolerate into a red row: a loop device it could not claim, a pool another job still holds, a kernel without the module."
msgstr "Matrice rokas katru rindu tieši vienu filesystem, tāpēc vērtība izvietot darbu redz vienmēr ir šaura. Lasot, ka šaurums kā pieprasījums varētu pārvērst katru nosacījumu pieteikšanās solis ir uzcelta, lai paciest sarkanā rindā: cilpas ierīce tā nevarēja pieprasīt, baseins cits darbs joprojām tur, kodols bez moduļa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix is **directional** (the row hosts the plugin/flag); bidirectional pairs such as `nextcloud`↔`openproject` carry a symbol in both cells. It is generated by [cli/build/docs/integration_matrix](../../cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/__main__.py): ☑️ edges are scanned from every role's `meta/services.yml` (the `sso`/`matomo`/`prometheus`/`email`/`dashboard`/`css`/`logout`/`cdn`/`coturn`/`collabora`/`onlyoffice`/`libretranslate` keys), and ✅/🪙 edges come from a curated, web-verified `EDGES` map. It MUST be regenerated rather than hand-edited. At creation time it covers 82 roles with **523 infinito-native (☑️) wired edges plus 96 curated upstream (✅/🪙) edges**. The ☑️ layer is exhaustive (it is scanned from the repo); the ✅/🪙 layer is **not yet exhaustive** and grows as each role's upstream plugin ecosystem is researched in depth (e.g. a MediaWiki deep-dive added `DiscourseSsoConsumer`, `PeerTubeEmbed`, `MachineTranslation`→libretranslate, `Extension:AWS`→minio, and an LLM editor→openwebui). The ✅/🪙 set is the **backlog**: every ✅ pair is an addon this requirement commits to declare and wire (see Acceptance Criteria), and completing the per-role upstream survey is itself an acceptance criterion."
msgstr "Matrice ir **virziena** (rindā atrodas spraudnis/flag); divvirzienu pāri, piemēram, `nextcloud`↔`openproject` nēsā simbolu abās šūnās. To rada [cli/build/docs/integration_matrix](../../cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/__main__.py): ☑️ malas skenētas no katras lomas `meta/services.yml` (gads `sso`/`matomo`/`prometheus`/`email`/`dashboard`/`css`/`logout`/`cdn`/`coturn`/`collabora`/`onlyoffice`/`libretranslate` taustiņi)un ✅/🪙 malas nāk no kūrēts, tīmekļa pārbaudīts `EDGES` karte. Tas ir jāatjauno, nevis jārediģē ar roku. Radīšanas laikā tas aptver 82 lomas ar **523 infinito-native (☑️) Vadu malas plus 96 kūrēts augšpus (✅/🪙) malas**. ☑️ slānis ir izsmeļošs (tas ir skenēts no repo); ✅/🪙 slānis ir **vēl nav pilnīga** un aug, jo katra loma ir augšpusējā spraudnis ekosistēma tiek pētīta padziļināti (piem., MediaWiki pievienoti dziļi dive `DiscourseSsoConsumer`, `PeerTubeEmbed`, `MachineTranslation`→libretranslate, `Extension:AWS`→minio un LLM redaktors→openwebui). ✅/🪙 iestatīts ir **neizskatīts**: katru ✅ pāris ir addon šī prasība apņemas deklarēt un stieples (Skatīt pieņemšanas kritērijus), un pabeigt per-lome augšpusējo apsekojumu pats par sevi ir pieņemšanas kritērijs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix is **directional**: the row hosts the plugin/flag. Bidirectional pairs (e.g. `nextcloud`↔`openproject`) carry a symbol in both cells, each linking to that side."
msgstr "Matrice ir **virziena**: rindā saimnieki spraudnis / Flag. Divvirzienu pāri (Piemēram, `nextcloud`↔`openproject`) uz abām šūnām ir simbols, kas savienojas ar šo pusi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix orchestrator (`utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py`) drives the deploy stage per variant round; `routine/00_one.sh` drives the surrounding stages for one distro, and the workflow `.github/workflows/call-test-deploy.yml` drives the distro loop. Run one app locally with `make swarm-zombie app=<id>` (keeps the cluster for inspection) or the whole matrix via `make roundtrip`."
msgstr "Matrices orķestris (`utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py`) virza izvēršanas stadiju katrā varianta kārtā; `routine/00_one.sh` vada apkārtējos posmus par vienu distro, un darbplūsmu `.github/workflows/call-test-deploy.yml` vada distro cilpu. Darbināt vienu programmu lokāli ar `make swarm-zombie app=<id>` (saglabā klasteri pārbaudei) vai visu matrici caur `make roundtrip`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix orchestrator needs these before it provisions, so that the authorized_keys reach host_vars through the merging ``--vars`` channel rather than through the replacing extra-vars file."
msgstr "Matrices orķestram ir nepieciešami šie, pirms tas paredz, lai authorized_keys sasniegt host_vars apvienojoties ``--vars`` kanālu, nevis, aizstājot extra-vars failu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix-variant planner (see [variants.md](variants.md)) calls the expansion once per round, so each round's inventory gets the right transitive closure for that round's variant set."
msgstr "Matrices variantu plānotājs (skatīt [variants.md](variants.md)) aicina paplašināšanu vienu reizi kārtā, tāpēc katra kārta inventarizācija saņem pareizo tranzītu slēgšanu, lai šīs kārtas variants iestatīts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mautrix network bridges are declared in ``meta/addons/`` as ``mechanism: bridge`` addons (requirement 026, Decision 13). Each is ``required: false`` and **disabled by default**; its per-network DB password and its appservice ``as_token``/``hs_token`` pair are referenced from ```meta/secrets.yml`` <./meta/secrets.yml>`__ ``credentials:``, never inlined. The role renders each bridge’s ``config.yaml`` and the matching Synapse ``registration.yaml`` from the same tokens."
msgstr "Mautrix tīkla tilti tiek deklarēti ``meta/addons/`` kā ``mechanism: bridge`` addons (prasība 026, Lēmums 13). Katrs ir ``required: false`` kā arī **izslēgts pēc noklusējuma**; tā katra tīkla DB paroli un tās appservice ``as_token``/``hs_token`` pāri norāda no ```meta/secrets.yml`` <./meta/secrets.yml>`__ ``credentials:``, never inlined. The role renders each bridge’s ``config.yaml`` and the matching Synapse ``registration.yaml`` no tiem pašiem žetoniem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mautrix network bridges are declared in `meta/addons/` as `mechanism: bridge` addons (requirement 026, Decision 13). Each is `required: false` and **disabled by default**; its per-network DB password and its appservice `as_token`/`hs_token` pair are referenced from [`meta/secrets.yml`](./meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:`, never inlined. The role renders each bridge's `config.yaml` and the matching Synapse `registration.yaml` from the same tokens."
msgstr "Mautrix tīkla tilti tiek deklarēti `meta/addons/` kā `mechanism: bridge` addons (prasība 026, Lēmums 13). Katrs ir `required: false` kā arī **izslēgts pēc noklusējuma**; tā katra tīkla DB paroli un tās appservice `as_token`/`hs_token` pāri norāda no [`meta/secrets.yml`](./meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:`, nekad nav iekļauti. Loma padara katra tilta `config.yaml` un atbilstošo sinapse `registration.yaml` no tiem pašiem žetoniem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The measurement decides **which** value each axis takes, never **whether** it takes one:"
msgstr "Mērīšana **kas** vērtība katrai asij, nekad **vai** tas aizņem vienu:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The merged map is what the inventory ALSO bakes into host_vars, so feeding the same dict into `CombinedResolver(services_overrides=...)` eliminates the topology-vs-host_vars drift that variant-blind resolution produced."
msgstr "Apvienotā karte ir tas, ko inventārs ARĪ bakes host_vars, tādējādi barojot to pašu dikt `CombinedResolver(services_overrides=...)` novērš topoloģiju-vs-host_vars dreifē, ka radīta varianta maskēta izšķirtspēja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The metrics endpoint needs a server-generated token that cannot be pre-seeded into a static scrape config from the inventory. Same pattern as `web-app-gitea`. Gives the `openbao_core_unsealed` gauge."
msgstr "Metrikas galauzstādījumam nepieciešams servera radīts marķieris, kuru nevar iepriekš iesmidzināt statiskā skrāpju konfigurācijā no inventāra. Tas pats modelis kā `web-app-gitea`. Dod `openbao_core_unsealed` gabarīti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The minimum env set for any spec following the persona flows is `APP_BASE_URL`, `CANONICAL_DOMAIN`, and `LOGOUT_URL`. `DASHBOARD_BASE_URL` is rendered only by the dashboard role's own spec, because consumer personas enter at `APP_BASE_URL` directly. Specs that gate on auth additionally read at least one of `OIDC_ISSUER_URL`, `KEYCLOAK_BASE_URL`, plus the persona credentials `ADMIN_USERNAME` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD` and `BIBER_USERNAME` / `BIBER_PASSWORD`. Specs that exercise integrations (Matomo, Discourse, Email, Prometheus, …) read the integration-specific keys defined in [Agent `playwright.env.j2`](../../../../agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md)."
msgstr "Minimālais env iestatījums jebkuram spec pēc personas plūsmas ir `APP_BASE_URL`, `CANONICAL_DOMAIN`, un `LOGOUT_URL`. `DASHBOARD_BASE_URL` tiek renderēta tikai paneļa lomu savu spec, jo patērētāju personas ievadīt `APP_BASE_URL` tieši. Specs ka vārti uz auth papildus lasīt vismaz vienu no `OIDC_ISSUER_URL`, `KEYCLOAK_BASE_URL`, kā arī personas pilnvaras `ADMIN_USERNAME` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD` kā arī `BIBER_USERNAME` / `BIBER_PASSWORD`. Specs, kas īsteno integrāciju (Matomo, Discourse, e-pasts, Prometheus, ...) lasīt integrācijas specifiskas atslēgas, kas definētas [Aģents `playwright.env.j2`](../../../../agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mirror workflow runs as stage 8 of the CI pipeline. See [ci.md](../git/pipeline.md). It runs in parallel with the DNS tests and MUST complete before deploy tests start."
msgstr "Spoguļa darbplūsma darbojas kā posms 8 CI cauruļvada. Skatīt [ci.md](../git/pipeline.md). Tas darbojas paralēli DNS testiem un jāpabeidz pirms izvietot testus sākt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The mirrors file is generated into the inventory directory. The inventory creator applies mirror image overrides to host variables via `cli/administration/inventory/provision/mirror_overrides.py`, which reads `mirrors.yml.applications` and writes `applications.{role}.services.{service}.image` (and `.version`) into host vars subject to the per-service `mirror_policy`."
msgstr "Spoguļu fails tiek ģenerēts inventarizācijas direktorijā. Inventāra veidotājs piemēro spoguļattēlu ignorē resursdatora mainīgos caur `cli/administration/inventory/provision/mirror_overrides.py`, kas skan `mirrors.yml.applications` un raksta `applications.{role}.services.{service}.image` (kā arī `.version`) saņēmēja vari, uz kuru attiecas pakalpojums `mirror_policy`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode is read as ``compose_mode_force or DEPLOYMENT_MODE`` rather than the bare cluster mode, because ``container_networks`` resolves attachments through that same effective mode: a role with an override must not lose its pin and its overlay at once."
msgstr "Režīms ir nolasīts kā ``compose_mode_force or DEPLOYMENT_MODE`` nevis tukša klastera režīmā, jo ``container_networks`` Atrisina pielikumus tādā pašā efektīvā režīmā: funkcija ar pārmiju nedrīkst uzreiz zaudēt savu pin un tā pārklājumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode selection is a *filter*, not an axis: ``--modes swarm`` keeps the rows whose role can be deployed as a swarm stack, ``--modes \"compose swarm\"`` keeps the rows at least one of the two can take. The shared filter is mode-clause + INFINITO_WHITELIST + INFINITO_BLACKLIST, the order is INFINITO_DISCOVERY_SORT, whose first key sorts clones last (one representative per dna cluster stays ahead of the budget cut, so redundant same-service-set variants fall behind it first), and the lifecycle envelope is INFINITO_LIFECYCLES."
msgstr "Izvēlētais režīms ir a *filtrs*, nevis ass: ``--modes swarm`` uztur rindas, kuru lomu var izvietot kā bara steku, ``--modes \"compose swarm\"`` saglabā rindas vismaz viens no diviem var veikt. Koplietotais filtrs ir režīma punkts + INFINITO_WHITELIST + INFINITO_BLACKLIST, rīkojums ir INFINITO_DISCOVERY_SORT, kura pirmā atslēga šķiro klonus pēdējo (viens pārstāvis uz vienu dna klasteri paliek pirms budžeta samazinājuma, tāpēc liekie viena un tā paša pakalpojuma varianti atpaliek no tā pirmā), un dzīves cikla aptver INFINITO_LIFECYCLES."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode sequence defaults to `compose swarm` and is overridable with `modes=\"compose swarm\"`. The order is always compose first, so the cheaper mode fails fast before the expensive swarm rebuild. Append `k8s` here once that mode exists."
msgstr "Režīma secības noklusējums uz `compose swarm` un tas ir aizstājams ar `modes=\"compose swarm\"`. Pasūtījums vienmēr ir komponēt pirmais, tāpēc lētāks režīms neizdodas ātri pirms dārgs bars pārbūvēt. Pievienot `k8s` šeit, kad šis režīms eksistē."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode the guide would replay *app* in, or ``''`` when it cannot."
msgstr "Režīms, ko ceļvedis atskaņos *lietotne* vai ``''`` kad tas nevar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The module is deliberately free of deploy-runtime imports: the CI selection resolves its closure on a runner that has no inventory, no container and no `INFINITO_SRC_DIR`."
msgstr "Modulis apzināti ir brīvs no izmantošanas laika importa: KI izvēle atrisina tā slēgšanu skrējējam, kam nav inventarizācijas, nav konteinera un nav `INFINITO_SRC_DIR`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mount MUST be available before Docker starts. Otherwise the daemon may fall back to the system drive or fail to start cleanly."
msgstr "Montāžai jābūt pieejamai pirms doka palaišanas. Pretējā gadījumā dēmons var atkrist atpakaļ uz sistēmas disku vai nedarboties tīri."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The name never holds a space: the ``whitelist`` and ``priority`` workflow inputs are space-separated lists, so a display name with a space in it would make a two-role list unparseable."
msgstr "Nosaukums nekad nav telpa: ``whitelist`` kā arī ``priority`` darbplūsmas ieejas ir ar atstarpi atdalīti saraksti, tāpēc displeja nosaukums ar atstarpi tajā padarītu divu lomu sarakstu neatdalāmu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The name of the matching role directory."
msgstr "Saskaņošanas lomu mapes nosaukums."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The names in declaration order, aliases substituted."
msgstr "Nosaukumi deklarācijas secībā, aizstājot ar citu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The names payload is stored under in THIS generation."
msgstr "Nosaukumi derīgo kravu uzglabā zem ŠĪS paaudzes."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The naming conventions below are additionally checked locally by the lint test [test_branch_name.py](../../../../tests/lint/repository/naming/test_branch_name.py), which fails `make test-lint` when the checked-out branch uses an unknown prefix (e.g. `feat/` instead of `feature/`) or a non-kebab-case description."
msgstr "Turpmāk minētos nosaukumu noteikšanas nosacījumus papildus pārbauda uz vietas, veicot linuma testu. [test_branch_name.py](../../../../tests/lint/repository/naming/test_branch_name.py), kas neizdodas `make test-lint` kad pārbaudītais zars izmanto nezināmu prefiksu (Piemēram, `feat/` vietā `feature/`) vai aprakstu, kas nav Kebab gadījumā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The narrow case is what a deploy job actually sees, because the matrix hands every row exactly one kind. Reading that narrowness as a demand would turn every condition the applying step tolerates into a red row on every deploy: a loop device it could not claim, a pool another job still holds. The run's own input decides instead."
msgstr "Šaurs gadījums ir tas, ko izvietot darbu faktiski redz, jo matrica rokas katru rindu tieši viena veida. Lasot, ka šaurums kā pieprasījums varētu pārvērst katru nosacījumu, piemērojot solis panes sarkanā rindā par katru izvietojumu: cilpas ierīce nevar pieprasīt, baseins cits darbs joprojām tur. Tā vietā izlemj paša palaišanas ievade."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The next `make compose-deploy mode=update apps=web-app-hugo` will pull the image, restart nginx, and serve the freshly rendered output."
msgstr "Nākamais `make compose-deploy mode=update apps=web-app-hugo` velciet attēlu, restartēt nginx, un kalpot tikko renderēta produkciju."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The next stage in the pipeline MUST NOT execute when the previous stage classified the plugin as `incompatible`."
msgstr "Nākamais posms cauruļvadā NEDRĪKST izpildīt, kad iepriekšējais posms klasificēts spraudnis kā `incompatible`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The nfs-server uses the userspace `nfs-ganesha` (`ganesha`) flavor in every runtime; `services.nfs-server.flavor` in `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/meta/services.yml` is the SPOT, and `kernel` is a per-inventory override. Ganesha is packaged for the `Debian` and `RedHat` os families only. Kernel `nfsd` in a privileged DinD node is wedge-prone: the export can be present yet the controller mount returns ENOENT, and `exportfs` can stick in D-state. If a swarm step hangs at `Reload NFS exports` from a stuck kernel-NFS mount, you MUST recover with `make swarm-clean` on the host; see the NFS gotcha in [Roundtrip Loop](roundtrip.md). You MUST NOT fall back to a compose-only sweep while swarm is blocked."
msgstr "Nfs serveris izmanto lietotāja vietu `nfs-ganesha` (`ganesha`) garša katrā skriešanas laikā; `services.nfs-server.flavor` skaits `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/meta/services.yml` ir SPOT un `kernel` ir inventārs. Ganesha ir iepakots `Debian` kā arī `RedHat` tikai os ģimenes. Kodols `nfsd` priviliģētā Dind mezgls ir ķīļa-prone: eksports var būt klāt, bet kontrolieris mount atgriež ENOENT, un `exportfs` var palikt D-state. Ja bara solis karājas `Reload NFS exports` no iestrēdzis kodols-NFS mount, jums ir atgūt ar `make swarm-clean` uz uzņēmēja; skatīt NFS gotcha in [Apaļsvītra cilpa](roundtrip.md). Jums nav jāatgriežas pie komponēt tikai slaucīšana, kamēr bars ir bloķēts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The nginx upstream map, the consumer compose override and the package managers' client configuration all follow from the ``cache:`` declarations in the roles' `meta/networks.yml`. None of them is tracked; this package regenerates them. Implementation lives in `utils.cache.render`."
msgstr "Nginx augšpusējā karte, patērētāju komponēšana un paketes pārvaldītāju klientu konfigurācija izriet no ``cache:`` paziņojumi par lomām” `meta/networks.yml`. Neviens no tiem nav izsekots; šis iepakojums tos reģenerē. Īstenošana `utils.cache.render`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The nightly timers (volume 01:00, nfs 01:30, secrets 01:45, device 02:00, remote pull 00:30) run independently of every step above and never fire during a lab run."
msgstr "Nakts taimeri (tilpums 01:00, nfs 01:30, Noslēpumi 01:45, ierīce 02:00, tālvadības pull 00:30) palaist neatkarīgi no katra soļa virs un nekad uguns laikā laboratorijas palaist."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The node hidden service exposes Mailu's mail ports in addition to `80`, via extra `HiddenServicePort` entries: `HiddenServicePort 25`, `587`, `465`, `143`, `993` → Mailu's local front binds on `127.0.0.1`. Mailu is then reachable at `<node>.onion` for SMTP/submission/IMAP."
msgstr "Mezgla slēptais serviss pakļauj Mailupapildus pasta portiem `80`, izmantojot papildus `HiddenServicePort` ieraksti: `HiddenServicePort 25`, `587`, `465`, `143`, `993` → Mailulokāla priekšpuse piesaistās `127.0.0.1`. Mailu pēc tam var sasniegt pie `<node>.onion` aizstāj SMTP/submission/IMAP."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The number of discarded translations; their entries keep no ``msgstr``."
msgstr "Noraidīto tulkojumu skaits; to ieraksti saglabā ``msgstr``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The number of dumps replayed."
msgstr "Izgāztuvju skaits atkārtojās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The oauth2 ACL in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) blacklists only `/login`, and `sys-svc-proxy` renders a blacklist as *expose everything by default, then protect the listed paths*. The helper lands on `/`, which is public, so the proxy never intercepts it and the Keycloak round trip never starts."
msgstr "Zvaigzne2 ACL in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) tikai melnie saraksti `/login`, un `sys-svc-proxy` padara melno sarakstu par *pakļaut visu pēc noklusējuma, tad aizsargāt uzskaitītos ceļus*. Palīgs nolaižas uz `/`, kas ir publiska, tāpēc starpnieks nekad pārtver to un Keycloak brauciens turp un atpakaļ nekad nesākas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The oauth2 ACL in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ blacklists only ``/login``, and ``sys-svc-proxy`` renders a blacklist as *expose everything by default, then protect the listed paths*. The helper lands on ``/``, which is public, so the proxy never intercepts it and the Keycloak round trip never starts."
msgstr "Zvaigzne2 ACL in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ blacklists only ``/login``, and ``sys-svc-proxy`` renders a blacklist as *expose everything by default, then protect the listed paths*. The helper lands on ``/``, kas ir publiska, tāpēc starpnieks nekad pārtver to un Keycloak brauciens turp un atpakaļ nekad nesākas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The offered modes are already narrowed by the run's ``--modes`` input, the onion states by its ``--tor`` input and the two pools by ``--distros`` and ``--filesystem``, so this catches a pin that fights the role, the variant, or the run's own axes with one check each."
msgstr "Piedāvātie režīmi jau ir sašaurināti ar palaist s ``--modes`` ievadi, sīpolu valstis tās ``--tor`` ieguldījums un divi baseini ``--distros`` kā arī ``--filesystem``, tāpēc tas nozvejas pin, kas cīnās ar lomu, variants, vai palaist savas asis ar vienu pārbaudīt katru."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The official Baserow SSO feature is Enterprise-only. This role instead gates the community image with the shared Keycloak oauth2-proxy and installs a small trusted-header bridge in the Baserow backend. The bridge trusts the identity headers injected by nginx after oauth2-proxy authentication and converts them into native Baserow JWT refresh/access tokens for the frontend."
msgstr "Amatpersona Baserow SSO funkcija ir tikai uzņēmums. Šī loma tā vietā vārti kopienas attēlu ar koplietošanas Keycloak oauts2- uzstāda mazu uzticamas galvas tiltu Baserow aizmugure. Tilts uzticas identitātes galvenēm, ko ievada nginx pēc oauth2- proxy autentificēšanu un pārvērš tos dzimtā Baserow JWT atsvaidzināšanas/piekļuves marķierierīces priekšpusei."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The official WordPress MCP adapter pinned, its HTTP endpoint exposed, only reviewed Abilities with permission callbacks registered, authenticated as a real restricted user."
msgstr "Amatpersona WordPress MCP adapteri pinned, tā HTTP galapunkts atklāts, tikai pārskatītas iespējas ar atļauju zvani reģistrēti, autentificēts kā reāls ierobežots lietotājs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The official installer is **downloaded at runtime** and verified before execution:"
msgstr "Oficiālais uzstādītājs ir **lejupielādēti darblaikā** un pārbaudīts pirms izpildes:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The offset a run was given, as written. ``None`` reads ``INFINITO_CI_OFFSET``; :func:`offset_index` decides what it means."
msgstr "Nobīde skrējiens tika dota, kā rakstīts. ``None`` lasītājs ``INFINITO_CI_OFFSET``; :func:`offset_index` izlemt, ko tas nozīmē."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The one accepted ``--set`` key shape for a credential override."
msgstr "Tā piekrita ``--set`` atslēgas formas credential ignorēšana."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The one-shot smoke mail the msmtp prefix puts in front of a probe."
msgstr "Vienšāviena dūmu pasts msmtp prefiksu novieto zondes priekšā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion axis of the CI deploy matrix: what it may do, and to which rows."
msgstr "CI sīpola ass izvieto matricu: ko tā var darīt un pie kādām rindām."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion identity (key files) is minted/reused by ``cli.administration.inventory.onion``; this provisioner is the single spot that writes the resulting address into ``applications.svc-net-tor.services.tor.node`` of the host_vars — so consumers read it via ``lookup('config', 'svc-net-tor', 'services.tor.node')`` with no env indirection."
msgstr "Sīpolu identitāte (atslēgas faili) to kaltu/atkārtoti izmantotu ``cli.administration.inventory.onion``; šis noteikums ir vienīgā vieta, kas raksta rezultātā adresi ``applications.svc-net-tor.services.tor.node`` priekšsēdētāja host_vars — lai patērētāji to lasītu caur ``lookup('config', 'svc-net-tor', 'services.tor.node')`` bez inv netiešas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion key is minted offline during inventory build (``cli.administration.inventory.onion``) and stored in the inventory, so the address is stable across redeploys and restorable from a backup."
msgstr "Sīpolu taustiņš tiek kalts bezsaistē inventarizācijas laikā (``cli.administration.inventory.onion``) un glabājas inventāra, tāpēc adrese ir stabila pārdislocēšanas un atjaunojamu no rezerves."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion key is minted offline during inventory build (`cli.administration.inventory.onion`) and stored in the inventory, so the address is stable across redeploys and restorable from a backup."
msgstr "Sīpolu taustiņš tiek kalts bezsaistē inventarizācijas laikā (`cli.administration.inventory.onion`) un glabājas inventāra, tāpēc adrese ir stabila pārdislocēšanas un atjaunojamu no rezerves."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion state is spelled `+clearnet` rather than `-tor` because a role id may itself end in `-tor`."
msgstr "Sīpolu stāvoklis ir uzrakstīts `+clearnet` nevis `-tor` jo loma id var pats beigties `-tor`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion state spells out as ``+tor``/``+clearnet`` rather than as a ``-tor`` suffix: a role id may itself end in ``-tor`` (``svc-net-tor``), and a suffix that eats the tail of a role name selects a different role in silence."
msgstr "Sīpolu stāvoklis nosaka kā ``+tor``/``+clearnet`` nevis kā ``-tor`` sufikss: loma id pats var beigties ``-tor`` (``svc-net-tor``), un sufikss, kas ēd astes lomu nosaukuma izvēlas citu lomu klusumā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The onion states one *mode* is worth running for a priority row."
msgstr "Sīpols nosaka vienu *režīms* ir vērts darboties prioritārā rindā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The only account that form accepts is Checkmk's built-in `cmkadmin`, whose password comes from `credentials.cmk_password` (`CMK_PASSWORD` in the container env) — a site-local secret unrelated to the Keycloak credentials the personas use. No Checkmk user is provisioned for a non-admin identity at all. With SSO enabled both personas run through the header-auth chain."
msgstr "Vienīgais konts, kuru veidlapa pieņem, ir: Checkmkir iebūvēts `cmkadmin`, kura parole nāk no `credentials.cmk_password` (`CMK_PASSWORD` konteinerā env) — vietējs noslēpums, kas nav saistīts ar Keycloak apstiprina personas izmantošanu. Nē Checkmk lietotājs ir paredzēts, lai vispār nav admin identitāti. Ar SSO ļāva abām personām palaist caur galvenes-auth ķēdi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The only account that form accepts is Checkmk’s built-in ``cmkadmin``, whose password comes from ``credentials.cmk_password`` (``CMK_PASSWORD`` in the container env) — a site-local secret unrelated to the Keycloak credentials the personas use. No Checkmk user is provisioned for a non-admin identity at all. With SSO enabled both personas run through the header-auth chain."
msgstr "Vienīgais konts, kuru veidlapa pieņem, ir: Checkmkiebūvēts ``cmkadmin``, kura parole nāk no ``credentials.cmk_password`` (``CMK_PASSWORD`` konteinerā env) — vietējs noslēpums, kas nav saistīts ar Keycloak apstiprina personas izmantošanu. Nē Checkmk lietotājs ir paredzēts, lai vispār nav admin identitāti. Ar SSO ļāva abām personām palaist caur galvenes-auth ķēdi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The operator MUST review the staged diff and message before committing."
msgstr "Pirms nodošanas operatoram ir jāpārskata inscenētās atšķirības un ziņojums."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The orchestrator and the push entry workflow (`entry-push-latest.yml`) cancel in-progress runs on every ref except `main`, which no automatic trigger cancels. A `pull_request_target` run inherits `refs/heads/main` as its ref, so the orchestrator does not cancel there either; per-PR supersession is handled by the entry workflow's own `pr-ci-*` group. See [configuration.md](../../tools/github/actions/configuration.md)."
msgstr "Orķestors un grūdiena ieejas darbplūsma (`entry-push-latest.yml`) atcelt progresiju katrā ref, izņemot `main`, kas nav automātiskais trigeris atceļ. A `pull_request_target` pārmantotie `refs/heads/main` kā savu ref, tāpēc orķestru neatceļ tur arī; per-PR supersesiju apstrādā ieraksta darbplūsmas paša `pr-ci-*` grupa. Skatīt [configuration.md](../../tools/github/actions/configuration.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The orchestrator runs the following stages in order:"
msgstr "Orķestors vada šādus posmus:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The orchestrator's `wait-fork-prereq-run` job **skips the wait** for the privileged fork images."
msgstr "Orķestra `wait-fork-prereq-run` darbs **atņem gaidīt** priviliģētiem dakšas attēliem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The order in `ORDERED_HANDLERS` MUST respect data dependencies. Example: `infinito_container` runs after `passthrough` so it can read the resolved `INFINITO_DISTRO`."
msgstr "Rīkojums `ORDERED_HANDLERS` JĀrespektē datu atkarība. Piemērs: `infinito_container` sākas pēc `passthrough` lai varētu izlasīt atrisināto `INFINITO_DISTRO`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The order is a precondition, not a preference. `baudolo-restore --empty` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays in the next; a booting consumer recreates it in between and the dump's own `CREATE TABLE` fails — which is how zammad turned this drill red with `relation \"ar_internal_metadata\" already exists`. The chain refuses the replay while a consumer runs, so a drill that got the order wrong would fail loudly instead of flaking."
msgstr "Pasūtījums ir priekšnosacījums, nevis priekšroka. `baudolo-restore --empty` iepriekš attīra shēmu vienā psql sesijā un atkārto nākamajā; booting patērētājs atjauno to starp un izgāztuves paša `CREATE TABLE` neveiksme – kas ir, kā zammad pagriezās šo urbi sarkans ar `relation \"ar_internal_metadata\" already exists`. Ķēde atsakās atkārtot, kamēr patērētājs darbojas, tāpēc urbis, kas got rīkojumu nepareizi varētu neizdoties skaļi, nevis pārslās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The order of those mocks is load-bearing and the router is not what reads it. `AI_AGENT_MODEL` takes `AI_MOCK_ALIASES | first`, so the mock declared first becomes the agent broker's model and its window becomes the context the broker gates platforms on. Declaring the 4096 mock first withheld `hermes`, whose `min_context` is 64000, and the broker's CLI test failed with the reason spelled out. The widest mock therefore leads. A sharper fix would be to have `AI_AGENT_MODEL` pick the mock with the largest declared context instead of the first one, which would make the order irrelevant."
msgstr "Šo izsmieļu kārtība ir nesoša, un maršrutētājs nav tas, kas to lasa. `AI_AGENT_MODEL` ņem `AI_MOCK_ALIASES | first`, tāpēc ņirgā deklarētais pirmais kļūst par aģenta brokera modeli un tā logs kļūst par kontekstu brokeru vārtu platformas uz. Deklarējot 4096 ņirgāties pirmo reizi ieturēts `hermes`, kura `min_context` ir 64000, un brokera CLI tests neizdevās ar izskaidrotu iemeslu. Tāpēc ved platākā izsmiekla. Asāks labojums būtu `AI_AGENT_MODEL` izvēlieties izsmieklu ar lielāko deklarēto kontekstu, nevis pirmo, kas padarītu pasūtījumu nesvarīgu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The ordered ``role#variant`` tokens the query yields."
msgstr "Rīkojums ``role#variant`` žetoni vaicājumu ieguvumus."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The ordered candidate rows, each the complexity payload of one ``role#variant``. Uncapped: the chunker decides what a sweep spends."
msgstr "Pasūtītās kandidātu rindas, katra sarežģītības derīgā krava viena ``role#variant``. Uncaped: chanker izlemt, ko slaucīšana pavada."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The outcome of comparing the two sources."
msgstr "Abu avotu salīdzināšanas rezultāts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The output format is the docker-compose `.env`-subset that is also sourceable from bash (via `set -a; source .env; set +a`). Values that contain only \"safe\" characters are emitted bare; everything else is double-quoted with backslash-escaping of `\\` and `\"`."
msgstr "Izvades formāts ir docker- compose `.env`-subset, kas ir arī avots no bash (caur `set -a; source .env; set +a`). Vērtības, kas satur tikai \"safe\" rakstzīmes tiek emitēti kailas; viss pārējais ir dubultā kotēta ar muguras-izbēgt `\\` kā arī `\"`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The output starts at column 0 (no caller-side indent)."
msgstr "Izvade sākas kolonnā 0 (nav zvanītāja puses ievilkuma)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The override path is host-vars `applications.<role>.services.<service>.{image,version}`. The inventory mirror step (see [mirror.md](mirror.md)) writes there automatically; manual overrides go to the same key."
msgstr "Atskaites ceļš ir host-vars `applications.<role>.services.<service>.{image,version}`. Inventāra spogulis solis (skatīt [mirror.md](mirror.md)) raksta tur automātiski; manuālā pārslēgšana iet uz to pašu atslēgu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, no-python-format, python-brace-format
msgid "The override path lives at the caller because Jinja-scope `{% set %}` bindings are visible only in the rendering template, never in the Ansible variable context that the lookup sees."
msgstr "Izņēmums ceļš dzīvo pie zvanītāja, jo Jinja-scope `{% set %}` saistījumi ir redzami tikai renderēšanas veidnē, nekad Ansible mainīgajā kontekstā, ko skats redz."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The override value for one credential, or None when unset."
msgstr "Pārsteidzošā vērtība vienam kredentiālam vai Nav, kad atiestatīts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The package converts the committed [default.env](../../default.env) plus a small runtime context into the gitignored `.env` at the repo root. Every module here belongs to one of four roles: parse, resolve, orchestrate, write."
msgstr "Pakete pārvērš [default.env](../../default.env) plus neliels runtime kontekstā uz gitignored `.env` repo saknes. Katrs modulis šeit pieder vienai no četrām lomām: parse, atrisināt, orķestra, rakstīt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The package installs the lint toolchain (actionlint, shfmt, ruff, ansible-lint, mbake, markdownlint-cli2, eslint, shellcheck, ansible-playbook, ansible-galaxy) using the right channel per tool (system package manager, pip, npm, or GitHub release). Modules at this level are channel-agnostic primitives; per-tool policy lives one level down in [lint/](lint/)."
msgstr "Pakotne instalē lint instrumentu ķēdi (akmeņplekste, shfmt, ruff, ansible-lint, mbake, marchownlint-kli2, eslints, shellcheck, ansible-playbook, ansible-galay) izmantojot labo kanālu katram rīkam (sistēmas pakotņu pārvaldnieks, pip, npm, vai GitHub atbrīvot). Moduļi šajā līmenī ir kanālu agnostiskie primitīvi; per-tool politika dzīvo vienu līmeni uz leju [Sviests](lint/)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The package is split by concern: - ``vault``: vault block construction + detection - ``overrides``: ``--set`` parsing + per-key resolution - ``emit``: recursive credentials emission into ruamel CommentedMaps - ``prompts``: interactive operator prompts - ``__main__``: argparse + orchestration"
msgstr "Pakete ir sadalīta pēc bažām: - ``vault``: velvju bloku konstrukcija + noteikšana - ``overrides``: ``--set`` parsēšana + uz atslēgas izšķirtspēju - ``emit``: rekursīvas akreditācijas emisija ruamel CommentedMaps - ``prompts``: interaktīva operatora uzvedne ``__main__``: argparse + orķestrācija"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The package metadata in these folders is used to keep Infinito.Nexus host dependencies explicit and distro-specific."
msgstr "Pakotņu metadati šajās mapēs tiek izmantoti, lai saglabātu Infinito.Nexus Saimnieciskās atkarības skaidri izteiktas un distro-specifiskas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The palette is generated from a base color through `colorscheme-generator`."
msgstr "Palete tiek ģenerēta no bāzes krāsas caur `colorscheme-generator`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The part of the role id the category labels do not already carry."
msgstr "Tās lomas daļa, kas attiecas uz kategoriju marķējumiem, vēl nav piešķirta."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The password is passed via environment variables (robust with special characters)."
msgstr "Parole tiek nodota caur vides mainīgajiem (robusts ar īpašām rakstu zīmēm)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The path ``INFINITO_SRC_DIR`` names."
msgstr "Ceļš ``INFINITO_SRC_DIR`` nosaukumus."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The pattern for hyphenated role names, which hold wherever they appear, and the one for titles, which holds only on a capitalised occurrence."
msgstr "Defiscēto lomu nosaukumu modelis, kas tur, kur tie parādās, un tituls, kas tur tikai kapitalizētu notikumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The people the roles name as their authors."
msgstr "Cilvēki lomas vārdu kā viņu autori."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The per-category port ranges that the suggester proposes from and that the lint check enforces live as a single `PORT_BANDS` map in [08_networks.yml](../../../../../group_vars/all/08_networks.yml). Suggesters and lint pick up new entries automatically, with no second registration step. See `cli contributing network ports suggest` in [port.md](../../../tools/network/port.md)."
msgstr "Katras kategorijas portu diapazoni, no kuriem iesaka ierosinātājs, un ka liesmu pārbaude nodrošina dzīvot kā viens `PORT_BANDS` karte iekš [08networks.yml](../../../../../group_vars/all/08_networks.yml). Ieteiktāji un lint uzņemt jaunus ierakstus automātiski, bez otrās reģistrācijas solis. Skatīt `cli contributing network ports suggest` skaits [port.md](../../../tools/network/port.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The per-role complexity score, its ``dna`` cluster key and ``siblings``."
msgstr "Par lomu sarežģītības rezultātu, tā ``dna`` klastera taustiņu un ``siblings``."

