# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role will load both sub-roles and satisfy all dependencies transparently."
msgstr "Šī loma noslogos gan apakšlomas, gan pārredzamā veidā apmierinās visas atkarības."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role will register mappings using ``doli add`` and can optionally run ``doli pull``."
msgstr "Šī loma reģistrēs kartēšanu, izmantojot ``doli add`` un var pēc izvēles vadīt ``doli pull``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role will register mappings using `doli add` and can optionally run `doli pull`."
msgstr "Šī loma reģistrēs kartēšanu, izmantojot `doli add` un var pēc izvēles vadīt `doli pull`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role's HTML references the expected asset host AND a request returns < 400 with the right content-type."
msgstr "Loma HTML atsauces gaidāmo aktīvu resursdators UN pieprasījums atgriež < 400 ar pareizo satura veidu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role's ``README.md`` heading as one separator-joined fragment."
msgstr "Nozīme ``README.md`` ar vienu atdalītāju savienotu fragmentu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role's addon-processing loop MUST include `tasks/addons/<addon_id>.yml` when present and tolerate its absence."
msgstr "Loma ir papildus apstrādes cilpa jāiekļauj `tasks/addons/<addon_id>.yml` ja klāt un pacieš tās neesamību."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role's documented integrations (OIDC, RBAC, email, dashboard, service-gating, etc., as applicable) are exercised end-to-end by its Playwright spec or by a peer role's spec when the integration is cross-role."
msgstr "Nozīme dokumentēta integrācija (OIDC, RBAC, e-pasts, vadības panelis, pakalpojumu nodrošināšana utt., pēc vajadzības) tiek realizēti no gala līdz galam ar savu Playwright spec vai ar vienādranga lomu spec, ja integrācija ir šķērsloma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The role's name is implied by the path. There is NO `web-app-<role>` key inside the file. The materialised path is `applications.<role>.networks.local.{subnet,dns_resolver}`."
msgstr "Uz lomas nosaukumu norāda ceļš. Nav `web-app-<role>` atslēgas failā. Materializētais ceļš ir `applications.<role>.networks.local.{subnet,dns_resolver}`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role's playwright lint contracts (Tests A + B + env_keys_used) are green; role-closure remains pending the orchestration fix."
msgstr "Loma dramaturga lint līgumi (Testi A + B + env_keys_used) ir zaļi; līdz orķestra fiksēšanai paliek brīva vieta."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role's purpose is to automate the provisioning and configuration of a centralized database service. This not only reduces manual setup but also ensures consistent, reliable deployment across production and homelab environments."
msgstr "Loma mērķis ir automatizēt centralizēta datu bāzes pakalpojuma nodrošināšanu un konfigurāciju. Tas ne tikai samazina manuālo uzstādīšanu, bet arī nodrošina konsekventu, uzticamu ieviešanu visā ražošanas un mājas lapu vidē."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role's service config (file root IS the services map keyed by `<entity_name>`). For `svc-db-mariadb` this carries the entity-keyed image, version, and hostname:"
msgstr "Loma servisa konfigurācija (faila root IS pakalpojumu kartē taustiņu `<entity_name>`). Par `svc-db-mariadb` tas satur uzņēmuma atslēgas attēlu, versiju un datora nosaukumu:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role-mapping schema decides which files MAY appear inside `roles/<role-name>/`, which MUST appear, and which dotted-path entries inside those files MUST be set per role type."
msgstr "Lomu kartēšanas shēma nolemj, kuri faili var parādīties iekšpusē `roles/<role-name>/`, kas jāparādās, un kas punktētā ceļa ierakstus šajos failos ir jānosaka katram funkciju veidam."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role-specific interaction callbacks and the peer-exchange test are part of the persona contract. Specs that ship only the personas without an interaction callback fulfil the bare minimum, but SHOULD extend with bespoke role coverage during the role's rollout iteration."
msgstr "Lomai specifiskie mijiedarbības izsaukumi un salīdzinošās apmaiņas tests ir daļa no personas līguma. Norāda, ka kuģis tikai personas bez mijiedarbības izsaukuma izpildīt kailu minimumu, bet būtu jāpaplašina ar bespoke lomu pārklājumu laikā lomu izvēršanās atkārtojumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The roles below are database-backed and their upstream app can store objects in S3, so the integration is **fundamentally possible but not yet implemented**. Roles whose upstream has no S3 backend, or whose S3 client is incompatible with SeaweedFS path-style, are listed at the end."
msgstr "Turpmāk norādītās lomas ir datubāzes atbalstītas, un to augšpusē lietotne var glabāt objektus S3, tāpēc integrācija ir **fundamentāli iespējams, bet vēl nav īstenots**. Lomas, kuru augšpusē nav S3 aizmugure vai kuras S3 klients nav savietojams ar SeaweedFS ceļa stila, ir uzskaitīti beigās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role’s purpose is to automate the provisioning and configuration of a centralized database service. This not only reduces manual setup but also ensures consistent, reliable deployment across production and homelab environments."
msgstr "Lomas mērķis ir automatizēt centralizēta datu bāzes pakalpojuma nodrošināšanu un konfigurāciju. Tas ne tikai samazina manuālo uzstādīšanu, bet arī nodrošina konsekventu, uzticamu ieviešanu visā ražošanas un mājas lapu vidē."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The root `index.rst` uses a `:glob:` toctree (`docs/**`) to automatically include every documentation page."
msgstr "Sakne `index.rst` lieto a `:glob:` tokoks (`docs/**`) automātiski iekļaut katru dokumentācijas lapu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The root causes that are still open without a run to point at: a fix landed whose effect nobody has seen, or a diagnosis that was never confirmed against the deployed code."
msgstr "Pamatcēloņi, kas joprojām ir atvērti bez palaist uz punktu: noteikt izkrauti, kura efekts neviens nav redzējis, vai diagnozi, kas nekad nav apstiprināts pret izvietoto kodu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The root mapping, with every scalar as a ``str``."
msgstr "Saknes kartēšana, ar katru skalāru kā ``str``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The roundtrip is a gate, not a debugger: when a step goes red it stops and leaves the evidence in place. Do NOT just re-run the roundtrip; drop into the matching focused loop."
msgstr "Roundtrip ir vārti, nevis atkļūdotājs: kad solis iet sarkana tas apstājas un atstāj pierādījumus vietā. Nevajag vienkārši atkārtoti palaist riņķot; iemetiet atbilstoša fokusēto cilpu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The router runs init, then deploy. Init materialises the inventory under `${INFINITO_INVENTORY_DIR}` (resolved by `make dotenv` via [resolve.sh](../../../scripts/inventory/resolve.sh); see [variables.md](../environment/variables.md))."
msgstr "Maršrutētājs darbojas init, pēc tam izvietot. Init īsteno inventarizāciju `${INFINITO_INVENTORY_DIR}` (atrisināta `make dotenv` caur [resolve.sh](../../../scripts/inventory/resolve.sh); skat. [variables.md](../environment/variables.md))."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The router sits inside the gateway. No consumer learns a second endpoint."
msgstr "Maršrutētājs sēž vārtejas iekšpusē. Neviens patērētājs neiemācās otru galapunktu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The row has to run in the guide's own mode. The replay is a second deploy on the same runner, so hanging it on a swarm row would ask that runner to bring a compose stack up beside a swarm one. Only rows in that mode count as deployed here either, so the variant search cannot settle on one that this sweep runs in swarm alone."
msgstr "Rindai jāskrien paša gida režīmā. Replay ir otrs izvietot uz tā paša skrējējs, tāpēc karājas to uz bara rindā lūgtu, ka skrējējs, lai ņemtu komponēt steku uz augšu blakus bars viens. Tikai rindas šajā režīmā skaitās izvietotas arī šeit, tāpēc varianta meklēšana nevar nokārtot uz vienu, ka šī slaucīšana notiek baros vien."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The row then draws from that intersection instead of the run's whole pool, and so does every row whose variant deploys that role, as the deploy planner resolves it. A role and a run that permit nothing in common abort the matrix rather than dropping the row."
msgstr "Pēc tam rinda tiek veidota no šī krustojuma, nevis no visa baseina, un tāpat arī no katras rindas, kuras variants izvieto šo lomu, kā to atrisina izvietojuma plānotājs. Loma un skrējiens, kas pieļauj neko kopējā pārtraukt matricu, nevis nometot rindu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The rows the source run proved, as ``role#variant``, axes dropped."
msgstr "Rindās avota palaist izrādījās, kā ``role#variant``, asis samazinājās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The rules were written first and the code audited against them afterwards. Each of the following was live at the time it was found, not a hypothetical the design ruled out:"
msgstr "Noteikumi tika uzrakstīti vispirms, un kodekss pēc tam tika revidēts pret tiem. Tajā laikā, kad tas tika atrasts, katrs no šiem bija dzīvs, nevis hipotētisks dizains izslēdza:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The run is marked failed. GitHub notifies repository admins. No PR is created with a wrong identity."
msgstr "Darbināšana neveiksmīga. GitHub paziņo repozitorija adminus. Neviens PR nav izveidots ar nepareizu identitāti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The run leaves the cluster up (`INFINITO_KEEP_SWARM_NODES=true`). You MUST reproduce the failure on it via `make swarm-exec` / `make swarm-shell`, then release it with `make swarm-down`."
msgstr "Darbināšana atstāj klasteri augšup (`INFINITO_KEEP_SWARM_NODES=true`). Jums ir reproducēt neveiksmi par to, izmantojot `make swarm-exec` / `make swarm-shell`, tad atlaidiet to ar `make swarm-down`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The run this builds differs from a retrigger: a retrigger replays what a run already judged, this one asks about rows nobody has judged yet or whose verdict is still disputed. It therefore states its axes instead of carrying them over."
msgstr "Darbināšana šī būvē atšķiras no retrigger: retrigger atkārto to, ko palaist jau spriests, šis jautā par rindām neviens vēl nav spriests vai kuras spriedums joprojām tiek apstrīdēts. Tāpēc tā nevis pārnesīs tās pāri, bet gan paziņos par savām asīm."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The run's 256-job cap is the second ceiling. `slots` counts every non-deploy job the orchestrator chain spawns, subtracts the worst `entry-*.yml` overhead, and what remains is `available` — the rows one sweep may deploy across all its chunks. Rows beyond that roll into the next sweep, which starts reading the regular line at an offset (`cli.meta.ci.chunks`), so consecutive sweeps walk the whole list instead of re-testing the same head forever."
msgstr "Darbs 256- Darba cepure ir otrais griesti. `slots` skaita katru ne-deploy darbu orķestra ķēdes nārsto, atņem sliktāko `entry-*.yml` pieskaitāmās izmaksas, un kas paliek ir `available` — rindas var izvietot uz visiem tās gabaliem. Rindas aiz šī roll uz nākamo slaucīšana, kas sāk lasīt regulāru līniju pie nobīdes (`cli.meta.ci.chunks`), tāpēc pēc kārtas slaucīšana staigāt visu sarakstu, nevis atkārtoti pārbaudīt to pašu galvu uz visiem laikiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The runnable journey lives in ``files/playwright/test-login-biber.js``, which first grants biber the KIX user group over the Keycloak Admin API and then drives ``runKixLoginLogoutFlow`` through both stages to the universal logout. The path back to the generic persona is a KIX build that accepts the proxy’s trusted headers instead of demanding its own login."
msgstr "Braucamais ceļojums dzīvo ``files/playwright/test-login-biber.js``, kas vispirms piešķir biber KIX lietotāju grupa Keycloak Administrators API un tad brauc ``runKixLoginLogoutFlow`` caur abiem posmiem uz universālo atslēgties. Ceļš atpakaļ uz vispārējo persona ir KIX veidot, kas pieņem starpniekservera uzticamo galvenes, nevis pieprasīt savu pieteikšanās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The runnable journey lives in `files/playwright/test-login-biber.js`, which first grants biber the KIX user group over the Keycloak Admin API and then drives `runKixLoginLogoutFlow` through both stages to the universal logout. The path back to the generic persona is a KIX build that accepts the proxy's trusted headers instead of demanding its own login."
msgstr "Braucamais ceļojums dzīvo `files/playwright/test-login-biber.js`, kas vispirms piešķir biber KIX lietotāju grupa Keycloak Administrators API un tad brauc `runKixLoginLogoutFlow` caur abiem posmiem uz universālo atslēgties. Ceļš atpakaļ uz vispārējo persona ir KIX veidot, kas pieņem starpniekservera uzticamās galvenes, nevis pieprasa savu pieteikšanos."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The runner is intentionally test-agnostic at runtime: it executes only tests provided by application roles."
msgstr "Skrējējs ir apzināti test-agnostisks pie palaišanas: tas veic tikai testus, ko nodrošina lietojumprogrammas lomas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The runner keeps Playwright traces, screenshots, and videos for every test only when the resolved environment variable `INFINITO_PLAYWRIGHT_KEEP` evaluates to `true` (case-insensitive). Any other value, including unset or empty, keeps artefacts only when a test fails."
msgstr "Skrējējs tur Playwright pēdas, ekrānšāviņi, un video katram testam tikai tad, kad atrisināta vides mainīgo `INFINITO_PLAYWRIGHT_KEEP` novērtē, lai `true` (Nejutīgs). Jebkura cita vērtība, ieskaitot atiestatītu vai tukšu, saglabā artefaktus tikai tad, kad tests neizdodas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The runner label *architecture* deploys on."
msgstr "Skrējēja etiķete *arhitektūra* izmanto."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The runner label each architecture deploys on."
msgstr "Skrējēja etiķete katra arhitektūra izvietojas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The runner's `compose` wrapper at [roles/sys-svc-compose/files/python/compose.py](../../../roles/sys-svc-compose/files/python/compose.py) auto-detects compose files when invoked from per-app directories under `/opt/compose/<app>/`:"
msgstr "Skrējēja `compose` iesaiņojums [roles/sys-svc-compose/files/python/compose.py](../../../roles/sys-svc-compose/files/python/compose.py) automātiski nosaka veido failus, ja piesakās no per-app direktorijiem saskaņā `/opt/compose/<app>/`:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The runner's `infinito` service receives:"
msgstr "Skrējēja `infinito` pakalpojums saņem:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The safety of this design comes entirely from **confinement of the device**, not from confinement of the agent: the machine is dedicated to Hermes, single-tenant, network-segmented, and physically separate from shared infrastructure. `svc-ai-robot` is the role that provisions that device and deploys Hermes on it in privileged mode. It builds on the [`web-app-hermes`](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md) role rather than reimplementing the agent."
msgstr "Šīs konstrukcijas drošība nāk no **Ierīces norobežošana**, nevis no aģenta ieslodzījuma: mašīna ir veltīta Hermes, viena tenanta, tīkla segmentiem un fiziski nodalīta no kopīgas infrastruktūras. `svc-ai-robot` ir funkcija, kas paredz šo ierīci un izvieto uz tās Hermes priviliģētā režīmā. Tas balstās uz [`web-app-hermes`](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md) loma, nevis atkārtota īstenošana aģents."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The same as JSON"
msgstr "Tāpat kā JSON"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The same command as one shell string, so a prefix can compose with it."
msgstr "Tā pati komanda kā viena čaulas virkne, lai ar to varētu komponēt prefiksu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The same mapping."
msgstr "Tāda pati kartēšana."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The same reachability problem exists without Tor wherever the host resolves through a listener of its own on loopback, which is how the simulated cluster nodes are wired. Handing containers the declared clearnet address there was what a literal bridge address in the inventory used to paper over, and that literal went stale the moment the daemon's address pool moved the bridge off Docker's default."
msgstr "Tāda pati sasniedzamības problēma pastāv bez Tor visur, kur saimnieks atrisina ar sava klausītāja palīdzību uz cilpas, kas ir veids, kā simulētie klastera mezgli tiek vadu veidā. Pasniedzot konteinerus deklarēto cleannet adresi tur bija kāda burtiska tilta adrese inventāra izmanto papīra, un ka burtisks gāja strupceļā brīdi dēmona adrešu baseins pārvietoja tiltu no Docker noklusējuma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The same selections with every axis dropped, one entry per role."
msgstr "Vienas un tās pašas izvēles ar katru asi samazinājās, pa vienam ierakstam uz lomu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The same shape serves the repository-root file, which holds the shared collection any role and any inventory bundle may install from, and a role's own file, which holds what only that role installs."
msgstr "Tāda pati forma kalpo repozitorija root failu, kas tur dalīto vākšanu jebkuru lomu un jebkurš inventāra paketi var instalēt no, un loma paša failu, kas tur tikai šo lomu instalēt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The same string `.env` carries as ``INFINITO_CACHE_UPSTREAMS``, so the role's bootstrap task and the dev stack provision Nexus from one rendering. `utils.cache.records` owns the format."
msgstr "Tā pati virkne `.env` veic kā ``INFINITO_CACHE_UPSTREAMS``, tāpēc loma bootstrap uzdevums un dev steka noteikums Nexus no vienas renderēšanas. `utils.cache.records` pieder formāts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox (`allowWrite`, `denyRead`, `allowedDomains`, see [sandbox.md](sandbox.md)) bounds every write, every read, and every outbound connection. `deny` rules block destructive patterns unconditionally; `ask` rules force operator review on every mutating `gh`/`docker`/`git commit`/`Skill(update-config*)` invocation. The wildcard does **not** loosen any existing guardrail; it only drops the per-shape workarounds."
msgstr "Smilšu kaste (`allowWrite`, `denyRead`, `allowedDomains`, skat. [sandbox.md](sandbox.md)) saista katru rakstu, katru lasījumu un katru izejošo saiti. `deny` noteikumi bez nosacījumiem bloķē destruktīvus modeļus; `ask` noteikumi liek operatoram pārskatīt katru mutatis mutandis `gh`/`docker`/`git commit`/`Skill(update-config*)` atsauksmi. Zvaigzne dara **nav** Atbrīvot jebkuru esošo aizsargsliedi; tas tikai nomet per-forme darba ap."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox `denyRead: ~/.gnupg` rule blocks GPG access by design; agent commands must never touch private key material. This env override removes the resulting signing failure without weakening the credential-path protection. Agent-authored commits land unsigned; the `Co-Authored-By` trailer documents authorship."
msgstr "Smilšu kaste `denyRead: ~/.gnupg` noteikums bloķē GPG piekļuvi ar dizainu; aģents komandas nekad nedrīkst pieskarties privāto atslēgu materiālu. Šis env pārmiju noņem rezultātā parakstīšanas neveiksme, nevājinot kredentiālo ceļu aizsardzību. Aģents-autors veic neparakstītu zemi; `Co-Authored-By` piekabes dokumentu autorība."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox can connect to any Unix-domain socket on the host. Required so commands like `docker`, `systemctl`, and language servers continue to work; these all communicate over Unix sockets (e.g. `/var/run/docker.sock`)."
msgstr "Smilšu kaste var pieslēgties jebkurai Unix domēna ligzdai uz datora. Nepieciešams, lai komandas, piemēram `docker`, `systemctl`, un valodu serveri turpina strādāt; šie visi sazināties vairāk Unix ligzdas (Piemēram, `/var/run/docker.sock`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox cannot be escaped through the host daemon"
msgstr "Smilšu kaste nevar izbēgt caur saimnieka dēmonu"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox has `sandbox.network.allowAllUnixSockets: true` so that normal workflow tools (`docker`, `systemctl`, language servers) continue to work. Any command that reaches `/var/run/docker.sock` can request a container with `-v /:/host --privileged`, which the Docker daemon executes as root and mounts the host filesystem. The sandbox's `allowWrite` does NOT protect against this path because Docker is a trusted service on the other end of the socket."
msgstr "Smilšu kaste ir `sandbox.network.allowAllUnixSockets: true` tā, lai parasti darbplūsmas rīki (`docker`, `systemctl`, valodu serveri) turpina strādāt. Jebkura komanda, kas sasniedz `/var/run/docker.sock` var pieprasīt konteineru ar `-v /:/host --privileged`, kuru Docker dēmons izpilda kā saknes un mounts host failu sistēmu. Smilšu kaste `allowWrite` nepasargā no šī ceļa, jo Docker ir uzticams pakalpojums ligzdas otrā galā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The sandbox is activated unconditionally via `\"sandbox\": { \"enabled\": true }`. This means filesystem and network restrictions below are enforced **at every session**, not only when the operator manually switches into sandbox permission mode. The OS-level sandbox is the source of truth for what commands may read, write, and reach over the network; the `allow`/`ask`/`deny` permission lists remain in force as a second line of defence for policy concerns the OS cannot express (e.g. requiring confirmation before publishing a commit)."
msgstr "Smilšu kaste ir aktivizēta bez nosacījumiem caur `\"sandbox\": { \"enabled\": true }`. Tas nozīmē, ka failu sistēma un tīkla ierobežojumi zemāk ir ieviesti **katrā sesijā**, ne tikai tad, kad operators manuāli pārslēdzas smilšu kastes atļaujas režīmā. OS līmeņa smilšu kaste ir patiesības avots tam, kādas komandas var lasīt, rakstīt un sasniegt tīklā; `allow`/`ask`/`deny` atļauju saraksti paliek spēkā kā otra aizsardzības līnija politikas jautājumiem, kurus OS nevar izteikt (Piemēram, nepieciešams apstiprinājums pirms saistību publicēšanas)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox's `denyRead` list (`~/.gnupg`, `~/.kube`, `~/.aws`, `~/.config/gcloud`) is the primary mechanism that prevents the agent from reading host credentials. Every credential store an operator uses on the host is assumed to be covered, **with the documented exception of `~/.ssh`** (see Assumption 10)."
msgstr "Smilšu kaste `denyRead` saraksts (`~/.gnupg`, `~/.kube`, `~/.aws`, `~/.config/gcloud`) ir primārais mehānisms, kas neļauj aģentam nolasīt resursdatora akreditācijas datus. Katrs rezervācijas veikals, ko operators izmanto uz saimnieka, tiek uzskatīts par aptvertu, **izņemot dokumentētu `~/.ssh`** (Skatīt pieņēmumu 10)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scan is cached behind a fresh list, because one source message is scanned once per target language and callers may sort or trim the result."
msgstr "Skenēšana tiek glabāta aiz jauna saraksta, jo vienu avota ziņojumu skenē vienu reizi katrā mērķa valodā un zvanītāji var kārtot vai apgriezt rezultātu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scheduled `🔄 Update versions` pipeline (version bumps and PR open/refresh)."
msgstr "Plānotais `🔄 Update versions` cauruļvadu (versijas izciļņi un PR atver/atsvaidzina)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scheduled update workflow MUST be able to reuse the same discovery logic in update mode. Version bumps MAY update `version`; new addon entries MAY be added with `enabled: false`, `required: false`, and complete `update` metadata."
msgstr "Plānotajai atjaunināšanas darbplūsmai jāspēj atkārtoti izmantot to pašu meklēšanas loģiku atjaunināšanas režīmā. Versijas izciļņi VAR atjaunināt `version`; jaunus addon ierakstus var pievienot ar `enabled: false`, `required: false`, un pabeigt `update` metadatiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The schema lives at ``meta/networks.yml.overlay`` per provider role, discovered into the service_registry by ``discover_role_services``. Keys:"
msgstr "Schema dzīvo ``meta/networks.yml.overlay`` par katru pakalpojumu sniedzēja lomu, atklāts service_registry līdz ``discover_role_services``. Atslēgas:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The schema rejects a generic URL, a runtime OpenAPI document, free-form GraphQL, a raw SQL tool, an unrestricted bucket, an arbitrary filesystem root, a shell command, a Docker socket, and implicit exposure of every operation an upstream upgrade adds."
msgstr "Schema noraida vispārēju URL, palaist laika OpenAPI dokumentu, brīvās formas GraphQL, neapstrādātu SQL rīks, neierobežots spainis, patvaļīga filesystem root, čaulas komanda, Docker ligzda, un netieša iedarbība uz katru operāciju augšpusē jauninājums piebilst."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope MUST be a **default** client scope on every OIDC client that needs group-based RBAC. Making it optional reintroduces a userinfo regression: when optional with `include.in.token.scope=false`, Keycloak drops the group-membership mapper from userinfo even when the scope is explicitly requested, so consumers receive no groups and fall back to `subscriber`."
msgstr "Darbības jomai jābūt **noklusētais** klienta tvērums katram OIDC klientam, kam nepieciešams uz grupu balstīts RBAC. Padarot to fakultatīvu, atkārtoti ievieš userinfo regresiju: ja pēc izvēles ar `include.in.token.scope=false`, Keycloak nomet grupas dalībnieku kartētāju no userinfo pat tad, ja joma ir skaidri pieprasīta, tāpēc patērētāji nesaņem grupas un ir atpakaļ uz `subscriber`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is image handling. Workflow orchestration, metadata resolution, and generic waiting logic should live in other script directories."
msgstr "Šīs mapes darbības joma ir attēlu apstrāde. Darbplūsmas orķestrācijai, metadatu izšķirtspējai un vispārējai gaidīšanas loģikai vajadzētu dzīvot citās skriptu direktorijās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is installation and bootstrap. Lint execution, build workflows, and test orchestration should stay in their dedicated script directories."
msgstr "Šīs mapes darbības joma ir uzstādīšana un bootstrap. Lint izpilde, veidot darbplūsmas, un testa orķestrācija būtu jāpaliek savā veltīta skriptu direktorijām."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is lint execution. Tool installation belongs in `scripts/install`, while build and test workflows should stay in their dedicated script directories."
msgstr "Šīs mapes darbības joma ir lint izpilde. Rīku uzstādīšana pieder pie `scripts/install`, bet veidot un pārbaudīt darbplūsmas būtu jāpaliek to veltīta skriptu direktorijām."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is missing-state resolution. Image build, release, and workflow orchestration should stay in their dedicated script or workflow locations."
msgstr "Šīs mapes darbības jomai trūkst statusa. Attēlu veidošanas, atbrīvošanas, un darbplūsmas orķestrācija būtu jāpaliek savā veltīta skriptu vai darbplūsmas vietās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is script organization at the repository level. Detailed responsibilities belong in the README files of the respective subdirectories."
msgstr "Šīs mapes apjoms ir skriptu organizācija repozitorija līmenī. Detalizēti pienākumi pieder attiecīgo apakšdirektoriju LASĪTME failiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is value resolution. Build, release, and wait-oriented behavior should stay in their dedicated script directories."
msgstr "Šīs mapes darbības joma ir vērtību izšķirtspēja. Veidot, atbrīvot, un gaida orientēta uzvedība būtu jāpaliek viņu veltīta skriptu direktorijām."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is waiting and availability checks. Build, release, and resource-specific lifecycle operations should stay in their dedicated directories."
msgstr "Šīs mapes darbības joma ir gaidīšana un pieejamības pārbaudes. Veidojot, atbrīvojot un resursiem specifiskām dzīves cikla darbībām būtu jāpaliek savās speciālajās direktorijās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script **prefers `/mnt`** when it is a separate partition (classic `ubuntu-latest` layout with `/dev/sdb` mounted at `/mnt`) and falls back to `/` otherwise. Current public runners no longer expose a separate `/mnt`, so the swapfile lands on `/` and must not starve the root filesystem."
msgstr "Skripts **dod `/mnt`** kad tas ir atsevišķs nodalījums (klasika `ubuntu-latest` izkārtojums ar `/dev/sdb` montēts pie `/mnt`) un atgriežas `/` citādi. Pašreizējie valsts skrējēji vairs neatklāj atsevišķu `/mnt`, tāpēc mijmaiņas fails nolaižas uz `/` un nedrīkst badā saknes failu sistēmu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script first starts the role's deployed backup unit (a fresh differential generation of the live material), then mirrors each present subtree back to its fixed system path (`rsync -a --delete`): `secrets` into `/var/lib/infinito/secrets`, `ca` into `/etc/<domain>/ca`, `acme` into `/etc/letsencrypt`, `certbot` into `/etc/certbot`. `--no-safety-backup` skips the pre-recover unit run. The `node` subtree (ssh host keys + machine-id) is restored only with `--restore-node-identity`, because overwriting the running machine-id / ssh host keys changes the host's identity mid-flight — do it on a fresh host after total loss."
msgstr "Skripts vispirms palaiž lomu izvietoto rezerves bloku (dzīvā materiāla jauna diferenciālā ģenerācija), tad spoguļi katru esošo apakškoku atpakaļ uz tās fiksēto sistēmas ceļu (`rsync -a --delete`): `secrets` uz `/var/lib/infinito/secrets`, `ca` uz `/etc/<domain>/ca`, `acme` uz `/etc/letsencrypt`, `certbot` uz `/etc/certbot`. `--no-safety-backup` izlaiž priekšatgūstamo vienību. E ir o pa s `node` apakškoks (ssh saimnieka taustiņi + mašīnas ID) ir atjaunota tikai ar `--restore-node-identity`, jo pārrakstot darbojošos automātu-id / ssh saimnieka atslēgas maina saimnieka identitāti lidojuma vidū — dari to uz jauna saimnieka pēc pilnīga zaudējuma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script first starts the role’s deployed backup unit (a fresh differential generation of the live material), then mirrors each present subtree back to its fixed system path (``rsync -a --delete``): ``secrets`` into ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets``, ``ca`` into ``/etc/<domain>/ca``, ``acme`` into ``/etc/letsencrypt``, ``certbot`` into ``/etc/certbot``. ``--no-safety-backup`` skips the pre-recover unit run. The ``node`` subtree (ssh host keys + machine-id) is restored only with ``--restore-node-identity``, because overwriting the running machine-id / ssh host keys changes the host’s identity mid-flight — do it on a fresh host after total loss."
msgstr "Skripts vispirms sāk lomu izvietoto rezerves bloku (dzīvā materiāla jauna diferenciālā ģenerācija), tad spoguļi katru esošo apakškoku atpakaļ uz tās fiksēto sistēmas ceļu (``rsync -a --delete``): ``secrets`` uz ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets``, ``ca`` uz ``/etc/<domain>/ca``, ``acme`` uz ``/etc/letsencrypt``, ``certbot`` uz ``/etc/certbot``. ``--no-safety-backup`` izlaiž priekšatgūstamo vienību. E ir o pa s ``node`` apakškoks (ssh saimnieka taustiņi + mašīnas ID) ir atjaunota tikai ar ``--restore-node-identity``, jo pārrakstot darbojošos automātu-id / ssh saimnieka atslēgas maina saimnieka identitāti lidojuma vidū — dari to uz svaiga saimnieka pēc pilnīga zaudējuma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script must stay free of every shell ``$``: the compose and swarm render paths launder dollars differently (a ``$pid`` reached the container as ``\"\"`` and crash-looped the sidecar on a sh syntax error). The bucket bootstrap therefore polls ``/status`` from a backgrounded subshell while ``exec`` makes the server PID 1; the poll loop dies with the container and readiness is gated by the consumer's bounded wait."
msgstr "Skriptam jābūt brīvam no katras čaulas ``$``: komponēt un bars padarīt ceļus atmazgāt dolārus atšķirīgi (a ``$pid`` sasniedza konteineru kā ``\"\"`` un avārijas iekustināts blakusvāģis uz sh sintakses kļūdas). Tāpēc spaini bootstrap aptaujas ``/status`` no fona apakščaksta, kamēr ``exec`` padara serveri PID 1; poll cilpa iet bojā ar konteineru un gatavību gated ar patērētāja ierobežota gaidīšana."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script opens the LUKS device (interactive passphrase prompt; `--passphrase-stdin` for automation), mounts it, picks the newest device snapshot across every machine hash (a fresh host after total loss has a new machine id), mirrors it into the target (`rsync -a --delete`) and unmounts/closes the device again. No pre-recover service backup runs: the device itself is the backup this role maintains. Afterwards restore individual applications from the backup root with the matching role's `recover.py` (`svc-bkp-volume-2-local` for docker volumes, `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local` for NFS exports)."
msgstr "Skripts atver LUKS ierīci (interaktīva parole; `--passphrase-stdin` automatizācijai), mounts to, izvēlas jaunāko ierīci momentuzņēmums pāri katru mašīnu hash (svaigs saimnieks pēc pilnīga zaudējuma ir jauna mašīna id), spoguļi to mērķa (`rsync -a --delete`) un atkal nomontē/aizslēdz ierīci. Nav iepriekšējas atgūšanas pakalpojuma rezerves kopijas: pati ierīce ir rezerves kopija, ko uztur šī loma. Pēc tam atjaunot atsevišķas programmas no rezerves saknes ar atbilstošu lomu `recover.py` (`svc-bkp-volume-2-local` docker tilpumiem, `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local` NFS eksportam)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script opens the LUKS device (interactive passphrase prompt; ``--passphrase-stdin`` for automation), mounts it, picks the newest device snapshot across every machine hash (a fresh host after total loss has a new machine id), mirrors it into the target (``rsync -a --delete``) and unmounts/closes the device again. No pre-recover service backup runs: the device itself is the backup this role maintains. Afterwards restore individual applications from the backup root with the matching role’s ``recover.py`` (``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` for docker volumes, ``svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` for NFS exports)."
msgstr "Skripts atver LUKS ierīci (interaktīva parole; ``--passphrase-stdin`` automatizācijai), mounts to, izvēlas jaunāko ierīci momentuzņēmums pāri katru mašīnu hash (svaigs saimnieks pēc pilnīga zaudējuma ir jauna mašīna id), spoguļi to mērķa (``rsync -a --delete``) un atkal nomontē/aizslēdz ierīci. Nav iepriekšējas atgūšanas pakalpojuma rezerves kopijas: pati ierīce ir rezerves kopija, ko uztur šī loma. Pēc tam atjaunot atsevišķus pieteikumus no rezerves saknes ar atbilstošu lomu 's ``recover.py`` (``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` docker tilpumiem, ``svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` NFS eksportam)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script type/extension (e.g., sh, py, yml)."
msgstr "Skripta tips/paplašinājums (piem., sh, py, yml)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script-level references for `scripts/tests/deploy/act/` live in [scripts/tests/deploy/act/README.md](../../../scripts/tests/deploy/act/README.md). For broader test and validation guidance, see [Testing and Validation](../actions/testing.md)."
msgstr "Skripta līmeņa atsauces `scripts/tests/deploy/act/` dzīvot [scripts/tests/deploy/act/README.md](../../../scripts/tests/deploy/act/README.md). Plašākus norādījumus par testiem un validēšanu skatīt [Testēšana un apstiprināšana](../actions/testing.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The section titles are the classification vocabulary itself, and each role that ships a `meta/mcp.yml` is filed under the value that file declares. The authoritative disposition of a deployed surface is that file; this list is the record of the review, including the roles that deliberately carry no surface."
msgstr "Sadaļas virsraksti ir klasifikācijas vārdnīca pati, un katru lomu, ko kuģi a `meta/mcp.yml` tiek iesniegts saskaņā ar vērtību, ko šī lieta deklarē. Izvietotās virsmas autoritatīvais izvietojums ir šis fails; šis saraksts ir pārskats, tostarp lomas, uz kurām apzināti nav virsmas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The security policies enforced on this repository are documented here:"
msgstr "Šajā repozitorijā īstenotā drošības politika ir dokumentēta šeit:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The selected deploy modes this row can actually run in. Never empty for a row the query returned -- the filter kept it precisely because at least one selected mode claims it."
msgstr "Izvēlētie izvietošanas režīmi, kuros rinda faktiski var darboties. Nekad neaizpildīt rindu vaicājums atgriezās -- filtrs to tur tieši tāpēc, ka vismaz viens izvēlētais režīms to apgalvo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The selection and retry logic is implemented in   `scripts/install/ansible.sh`."
msgstr "Atlases un atkārtošanas loģika tiek īstenota `scripts/install/ansible.sh`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The selection tokens that reproduce exactly what did not pass."
msgstr "Atlases žetoni, kas precīzi atveido to, kas netika izturēts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The selections of the last finished deploy run on the branch that are not green. `cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.failed_selections` reads them straight out of the job titles, so each candidate arrives with the variant, mode and onion state it failed in."
msgstr "Pēdējās pabeigtās izvietošanas izlases palaistas uz zara, kas nav zaļa. `cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.failed_selections` nolasa tos tieši no amata nosaukumiem, tāpēc katrs kandidāts ierodas ar variantu, režīmu un sīpolu stāvoklī tas neizdevās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sequenced flow lives in [`routine/`](routine/), the naming SPOT in `utils/topology/`, shared helpers in `utils/`, and the cluster declaration (image, containers, network, DNS play) in `compose/swarm/` + `compose/swarm/compose.yml`."
msgstr "Secīga plūsma dzīvo [`routine/`](routine/), nosaukums SPOT `utils/topology/`, kopīgi palīgi `utils/`, un kopas deklarācija (attēls, konteineri, tīkls, DNS atskaņot) skaits `compose/swarm/` + `compose/swarm/compose.yml`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server answers with its input, lightly reworded, often enough that the result keeps every span and every markup character while still being English. Comparing scripts catches it wherever the target does not use the Latin one; for a Latin-script target it would need a language detector."
msgstr "Serveris atbild ar savu ievadi, viegli pārfrāzēts, bieži vien pietiekami, ka rezultāts saglabā katru laidumu un katru marķējumu raksturs, kamēr vēl ir angļu valodā. Salīdzināšana skripti nozvejot to visur, kur mērķis neizmanto latīņu vienu; latīņu rakstības mērķis būtu nepieciešams valodas detektors."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server needs an active browser tab and plugin connection, and can execute powerful design-context operations."
msgstr "Serverim ir nepieciešams aktīvs pārlūka cilnes un spraudņa savienojums, un var veikt jaudīgas dizaina konteksta operācijas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server starts with a token from the deployment's credential store, binds to the container network and publishes no port. Cross-site request checking is off and any origin is accepted, because the caller is a service on the same network that presents the token rather than a browser carrying a cookie."
msgstr "Serveris sākas ar marķierierīci no izvēršanas cidentiālā veikala, saistās ar konteineru tīklu un nepublicē portu. Starpvietņu pieprasījumu pārbaude ir izslēgta un jebkura izcelsme ir pieņemama, jo zvanītājs ir pakalpojums vienā tīklā, kas drīzāk uzrāda marķierierīci, nevis pārlūkprogrammu, kurā ir sīkfails."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server starts with a token from the deployment’s credential store, binds to the container network and publishes no port. Cross-site request checking is off and any origin is accepted, because the caller is a service on the same network that presents the token rather than a browser carrying a cookie."
msgstr "Serveris sākas ar marķierierīci no izvēršanas kredentālā veikala, saistās ar konteineru tīklu un nepublicē portu. Starpvietņu pieprasījumu pārbaude ir izslēgta un jebkura izcelsme ir pieņemama, jo zvanītājs ir pakalpojums vienā tīklā, kas drīzāk uzrāda marķierierīci, nevis pārlūkprogrammu, kurā ir sīkfails."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The server's own thread count follows the CPUs its container may use, which a deploy decides; only the client side is free to vary per run. This sweeps it against real catalog entries and records the winner for the env builder, so a tuned host keeps its numbers across every `make dotenv`."
msgstr "Servera paša pavedienu skaits seko tam, ko var izmantot procesori tā konteinerā, kuru kādā izvietojumā izlemj; tikai klienta puse var brīvi variēt vienā braucienā. Šis slauc to pret reālu katalogu ierakstus un ieraksti uzvarētāju env celtnieks, tāpēc uzskaņots resursdators saglabā savus numurus pāri katru `make dotenv`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The service registry (service key -> provider role) stays built from the full rendered base set so provider discovery is unaffected by the active variants; only the dep-walk sees the variant configs (with the swarm force-shared DB view applied on top)."
msgstr "Pakalpojumu reģistrs (pakalpojumu sniedzēja loma) paliek būvēts no pilna renderēta bāzes komplekta, lai piedāvātāja atrašanu neietekmē aktīvie varianti; tikai dep-walk redz varianta konfigurācijas (ar sānsveres spēku dalītu DB skatu virsotnē)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The service runs as a lightweight Node.js app backed by PostgreSQL."
msgstr "Pakalpojums darbojas kā viegls Node.js app atbalsta ar PostgreSQL."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The settings file additionally sets `\"sandbox\": { \"failIfUnavailable\": true }`. This prevents a dangerous false-security state: if the OS-level sandbox backend (e.g. `bwrap` on Linux, `sandbox-exec` on macOS) is missing or non-functional, Claude Code would otherwise silently fall back to no sandboxing while `autoAllowBashIfSandboxed` continues to auto-approve commands as if they were confined. With `failIfUnavailable: true`, Claude Code refuses to proceed in that situation, forcing the operator to install the missing backend or explicitly downgrade the policy before any command runs. Contributors on systems without a working sandbox backend MUST install the appropriate binary rather than weakening this flag locally."
msgstr "Papildus iestatījumu fails `\"sandbox\": { \"failIfUnavailable\": true }`. Tas novērš bīstamu viltus drošības stāvokli: ja OS līmeņa smilšu kastes aizmugure (Piemēram, `bwrap` par Linux, `sandbox-exec` par makOS) ir pazudis vai nedarbojas, Claude Code citādi klusi krist atpakaļ bez smilšu kastes, bet `autoAllowBashIfSandboxed` turpina automātiski piešķirt komandas, it kā tās būtu ierobežotas. kur: `failIfUnavailable: true`, Claude Code atsakās rīkoties šādā situācijā, piespiežot operatoru uzstādīt trūkstošo aizmuguri vai skaidri pazemināt politiku pirms komandas vadīšanas. Atbalstītāji uz sistēmām bez darba smilšu kastes aizmugure jāuzstāda atbilstošu bināro nevis vājinot šo karogu uz vietas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The setup tasks handle the full first-deploy bootstrap automatically:"
msgstr "Uzstādīšanas uzdevumi apstrādā pilnu pirmās izvietošanas bootstrat automātiski:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shape each key must have is declared per role rather than here, in [roles/svc-ai-litellm/meta/secrets.yml](../../../../../roles/svc-ai-litellm/meta/secrets.yml) with a `type:` and a `regex:`. The pattern rejects a truncated or whitespace-carrying paste and deliberately accepts any vendor prefix, so a provider changing its issuance format cannot turn a valid key into a failed inventory run."
msgstr "Katras atslēgas forma ir deklarēta par lomu, nevis šeit, jo [roles/svc-ai-litellm/meta/secrets.yml](../../../../../roles/svc-ai-litellm/meta/secrets.yml) ar `type:` un a `regex:`. Modelis noraida atdalītu vai atstarpi nesošu pastu un apzināti pieņem jebkuru pārdevēja priedēkli, tāpēc pakalpojuma sniedzējs, mainot savu izdošanas formātu, nevar pārvērst derīgu atslēgu neveiksmīgā inventāra braucienā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shape every consumer renders from: the ansible lookups, which then apply the inventory, and the dev stack, which does not."
msgstr "Forma katrs patērētājs renderē no: ansible lookups, kas pēc tam piemēro inventāra, un dev steka, kas nav."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shape mirrors the schema tree: nested keys stay nested. The literal string is preserved verbatim, with no rendering and no validation. Leaves WITHOUT ``default:`` are intentionally absent so the inventory's apply_schema-generated values win the merge."
msgstr "Forma atstaro schema koku: ligzdas taustiņi palikt ligzdu. Burtiskā virkne tiek saglabāta stenogrammā, bez renderēšanas un bez apstiprināšanas. Lapas BEZ ``default:`` nav apzināti, lai inventārs ir apply_schema- izveido vērtības uzvarēt apvienojumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Nextcloud presents three different login surfaces depending on the variant (native, ``oidc_login``, ``sociallogin``), the native administrator authenticates with the role-local ``credentials.administrator_password`` rather than the Keycloak secret, and the ``#firstrunwizard`` modal intercepts the user-menu click the generic logout depends on. Both personas are therefore driven by the role’s own login specs — ``test-login-admin-native.js``, ``test-login-admin-oidc.js``, ``test-login-biber-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-biber-ldap.js`` under ``files/playwright/`` — which carry the flavor switch, the modal dismissal and the login retry the shared helper lacks."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas palīgi tiek pasludināti par bloķētiem `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Nextcloud piedāvā trīs dažādas pieteikšanās virsmas atkarībā no varianta (dzimtā, ``oidc_login``, ``sociallogin``), dzimtā administrators autentificējas ar lomu-vietējo ``credentials.administrator_password`` Nevis Keycloak un ``#firstrunwizard`` modāls pārtver lietotāja-menu klikšķi, no kā ir atkarīga vispārēja atteikšanās. Tāpēc abas personas virza loma paša pieteikšanās specs — ``test-login-admin-native.js``, ``test-login-admin-oidc.js``, ``test-login-biber-oidc.js`` kā arī ``test-login-biber-ldap.js`` zem ``files/playwright/`` — kas nes garšas pārslēgu, modālo atlaišanu un pieteikšanās atkārtošanu kopīgajam palīgam trūkst."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Odoo renders its SSO provider link only on ``/web/login`` inside the ``.o_login_auth`` container, not on the site root the persona helper starts from, and it exposes no in-app logout control — signing out means navigating to ``/web/session/logout``. The full Keycloak round trip for both users is covered by the role’s own ``odoo: admin sso login, verify ui, logout`` and ``odoo: biber sso login, verify ui, logout`` scenarios in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas palīgi tiek pasludināti par bloķētiem `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Odoo padara savu SSO pakalpojumu sniedzēja saiti tikai uz ``/web/login`` sastāvdaļu ``.o_login_auth`` konteiners, nevis uz vietas saknes persona palīgs sākas no, un tas pakļauj nekādu in-app piesakās kontroli – parakstīšanās nozīmē navigācija uz ``/web/session/logout``. Pilns Keycloak brauciens turp un atpakaļ abiem lietotājiem ir ietverta loma ``odoo: admin sso login, verify ui, logout`` kā arī ``odoo: biber sso login, verify ui, logout`` scenāriji `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. OpenCloud Web answers Playwright’s headless Chromium user agent with a “browser not supported” splash unless ``forceAllowOldBrowser`` is seeded into ``localStorage`` before the first navigation, and its OIDC callback runs through OpenCloud’s own ``/oidc-callback`` → ``/web-oidc-callback`` routes instead of the oauth2-proxy pattern the shared helper detects. Both personas’ Keycloak round trip is covered by `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__, which does that priming in `files/playwright/\\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas palīgi tiek pasludināti par bloķētiem `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. OpenCloud Web atbildes Playwright s headless Chromium lietotāja aģents ar “browser nav atbalstīts” šļakatu, ja vien ``forceAllowOldBrowser`` tiek izsēta ``localStorage`` pirms pirmās navigācijas, un tās OIDC atzvanīšana iet cauri OpenCloudpaša ``/oidc-callback`` → ``/web-oidc-callback`` maršruti2-Proxy modelis kopīgo palīgs atklāj. Abas personas” Keycloak brauciens turp un atpakaļ `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__, kas to dara, lai `files/playwright/\\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Pixelfed’s login id is the account e-mail rather than the Keycloak username, and the artisan-bootstrapped administrator name is reserved, so pixelfed’s first-time OIDC registration cannot mint it either. ``biber`` additionally needs his Keycloak e-mail rewritten to a resolvable domain through the Keycloak admin API before the first OIDC login, because pixelfed’s ``dns,spoof`` validator rejects ``.example`` addresses. Both setups live in `files/playwright/\\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__ and drive the dedicated login specs in ``files/playwright/``."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas palīgi tiek pasludināti par bloķētiem `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Pixelfed pieteikšanās id ir konta e-pastu, nevis Keycloak lietotājvārds, un amatnieciski bootstrapped administrators nosaukums ir rezervēts, tāpēc pixelfed pirmo reizi OIDC reģistrācija nevar kalt to arī. ``biber`` papildus nepieciešams viņa Keycloak e-pasts pārrakstīts uz noregulējamu domēnu caur Keycloak admin API pirms pirmā OIDC pieteikšanās, jo pixelfed s ``dns,spoof`` vērtētājs noraida ``.example`` adreses. Abi iestatījumi dzīvo `files/playwright/\\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__ un vadīt veltīta pieteikšanās specs in ``files/playwright/``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. The OpenTalk frontend is a public-client OIDC single-page app — the container env carries nothing but the issuer and the client id, there is no server-side session and no HTML login form — so the role drives it with its own redirect-racing helper keyed on ``LOGIN_*`` / ``BIBER_*`` instead of the ``ADMIN_*`` pair the shared helper expects, and the browser-side session leaves the contract’s in-app logout leg without a target. Both personas’ Keycloak → dashboard chain is covered by `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas palīgi tiek pasludināti par bloķētiem `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. OpenTalk frontend ir publiska-klients OIDC vienas lapas app — konteiners env nes neko, bet emitents un klients id, nav servera puses sesiju un nav HTML pieteikšanās forma - tāpēc loma vada to ar savu novirzīt-rakšanas palīgs taustiņu uz ``LOGIN_*`` / ``BIBER_*`` vietā ``ADMIN_*`` pāri kopīgo palīgs sagaida, un pārlūkprogrammas puses sesija atstāj līguma in-app pieteikšanās kāju bez mērķa. Abas personas” Keycloak → paneļa ķēdi sedz `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. The role provisions no pretix account at all — `tasks/main.yml <./tasks/main.yml>`__ only deploys the stack — while pretix’s native auth backend authenticates a pretix ``User`` row that is created by the interactive first-run setup. The ``pretix-oidc`` backend added on top lives on pretix’s ``/control`` login page, whereas the role’s base URL serves the public ticket shop that the baseline scenarios in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__ assert. Seeding a backend user is the path back to a runnable persona journey."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas palīgi tiek pasludināti par bloķētiem `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Nozīme neparedz pretix kontu vispār – `tasks/main.yml <./tasks/main.yml>`__ tikai izvieto steku — kamēr pretix dzimtā auth aizmugure autentificē pretix ``User`` rindu, kas ir izveidota ar interaktīvu pirmās kārtas uzstādīšanas. E ir o pa s ``pretix-oidc`` Aizmugure pievienota uz augšu dzīvi uz pretix s ``/control`` pieteikšanās lapa, bet lomu bāzes URL kalpo publiskā biļešu veikals, ka bāzes scenāriji `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__ apgalvo. Piedāvāt aizmugures lietotāju ir ceļš atpakaļ uz vadāmu personu braucienu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. As soon as an IAM source is wired, the role sets ``GITEA__service__DISABLE_REGISTRATION`` (``templates/env.j2``, driven by ``GITEA_IAM_ENABLED`` in ``vars/main.yml``), and ``tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` registers only the auth source — never a Gitea user — so a Keycloak identity without a pre-linked Gitea account is bounced back to ``/user/login``. The opt-out lapses once the deploy provisions (or auto-links) Gitea accounts for the persona identities."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas braucienus izvēlas, izmantojot ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` skaits ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Tiklīdz IAM avots ir vadu, lomu komplekti ``GITEA__service__DISABLE_REGISTRATION`` (``templates/env.j2``, brauc ``GITEA_IAM_ENABLED`` skaits ``vars/main.yml``), un ``tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` reģistrē tikai auth avots – nekad Gitea līdz ar to Keycloak identitāte bez iepriekš piesaistīta Gitea konts ir piepeši atpakaļ uz ``/user/login``. Atteikšanās zaudē spēku pēc tam, kad spēkā stāšanās noteikumi (vai automātiskās saites) Gitea veido personas identitāti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Fider’s SSO entry is a two-step modal: the header “Sign in” button only opens the provider dialog, and a second click on “Continue with … SSO” performs the Keycloak redirect, whereas the shared helper clicks exactly once and never reaches the IdP. Both journeys are covered end-to-end by this role’s own ``fider: admin sso login`` and ``fider: biber sso login as regular user`` scenarios in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``; the opt-out lapses once the shared helper learns Fider’s modal."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas braucienus izvēlas, izmantojot ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` skaits ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Fider SSO ieraksts ir divpakāpju modāls: galvene “Sign in” poga tikai atver pakalpojumu sniedzēja dialogu, un otrais klikšķis “Turpināt ar ... SSO” veic Keycloak novirzīt, bet dalītais palīgs klikšķi tieši vienreiz un nekad sasniedz IdP. Abiem braucieniem no gala līdz galam ir sava loma. ``fider: admin sso login`` kā arī ``fider: biber sso login as regular user`` scenāriji ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``; atteikšanās zaudē, kad dalītais palīgs mācās Fidermodāls."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Flowise has no in-app OIDC adapter: SSO is an oauth2-proxy sidecar (``services.sso.flavor: oauth2``), and behind that gate Flowise still presents its own sign-in form for the single instance account seeded from ``FLOWISE_USERNAME`` / ``FLOWISE_PASSWORD`` in ``templates/env.j2``. ``biber`` has no Flowise identity at all, and the shared helpers only drive Keycloak forms while ``services.sso`` is enabled, so neither persona can reach an authenticated Flowise surface; the OIDC gate itself is covered by ``files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js``."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas braucienus izvēlas, izmantojot ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` skaits ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Flowise nav in-app OIDC adapter: SSO ir oauth2- proxy sidecar (``services.sso.flavor: oauth2``), un aiz tiem vārtiem Flowise joprojām uzrāda savu reģistrācijas formu, kas paredzēta vienīgā kontam, no kura ``FLOWISE_USERNAME`` / ``FLOWISE_PASSWORD`` skaits ``templates/env.j2``. ``biber`` nav Flowise identitāte vispār, un kopīgi palīgi tikai vadīt Keycloak forma ``services.sso`` ir ieslēgta, tāpēc neviens persona var sasniegt autentificēts Flowise virsmu; pati OIDC vārtiem sedz ``files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Joomla’s site template ships no login/logout module, and ``plg_system_keycloak`` exposes sign-out only as the route ``index.php?option=keycloak&task=logout`` (``files/joomla-oidc-plugin/plg_system_keycloak/src/Extension/Keycloak.php``, ``handleLogout``) rather than as a rendered control, so the persona’s mandatory in-app logout click has no target and navigating a logout URL directly is forbidden by the contract. The OIDC handshake itself, the LDAP variant and the ``/administrator?fallback=local`` hatch are covered by ``files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js``, ``test-ldap-login.js`` and ``test-oidc-fallback.js``."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas braucienus izvēlas, izmantojot ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` skaits ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Joomla vietas veidnes kuģiem nav pieteikšanās / pieteikšanās modulis, un ``plg_system_keycloak`` atklāj izrakstīšanos tikai kā maršrutu ``index.php?option=keycloak&task=logout`` (``files/joomla-oidc-plugin/plg_system_keycloak/src/Extension/Keycloak.php``, ``handleLogout``) nevis kā renderēta kontrole, tāpēc persona ir obligāta in-app pieteikšanās klikšķis nav mērķa un navigācija pieteikšanās URL tieši ir aizliegta ar līgumu. Pati OIDC rokasspiediens, LDAP variants un ``/administrator?fallback=local`` lūku sedz ``files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js``, ``test-ldap-login.js`` kā arī ``test-oidc-fallback.js``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, no-python-format, python-brace-format
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Outside the OIDC variant, ``templates/casc.yaml.j2`` selects the ``ldap`` or ``local`` security realm and Jenkins’ only login surface is its own Java-realm form, whose fields are named ``j_username`` / ``j_password`` (pinned by the LDAP scenario in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``) — names the shared native-login probe does not match, so the persona never authenticates. The flag is currently unconditional; narrowing it to ``{% if not JENKINS_OIDC_ENABLED %}`` once the OIDC persona journey has been verified end-to-end is the path back."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas braucienus izvēlas, izmantojot ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` skaits ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. ārpus OIDC varianta; ``templates/casc.yaml.j2`` izvēlas ``ldap`` vai ``local`` drošības joma un Jenkins” vienīgā pieteikšanās virsma ir tā Java-reāla forma, kuras lauki ir nosaukti ``j_username`` / ``j_password`` (Name ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``) — nenosauc kopīgoto native-login zondi, tāpēc persona nekad autentificējas. Karogs pašlaik ir beznosacījumu; sašaurinot to ``{% if not JENKINS_OIDC_ENABLED %}`` tiklīdz OIDC persona ceļojums ir pārbaudīts no gala līdz galam ir ceļš atpakaļ."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. The oauth2-proxy sidecar only gates the vhost — FusionDirectory keeps its own LDAP-bind login behind it, which the role’s OIDC scenario in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` asserts by expecting a “Sign in” button to still be visible after the Keycloak round-trip. ``tasks/main.yml`` provisions no FusionDirectory account, so the Keycloak identity maps to no directory session the shared helpers could carry through to an in-app logout."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas braucienus izvēlas, izmantojot ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` skaits ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Zvaigznes2- proxy blakusvāģis tikai vārtiem vhost - FusionDirectory saglabā savu LDAP-bind pieteikšanās aiz tā, kas loma OIDC scenārijs ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` apgalvo, gaidot “Pierakstīties” pogas joprojām ir redzams pēc Keycloak turp un atpakaļ. ``tasks/main.yml`` Noteikumu nav FusionDirectory līdz ar to Keycloak identitātes kartes uz ne direktoriju sesiju kopīgotie palīgi varētu veikt uz in-app logout."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. web-app-hugo serves a statically built site: ``services.sso`` is hard-disabled in ``meta/services.yml``, the container is a Hugo build baked into nginx (``templates/compose.yml.j2``), and the Playwright env file renders no ``ADMIN_*`` / ``BIBER_*`` credentials. There is no session, no admin surface and no logout control to drive, so the ``guest`` persona plus the reachability, CSP and rendered-HTML assertions are the complete contract for this role."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` kā arī ``administrator`` personas braucienus izvēlas, izmantojot ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` skaits ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. web-app-hugo kalpo statiski būvētai vietai: ``services.sso`` ir grūti atspējots ``meta/services.yml``, konteiners Hugo iebūvēts ginksā (``templates/compose.yml.j2``), un Playwright env fails padara nē ``ADMIN_*`` / ``BIBER_*`` pilnvaras. Nav sesija, nav admin virsmas un nav atteikšanās kontroli vadīt, tāpēc ``guest`` persona plus sasniedzamība, CSP un refer-HTML apgalvojumi ir pilnīgs līgums par šo lomu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` persona journey is opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. A Jellyfin account binds to exactly one authentication provider, so biber’s login is owned by the per-addon specs that know which provider is live: ``files/playwright/addons/sso-authentication.spec.js`` for OIDC and ``addons/ldap-authentication.spec.js`` for the LDAP-only matrix variant. The generic persona cannot pick between them and would duplicate or contradict that coverage; ``playwright.spec.js`` keeps the ``guest`` scenario and the native administrator login."
msgstr "Dalītais ``biber`` persona ceļojums ir izslēgts caur ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` skaits ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. A Jellyfin konts saistās tieši ar vienu autentifikācijas pakalpojumu sniedzēju, tāpēc bibder 's login pieder per-addon specs ka zināt, kurš pakalpojumu sniedzējs ir dzīvs: ``files/playwright/addons/sso-authentication.spec.js`` OIDC gadījumā un ``addons/ldap-authentication.spec.js`` tikai LDAP matricas variantam. Nepatentētā persona nevar izvēlēties starp tām un dublēt vai apstrīdēt šo pārklājumu; ``playwright.spec.js`` saglabā ``guest`` scenārijs un dzimtā administratora pieteikšanās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Nextcloud presents three different login surfaces depending on the variant (native, `oidc_login`, `sociallogin`), the native administrator authenticates with the role-local `credentials.administrator_password` rather than the Keycloak secret, and the `#firstrunwizard` modal intercepts the user-menu click the generic logout depends on. Both personas are therefore driven by the role's own login specs — `test-login-admin-native.js`, `test-login-admin-oidc.js`, `test-login-biber-oidc.js` and `test-login-biber-ldap.js` under `files/playwright/` — which carry the flavor switch, the modal dismissal and the login retry the shared helper lacks."
msgstr "Dalītais `biber` kā arī `administrator` personas palīgi tiek pasludināti par bloķētiem [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Nextcloud piedāvā trīs dažādas pieteikšanās virsmas atkarībā no varianta (dzimtā, `oidc_login`, `sociallogin`), dzimtā administrators autentificējas ar lomu-vietējo `credentials.administrator_password` Nevis Keycloak un `#firstrunwizard` modāls pārtver lietotāja-menu klikšķi, no kā ir atkarīga vispārēja atteikšanās. Tādēļ abas personas virza pašas loma pieteikšanās specs — `test-login-admin-native.js`, `test-login-admin-oidc.js`, `test-login-biber-oidc.js` kā arī `test-login-biber-ldap.js` zem `files/playwright/` — kas nes garšas pārslēgu, modālo atlaišanu un pieteikšanās atkārtošanu kopīgajam palīgam trūkst."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Odoo renders its SSO provider link only on `/web/login` inside the `.o_login_auth` container, not on the site root the persona helper starts from, and it exposes no in-app logout control — signing out means navigating to `/web/session/logout`. The full Keycloak round trip for both users is covered by the role's own `odoo: admin sso login, verify ui, logout` and `odoo: biber sso login, verify ui, logout` scenarios in [files/playwright/playwright.spec.js](./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js)."
msgstr "Dalītais `biber` kā arī `administrator` personas palīgi tiek pasludināti par bloķētiem [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Odoo padara savu SSO pakalpojumu sniedzēja saiti tikai uz `/web/login` sastāvdaļu `.o_login_auth` konteiners, nevis uz vietas saknes persona palīgs sākas no, un tas pakļauj nekādu in-app piesakās kontroli – parakstīšanās nozīmē navigācija uz `/web/session/logout`. Pilns Keycloak brauciens turp un atpakaļ abiem lietotājiem ir saistīta ar lomu `odoo: admin sso login, verify ui, logout` kā arī `odoo: biber sso login, verify ui, logout` scenāriji [files/playwright/playwright.spec.js](./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). OpenCloud Web answers Playwright's headless Chromium user agent with a \"browser not supported\" splash unless `forceAllowOldBrowser` is seeded into `localStorage` before the first navigation, and its OIDC callback runs through OpenCloud's own `/oidc-callback` → `/web-oidc-callback` routes instead of the oauth2-proxy pattern the shared helper detects. Both personas' Keycloak round trip is covered by [files/playwright/test-sso-login.js](./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js), which does that priming in [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js)."
msgstr "Dalītais `biber` kā arī `administrator` personas palīgi tiek pasludināti par bloķētiem [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). OpenCloud Web atbildes Playwright ir bez galvas Chromium lietotāju aģents ar \"pārlūks nav atbalstīts\" šļaksts, ja vien `forceAllowOldBrowser` tiek izsēta `localStorage` pirms pirmās navigācijas, un tās OIDC atzvanīšana iet cauri OpenCloud's pašu `/oidc-callback` → `/web-oidc-callback` maršruti2-Proxy modelis kopīgo palīgs atklāj. Abas personas” Keycloak brauciens turp un atpakaļ [files/playwright/test-sso-login.js](./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js), kas to dara, lai [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Pixelfed's login id is the account e-mail rather than the Keycloak username, and the artisan-bootstrapped administrator name is reserved, so pixelfed's first-time OIDC registration cannot mint it either. `biber` additionally needs his Keycloak e-mail rewritten to a resolvable domain through the Keycloak admin API before the first OIDC login, because pixelfed's `dns,spoof` validator rejects `.example` addresses. Both setups live in [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js) and drive the dedicated login specs in `files/playwright/`."
msgstr "Dalītais `biber` kā arī `administrator` personas palīgi tiek pasludināti par bloķētiem [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Pixelfed pieteikšanās id ir konta e-pasts, nevis Keycloak lietotājvārds, un amatnieciski bootstrapped administrators nosaukums ir rezervēts, tāpēc pixelfed pirmo reizi OIDC reģistrācija nevar kalt to arī. `biber` papildus nepieciešams viņa Keycloak e-pasts pārrakstīts uz noregulējamu domēnu caur Keycloak admin API pirms pirmās OIDC pieteikšanās, jo pikseļu barotājs `dns,spoof` vērtētājs noraida `.example` adreses. Abi iestatījumi dzīvo [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js) un vadīt veltīta pieteikšanās specs in `files/playwright/`."

