# translation-rejected: Dalītais `biber` kā arī `administrator` personas
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona journeys are opted out via `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` / `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`. The oauth2-proxy sidecar only gates the vhost — FusionDirectory keeps its own LDAP-bind login behind it, which the role's OIDC scenario in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` asserts by expecting a \"Sign in\" button to still be visible after the Keycloak round-trip. `tasks/main.yml` provisions no FusionDirectory account, so the Keycloak identity maps to no directory session the shared helpers could carry through to an in-app logout."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona journeys are opted out via `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` / `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`. web-app-hugo serves a statically built site: `services.sso` is hard-disabled in `meta/services.yml`, the container is a Hugo build baked into nginx (`templates/compose.yml.j2`), and the Playwright env file renders no `ADMIN_*` / `BIBER_*` credentials. There is no session, no admin surface and no logout control to drive, so the `guest` persona plus the reachability, CSP and rendered-HTML assertions are the complete contract for this role."
msgstr "Dalītais `biber` kā arī `administrator` personas braucienus izvēlas, izmantojot `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` / `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` skaits `templates/playwright.env.j2`. web-app-hugo kalpo statiski būvētai vietai: `services.sso` ir grūti atspējots `meta/services.yml`, konteiners Hugo iebūvēts ginksā (`templates/compose.yml.j2`), un Playwright env fails padara nē `ADMIN_*` / `BIBER_*` pilnvaras. Nav sesija, nav admin virsmas un nav atteikšanās kontroli vadīt, tāpēc `guest` persona plus sasniedzamība, CSP un refer-HTML apgalvojumi ir pilnīgs līgums par šo lomu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `biber` persona journey is opted out via `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`. A Jellyfin account binds to exactly one authentication provider, so biber's login is owned by the per-addon specs that know which provider is live: `files/playwright/addons/sso-authentication.spec.js` for OIDC and `addons/ldap-authentication.spec.js` for the LDAP-only matrix variant. The generic persona cannot pick between them and would duplicate or contradict that coverage; `playwright.spec.js` keeps the `guest` scenario and the native administrator login."
msgstr "Dalītais `biber` persona ceļojums ir izslēgts caur `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` skaits `templates/playwright.env.j2`. A Jellyfin konts saistās tieši ar vienu autentifikācijas pakalpojumu sniedzēju, tāpēc Biber 's login pieder per-addon specs, kas zina, kurš pakalpojumu sniedzējs ir dzīvs: `files/playwright/addons/sso-authentication.spec.js` OIDC gadījumā un `addons/ldap-authentication.spec.js` tikai LDAP matricas variantam. Nepatentētā persona nevar izvēlēties starp tām un dublēt vai apstrīdēt šo pārklājumu; `playwright.spec.js` saglabā `guest` scenārijs un dzimtā administratora pieteikšanās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `default.json.j2` MUST stay generic. App-specific protocol mappers, claims, or scopes MUST NOT be added there because the change affects every other client."
msgstr "Dalītais `default.json.j2` Jāpatur vispārīgs. Lietotnei specifisks protokols kartētāji, pretenzijas, vai tvērums nav jāpievieno tur, jo izmaiņas ietekmē katru citu klientu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared root file comes first and carries ``None`` as its role."
msgstr "Dalītais saknes fails ir pirmais un nes ``None`` kā savu lomu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared schema and first end-to-end slice MAY land together."
msgstr "Kopīgi shēma un pirmais beigu-to-end šķēle MAY kopā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared schema, loader, lint, and the first migrated role MAY land together."
msgstr "Kopīga shēma, iekrāvējs, lint, un pirmais migrēja loma MAI kopā nolaižas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shell prefix, or an empty string when email is disabled."
msgstr "Čaulas prefikss vai tukša virkne, kad e- pasts ir atslēgts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The shell-side installer scripts loop over distros with their own variable, so they render ``{slug}`` themselves rather than per distro."
msgstr "Čaulas puses uzstādītājs skripti cilpa virs distros ar savu mainīgo, tāpēc viņi renderēt ``{slug}`` paši, nevis per distro."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shipped weights are `locality: 1.0`, `cost: 0.4`, `speed: 0.25`, `caching: 0.15`, `throughput: 0.1`, and the constraint behind them is that locality **exceeds** the sum of the others, so no combination of the rest outscores staying in the cluster. That is a preference, not the protection: decision 7's restriction removes remote candidates before this runs, which is why a weighting that sends everything to the cheapest provider still cannot send a credential there."
msgstr "Nosūtīto svaru: `locality: 1.0`, `cost: 0.4`, `speed: 0.25`, `caching: 0.15`, `throughput: 0.1`, un ierobežojums aiz tiem ir, ka vieta **pārsniedz** pārējo summu, tāpēc nav kombinācija pārējo uzstāšanos klasterī. Tā ir priekšroka, nevis aizsardzība: lēmums 7's ierobežojums noņem attālos kandidātus pirms šīs darbības, tāpēc svērums, kas nosūta visu lētākajam pakalpojumu sniedzējam, joprojām nevar nosūtīt uz turieni pilnvaru."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shipped weights keep locality worth at least the other factors combined"
msgstr "Nosūtītie svari saglabā vietas vērtību vismaz citu faktoru kopā"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The short version:"
msgstr "Īsā versija:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar authenticates a Gitea token"
msgstr "Blakusvāģis autentificē a Gitea marķieris"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar creates its consumer's bucket itself at startup because a swarm stack's converge gate blocks before any post-deploy task could create it, deadlocking consumers that hard-fail on a missing bucket (e.g. the OpenTalk controller). The stock entrypoint routes every argv through ``weed`` (``sh`` as a command would become ``weed sh``), so the template overrides it with ``sh -c``; the server itself is still launched via ``/entrypoint.sh`` to keep its /data chown, privilege drop, and default server args."
msgstr "Blakusvāģis rada sava patērētāja spainis sevi pie starta, jo bara kaudze ir konverģents vārtu bloki pirms jebkurš post-deploy uzdevums varētu radīt to, strupceļā patērētājus, ka grūti trūkums uz trūkst spainis (Piemēram, OpenTalk kontrolieris). Krājumu ieejas punktu maršruti katru argv caur ``weed`` (``sh`` kā komanda kļūtu ``weed sh``), tā ka sagatave to aizstāj ar ``sh -c``; pats serveris joprojām tiek palaists caur ``/entrypoint.sh`` saglabāt tās / datu chown, privilēģija kritums, un noklusējuma servera args."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar is never routed publicly. A bearerless probe of `/mcp` on the public vhost is answered with an SSO redirect, never with an MCP response."
msgstr "Blakusvāģis nekad nav publiski maršrutēts. bezuzgaļa zonde `/mcp` par sabiedrības vhost tiek atbildēts ar SSO novirzīt, nekad ar MCP atbildi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar is never routed publicly. A bearerless probe of ``/mcp`` on the public vhost is answered with an SSO redirect, never with an MCP response."
msgstr "Blakusvāģis nekad nav publiski maršrutēts. bezuzgaļa zonde ``/mcp`` par sabiedrības vhost tiek atbildēts ar SSO novirzīt, nekad ar MCP atbildi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar is reachable on the container network only, so a client probes it from inside the stack:"
msgstr "Blakusvāģis ir sasniedzams tikai konteineru tīklā, tāpēc klients to zondē no skursteņa iekšpuses:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar oauth2-proxy admits only the LibreTranslate administrator RBAC group and whitelists just the machine API paths (`/translate`, `/detect`, …); see [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml). Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under [Single sign-on](#single-sign-on) above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`. The `administrator` and `guest` personas run unconditionally."
msgstr "Blakusvāģis2- proxy pieļauj tikai LibreTranslate administrators RBAC grupa un whitlists tikai mašīna API ceļi (`/translate`, `/detect`, ...); skat. [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml). Iekšā lietotnē, atļauja ir API- tikai atslēgas līmeņa un atdalīti no IdP, kā dokumentēts [Viena pierakstīšanās](#single-sign-on) iepriekš. Ne- admin apmeklētājs tāpēc nav UI sesiju vadīt, tāpēc [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) deklarē `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`. `administrator` kā arī `guest` persona darbojas bez nosacījumiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar oauth2-proxy admits only the LibreTranslate administrator RBAC group and whitelists just the machine API paths (``/translate``, ``/detect``, …); see ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under `Single sign-on <#single-sign-on>`__ above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run unconditionally."
msgstr "Blakusvāģis2- proxy pieļauj tikai LibreTranslate administrators RBAC grupa un whitlists tikai mašīna API ceļi (``/translate``, ``/detect``, ...); skat. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under `Viena pierakstīšanās <#single-sign-on>`__ above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` persona darbojas bez nosacījumiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar reads its upstream credential from an ``upstream.env`` file rather than from the compose environment, because the app password does not exist when the stack is first rendered. ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through ``svc-ai-mcp-adapter``\\ ’s ``rebuild.yml``: ``compose up`` resolves ``env_file`` while creating the container, which a restart would not."
msgstr "Blakusvāģis nolasa savu senatnīgo ``upstream.env`` failu, nevis no komponē vidi, jo app paroli neeksistē, kad steka pirmo reizi renderēta. ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through ``svc-ai-mcp-adapter``\\ ’s ``rebuild.yml``: ``compose up`` resolves ``env_file`` radot konteineru, kuru restartēt nevarētu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar reads its upstream credential from an `upstream.env` file rather than from the compose environment, because the app password does not exist when the stack is first rendered. [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through `svc-ai-mcp-adapter`'s `rebuild.yml`: `compose up` resolves `env_file` while creating the container, which a restart would not."
msgstr "Blakusvāģis nolasa savu senatnīgo `upstream.env` failu, nevis no komponē vidi, jo app paroli neeksistē, kad steka pirmo reizi renderēta. [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) raksta šo failu pēc piparmētru un atjauno blakusvāģi caur `svc-ai-mcp-adapter`'s `rebuild.yml`: `compose up` atrisinājumi `env_file` radot konteineru, kuru restartēt nevarētu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar starts with `-r` (read-only) and a scope list covering user, repository, issue, pull request, search, file, branch, tag, commit and release."
msgstr "Blakusvāģis sākas ar `-r` (tikai lasāms) un darbības jomas sarakstu, kas aptver lietotāju, repozitoriju, izdošanu, pull pieprasījumu, meklēšanu, failu, filiāles, tag, nodot un atbrīvot."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar starts with ``-r`` (read-only) and a scope list covering user, repository, issue, pull request, search, file, branch, tag, commit and release."
msgstr "Blakusvāģis sākas ar ``-r`` (tikai lasāms) un darbības jomas sarakstu, kas aptver lietotāju, repozitoriju, izdošanu, pull pieprasījumu, meklēšanu, failu, filiāles, tag, nodot un atbrīvot."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The single `make compose-deploy` target resolves one or more bundles into the role groups declared under `all.children` and feeds them into the standard local deploy flow when `bundles=<csv>` is set. The resolver is [`utils.inventory.bundle_apps`](../../utils/inventory/bundle_apps.py); it deduplicates across bundles and preserves declaration order."
msgstr "Viens `make compose-deploy` mērķis atrisina vienu vai vairākus grupējumus lomu grupās deklarēto `all.children` un ievada tos standarta vietējā izvietojuma plūsmu, kad `bundles=<csv>` ir iestatīts. Atrisinātājs ir [`utils.inventory.bundle_apps`](../../utils/inventory/bundle_apps.py); tas deduplicē pa saišķiem un saglabā deklarēšanas kārtību."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The single point of truth for the cache. A role declares the repositories it needs Nexus to proxy and, where a container must resolve an upstream by name, the hostname the frontend answers for::"
msgstr "Vienots patiesības punkts kešam. Loma paziņo repozitorijiem, kas tiem vajadzīgi Nexus, lai pilnvarotu, un, ja konteineram ir jāatrisina augšpusē pēc nosaukuma, resursdatora nosaukums, uz kuru priekšējā daļa atbild par:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The single-database dumps, and the cluster dumps, which name their instance in the file name and go through ``baudolo-restore cluster``."
msgstr "Vienas datubāzes izgāztuves, un klastera izgāztuves, kas nosaukumu savu instanci faila nosaukumu un iet caur ``baudolo-restore cluster``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The single-token `gh * <verb>*` patterns above only match when the third token starts with the verb. Compound names like `item-create` or `mark-template` slip through because the third token is the full compound, not the bare verb. These rules close that gap for Projects v2 mutations namespace-wide."
msgstr "Vienkomponenta `gh * <verb>*` modeļiem virs tikai saskaņot, kad trešais marķieris sākas ar darbības vārdu. Šādi salikti nosaukumi `item-create` vai `mark-template` izslīdēt cauri, jo trešais marķieris ir pilns savienojums, nevis tukšs darbības vārds. Šie noteikumi novērš nepilnības projektos v2 mutācijas vārdtelpā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The size is the config blob plus every layer blob, i.e. what a pull moves over the wire. A multi-platform index is resolved to the ``os_name``/``architecture`` manifest first."
msgstr "Izmērs ir konfigurācija blob plus katrs slānis blob, t.i., ko pull pārvietojas pa vadu. Daudzplatformu indekss ir atrisināts ``os_name``/``architecture`` izrakstiet vispirms."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The skill writes `.claude/settings.json` / `.claude/settings.local.json`, which is the source of truth for the permission model itself: allow/ask/deny rules, sandbox scope, env vars, and hook commands that run on every tool event. Auto-allowing it creates a privilege-escalation path where the agent can grant itself arbitrary new `allow` entries, install hooks that run arbitrary shell, or widen `sandbox.filesystem.allowWrite` / shrink `denyRead`, all without ever prompting. Sandbox write-scope does not stop this because `.` is in `allowWrite`. A single wildcard entry (`update-config*`) covers every current and future invocation shape in one rule."
msgstr "Prasmju raksti `.claude/settings.json` / `.claude/settings.local.json`, kas ir patiesības avots atļaujas modelim pats: allow/ask/deny noteikumi, smilšu kastes darbības joma, env var, un āķis komandas, kas darbojas uz katru rīku notikumu. Auto-ļaujot tas rada privilēģiju eskalācijas ceļu, kur aģents var piešķirt sev patvaļīgu jaunu `allow` ierakstus, instalēt āķi, kas palaist patvaļīgu čaulu, vai paplašināt `sandbox.filesystem.allowWrite` / sarukt `denyRead`, visi bez jelkāda pamudinājuma. Sandbox rakstīšanas skats to neaptur, jo `.` ir `allowWrite`. Viena zvaigznītes ieraksts (`update-config*`) aptver katru pašreizējo un nākotnes piesaukuma formu vienā noteikumā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The slug comes from :func:`axes.artifact_slug`, the same call the matrix entry carries into the workflow, so the name this looks for and the name CI uploads cannot drift apart."
msgstr "Gliemeži ir no :func:`axes.artifact_slug`, pats sauciens matricas ieraksta veic darbplūsmu, tāpēc nosaukums, kas tas izskatās un nosaukums CI augšupielādes nevar dreifēt atsevišķi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The software's identity: its repository, read from the group_vars SPOT, its author and address."
msgstr "Programmatūras identitāte: tās repozitorijs, lasīt no group_vars SPOT, tā autors un adrese."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The source code of this software is publicly available for transparency, learning, and private use."
msgstr "Šīs programmatūras pirmkods ir publiski pieejams pārskatāmībai, mācībām un privātai lietošanai."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The source run read a window of the ranking, starting where *carried* put it (:func:`carried_index`) and stopping at its budget. Only the green part of that window is newly settled, so the answer is the last row of the leading run of *successful* rows behind the window's start, as a selection token -- a token still names the same row after the ranking shifts, a row count does not."
msgstr "Avota palaist nolasīt logu ranga, sākot kur *pārvadāti* likt to (:func:`carried_index`) un apstāties pie sava budžeta. Tikai zaļā daļa no šī loga ir tikko nokārtots, tāpēc atbilde ir pēdējā rinda vadošās palaist *veiksmīgi* rindas aiz loga sākuma, kā izvēles marķieri -- marķieris joprojām nosauc to pašu rindu pēc ranga maiņām, rindu skaita nav."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The source run's ``priority`` input, whole."
msgstr "Avota palaišanas ``priority`` ieguldījums, viss."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The spec MUST be at `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`. The role-relative path is the SPOT constant `ROLE_FILE_PLAYWRIGHT_SPEC` in [mapping.py](../../../../../utils/roles/mapping.py); registered as optional on `ROLE_TYPE_APPLICATION`, disallowed elsewhere."
msgstr "Spec ir jābūt `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`. Lomu-relatīvais ceļš ir SPOT konstante `ROLE_FILE_PLAYWRIGHT_SPEC` skaits [mapping.py](../../../../../utils/roles/mapping.py); reģistrēts kā fakultatīvs `ROLE_TYPE_APPLICATION`, nav atļauts citur."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The split means contributors do not need to extend the allowlist for every new shell command: `Bash(*)` already covers them, and sandbox confinement bounds the blast radius. The `deny` list catches the small set of operations whose blast radius is destructive even within the sandbox. For example, `rm -rf .` would still erase the working tree and `.git/` because `.` is writable under `allowWrite`, so the `rm -rf*` deny rule closes that gap."
msgstr "Dalījums nozīmē, ka datu sniedzējiem nav nepieciešams pagarināt katras jaunas čaulas komandas sarakstu: `Bash(*)` jau aptver tos, un smilšu kastes norobežo sprādziena rādiusu. E ir o pa s `deny` uzskaita mazo operāciju kopumu, kuru sprādziena rādiuss ir postošs pat smilšu kastē. Piemēram, `rm -rf .` joprojām izdzēst darba koku un `.git/` jo `.` ir rakstāms saskaņā ar `allowWrite`, Tāpēc `rm -rf*` noliegt noteikums aizver šo plaisu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The stack deploy modes the CI test-deploy matrix (get_role_skip) covers."
msgstr "Steka izvietošanas režīmi CI testēšanas-izvietošanas matricā (get_role_skip) vāki."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The stack provides on-prem data storage, a local AI-adjacent service, centralized identity, and secure exposure through a reverse proxy. This bundle is a skeleton activation map."
msgstr "Steks nodrošina uz-prem datu glabāšanu, lokālu AI-adjacent servisu, centralizētu identitāti un drošu ekspozīciju caur atpakaļgaitas starpniekserveri. Šis kūlis ir skeleta aktivizācijas karte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The stage a role is invoked in (deepest matching category wins)."
msgstr "Šajā posmā loma tiek minēta (visdziļākās atbilstības kategorijas uzvaras)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The stage runs before the end-to-end tests that read the converged state, and not behind a task a red test aborts. Placed in the destructor stage it ran after the Playwright suite, and `any_errors_fatal` meant any failing role skipped reconciliation entirely, so the suite asserted a state nothing had produced."
msgstr "Posms sākas pirms beigu-to-end testiem, kas lasa konverģētu stāvokli, un nevis aiz uzdevuma sarkanā testa abortus. Izvietots destructor posmā tas skrēja pēc Playwright suite, un `any_errors_fatal` nozīmēja jebkādu neveiksmīgu lomu, pilnībā izlaižot izlīgumu, tāpēc suite apgalvoja, ka valsts nekas nebija radīts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The staging dir exists and contains a non-empty `.env`."
msgstr "Instances mape eksistē un satur ne- tukšumu `.env`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The standard OIDC `sub` claim is permitted as an alternative when the application explicitly requires a UUID-shaped identifier and stores its own mapping table. In that case the role MUST document the deviation in its README."
msgstr "Standarta OIDC `sub` norāde ir atļauta kā alternatīva, ja pieteikumā ir skaidri prasīts UUID formas identifikators un tajā ir sava kartēšanas tabula. Tādā gadījumā lomai jādokumentē novirze tās LASĪTUMĀ."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The steps, and the repos whose manifest could not be read. A repo that cannot state its layout is skipped rather than guessed at, but it must not take the others with it: recovering two repos of three beats recovering none because one manifest is corrupt."
msgstr "Soļi, un repo, kuru manifestu nevarēja lasīt. Repo, kas nevar norādīt savu izkārtojumu, tiek izlaists, nevis uzminēts, bet tas nedrīkst ņemt līdzi pārējos: atgūstot divus repo no trim sitieniem atgūstot nevienu, jo viens manifests ir korumpēts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The stored bearer still authenticates"
msgstr "Saglabātais nesējs joprojām autentificējas"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The subset path fails the run when:"
msgstr "Apakškopas ceļš neizdodas, kad:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The subtree mirrors the host-side `apps/` structure verb by verb and scope by scope:"
msgstr "Apakškoks atspoguļo saimnieka pusiName `apps/` struktūras darbības vārds pēc darbības vārda un darbības jomas pēc darbības jomas:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The subtree splits by user intent (the verb) and scope:"
msgstr "Apakškoku sadala pēc lietotāja nodoma (darbības vārds) un darbības joma:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The suppression is dropped only where it introduces a quote of this module's making. Sphinx carries a source comment into the catalog as a user comment, so a ``nocheck`` standing anywhere else belongs to the message and removing it would let the URL probe loose on the ``msgid``."
msgstr "Apspiešanu nomet tikai tad, ja tā ievieš citātu par šī moduļa izgatavošanu. Sfinx ir avota komentārs katalogā kā lietotāja komentārs, tāpēc ``nocheck`` stāv jebkur citur pieder pie ziņojuma un noņemot to ļautu URL zonde zaudēt uz ``msgid``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The swarm deploy chain across both flavors:"
msgstr "Barm izvietot ķēdi pāri abiem aromatizētājiem:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The swarm path applies the same cut through the `blocked` parameter of `applications_if_group_and_all_deps`; `disable` roles are cut from the dep walk, so orphaned providers never enter the provisioned inventory and `swarm_deploy_targets` (bounded by inventory presence) cannot re-add them."
msgstr "Zvejniecības trajektorija ir vienāda `blocked` parametrs `applications_if_group_and_all_deps`; `disable` lomas tiek pārtrauktas no dep staigāt, tāpēc bāreņu pakalpojumu sniedzējiem nekad ievadīt paredzēto inventāra un `swarm_deploy_targets` (ko ierobežo inventarizācija) nevar tos atkārtoti pievienot."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The swarm-test nfs-server serves shared storage from userspace `nfs-ganesha` (the `ganesha` flavor of `svc-storage-nfs-server`, the default in every runtime), which runs inside the privileged DinD node and never touches the host kernel `nfsd`, so an interrupted export cannot wedge the host. The `kernel` flavor is a per-inventory override for real hosts, where `nfsd` is not shared across clusters. If a swarm step ever hangs at `Reload NFS exports` from a stuck kernel-NFS mount, you MUST recover with `make swarm-clean` on the host (needs sudo): it removes what the docker CLI can, then runs `umount -f -l /var/lib/infinito` + `exportfs -ua` + `systemctl restart docker`. The no-sudo sandbox only prints those commands, so the host recovery is mandatory and the sweep MUST stop until it is done; never fall back to compose-only."
msgstr "Swarm-test nfs-server kalpo dalīta glabāšana no lietotāja vietas `nfs-ganesha` (gads `ganesha` aromāts `svc-storage-nfs-server`, noklusējuma katrā palaisto laiku), kas iet iekšā priviliģēto Dind mezglu un nekad pieskaras saimnieka kodolu `nfsd`, tāpēc pārtraukts eksports nevar ķīļveida saimnieks. E ir o pa s `kernel` aromāts ir per-inventory nomaina reālu saimniekiem, kur `nfsd` netiek dalīta starp kopām. Ja bara solis kādreiz karājas pie `Reload NFS exports` no iestrēdzis kodols-NFS mount, jums ir atgūt ar `make swarm-clean` uz resursdatora (nepieciešams sudo): tas noņem to, ko docker CLI var, tad iet `umount -f -l /var/lib/infinito` + `exportfs -ua` + `systemctl restart docker`. No-sudo smilšu kaste tikai izdrukā šīs komandas, tāpēc host atgūšana ir obligāta, un slaukšanas jāapstājas, līdz tas tiek darīts; nekad atkrist, lai komponēt tikai."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sweep's ordered candidate rows: priority line first, then the regular line, each annotated with the modes it offers and whether it is priority."
msgstr "Slaucīšanas pasūtītās kandidātu rindas: prioritātes līnija vispirms, tad regulārā līnija, katra anotēta ar tās piedāvātajiem režīmiem un vai tā ir prioritāte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sync pass is the whole disaster drill against the host this role deploys on (`BKP_TEST_IS_STACK_HOST`), in one sequence: back up, seed the marker, back up again so the tested generation carries it, take every project down, restore through the recover chain, require the marker and every recorded container back, and finally let the host's own container health service judge."
msgstr "Sinhronizācijas caurlaide ir viss katastrofu treniņš pret saimnieks šī loma izvieto uz (`BKP_TEST_IS_STACK_HOST`), vienā secībā: atpakaļ uz augšu, sēklu marķieri, atpakaļ uz augšu atkal, lai pārbaudītā paaudze nes to, veikt katru projektu uz leju, atjaunot caur atgūšanas ķēdē, pieprasīt marķieri un katru reģistrēto konteineru atpakaļ, un beidzot ļaujiet uzņēmēja paša konteineru veselības dienests tiesnesis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The systemd services installed by `svc.sh` require a host with a real init system. Registration, service install, and service start are skipped when `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true`; the role can be fully deployed in DinD (binary extraction and `.env` file work). The nested `deploy-fresh-purged-apps` call in `test.sh` is also skipped when `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true` — in DinD, `make up` does not start the package-cache proxy (`cache_stack_enabled()` returns false in CI), so apt inside the fresh container cannot resolve the proxy hostname and package installs fail. Structural checks (binary + `.env`) are sufficient proof of a correct deploy in DinD; the full end-to-end deploy only runs on a real host."
msgstr "Sistēmā uzstādītie pakalpojumi `svc.sh` nepieciešama resursdators ar reālu init sistēmu. Reģistrācija, pakalpojumu uzstādīšana, un pakalpojumu sākums tiek izlaists, kad `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true`; lomu var pilnībā izmantot Dind (binārā ekstrakcija un `.env` failu darbs). Ligzda `deploy-fresh-purged-apps` izsaukums `test.sh` tiek izlaists arī tad, ja `DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER=true` — Dindā, `make up` nepalaiž pakotnes- cache starpniekserveri (`cache_stack_enabled()` atgriež Aplams), tāpēc apt iekšpusē svaigajā konteinerā nevar atrisināt starpniekservera datora nosaukumu un pakotne instalēt neizdevās. Strukturālās pārbaudes (binārais + `.env`) ir pietiekams pierādījums pareizai izvietošanai Dind; pilnīga pilnīga izvietošana notiek tikai uz reāla resursdatora."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The table below summarizes common Ansible plugin types and their conventional directory names."
msgstr "Zemāk redzamajā tabulā apkopoti kopīgie Ansible spraudnis veidi un to parastie direktoriju nosaukumi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The table lives in its own ``## Roles Overview 🧩`` section directly above ``## Use it online 🚀`` in the root README.md and is fully regenerated on every run; every other section stays untouched. Rows are the invokable roles, sorted ascending by the Entity column."
msgstr "Galds dzīvo savā ``## Roles Overview 🧩`` Sekcija tieši virs ``## Use it online 🚀`` saknes README.md un ir pilnībā atjaunots katrā braucienā; katrs cits posms paliek neskarts. Rindas ir neatsaucamas lomas, kas sakārtotas pēc Vienības slejas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The target refuses to drop a worktree with uncommitted changes. Show the operator that status and let them decide; only add `force=true` when they explicitly ask for it, because it discards the changes."
msgstr "Mērķis atsakās piliens worktree ar nenodotām izmaiņām. Rādīt operatoram šo statusu un ļaut viņiem izlemt; tikai pievienot `force=true` kad viņi to skaidri pieprasa, jo tas atceļ izmaiņas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The target subtree must already exist; the script refuses to create export subtrees implicitly."
msgstr "Mērķa apakškolai jau jābūt; skripts atsakās netieši izveidot eksporta apakškokus."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The task sits in `tasks/stages/01_constructor.yml` after the `networks`, `design` and `service_provider` merges, after the `add_host` placements and after the token store, so the payload renders with the same `group_names`, `groups` and user records a role would see. Moving it earlier bakes stale values into the play."
msgstr "Uzdevums atrodas `tasks/stages/01_constructor.yml` pēc `networks`, `design` kā arī `service_provider` pēc `add_host` izvietojumi un pēc marķierierīces veikalu, lai derīgo kravu renderē ar to pašu `group_names`, `groups` un lietotājs reģistrē lomu varētu redzēt. Pārceļot to agrāk bakes strupceļā vērtības spēlē."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The template maps the generated palette to semantic variables such as `--color-01-solid-primary`, `--color-01-link-primary`, grayscale steps, and `--color-rgb-01-*`."
msgstr "Sagatave kartē ģenerēto paleti uz semantiskiem mainīgajiem kā `--color-01-solid-primary`, `--color-01-link-primary`, pelēktoņu soļi, un `--color-rgb-01-*`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The tested envelope 🧪"
msgstr "Testētais apvalks 🧪"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The theme MUST be bundled with the source repository (either checked in under ``themes/`` or referenced as a Hugo Module via ``go.mod``). V1 does not support a separate theme override."
msgstr "Tēmai jābūt apvienotai ar avota repozitoriju (vai nu pārbaudīts zem ``themes/`` vai atsaucas kā Hugo Modulis ``go.mod``). V1 neatbalsta atsevišķu tēmas ignorēšanu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The theme MUST be bundled with the source repository (either checked in under `themes/` or referenced as a Hugo Module via `go.mod`). V1 does not support a separate theme override."
msgstr "Tēmai jābūt apvienotai ar avota repozitoriju (vai nu pārbaudīts zem `themes/` vai atsaucas kā Hugo Modulis `go.mod`). V1 neatbalsta atsevišķu tēmas ignorēšanu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The three `API_*_KEY` entries are read as `${{ secrets.X || vars.X }}`, so a secret of the same name wins and the variable is the fallback. Prefer the secret: a repository **variable is not masked**, and the development inventory sets `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS: false`, so a key supplied as a variable can be printed by a task that echoes its own arguments."
msgstr "Trīs `API_*_KEY` ierakstus lasa kā `${{ secrets.X || vars.X }}`, tāpēc paša nosaukuma noslēpums uzvar un mainīgais ir atkāpšanās. Dot priekšroku noslēpumam: repozitorijs **mainīgais nav maskēts**, un attīstības inventarizācijas kopumi `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS: false`, lai atslēgu, kas tiek piegādāta kā mainīgais, var izdrukāt ar uzdevumu, kas atbalso pats savus argumentus."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The three `svc-bkp-*` repository rows come from `backup_repos.repo_placements`. `utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py` calls `backup_repos.backup_provider_ips`, which resolves the same two closures and returns the nodes as IPs, to build `svc-bkp-remote-2-local.services.remote-2-local.backup_providers`."
msgstr "Trīs `svc-bkp-*` Krātuves rindas ir no `backup_repos.repo_placements`. `utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py` zvani `backup_repos.backup_provider_ips`, kas atrisina tos pašus divus slēgšanu un atgriež mezglus kā IP, lai izveidotu `svc-bkp-remote-2-local.services.remote-2-local.backup_providers`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The three candidates that vendor documentation claimed were probed against running instances on 2026-08-27, and each is filed below on what the deployed artefact actually offers rather than on the claim:"
msgstr "Trīs kandidāti, kas pārdevējs dokumentācija apgalvoja, tika zondēts pret darbojas instances 2026-08-27, un katrs ir iesniegts zemāk par to, ko artefakts faktiski piedāvā, nevis par prasību:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The title a role presents itself under."
msgstr "Nosaukumam ir sava nozīme."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The title renders these as glyphs, so recovering one means translating a symbol back into a value; the log holds the word the operator picked. Reading it there keeps the retrigger honest even if the title's marker changes shape."
msgstr "Nosaukums padara tos par glifiem, tāpēc atgūstot viens nozīmē tulkojot simbolu atpakaļ uz vērtību; žurnāls tur vārdu operators izvēlējās. Lasot to tur retrigger godīgi, pat ja nosaukuma marķieris maina formu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The title's priority segment is the cross-check, not the source: it proves a priority line existed even when truncation mangled it, so an empty log read is a broken reader -- expired logs, a moved Inputs block, an inlined orchestrator -- rather than a run dispatched without one."
msgstr "Titula prioritātes segments ir kontrolpārbaude, nevis avots: tas pierāda prioritātes līniju pastāvēja pat tad, kad trancation mangled to, tāpēc tukšs log lasīt ir bojāts lasītājs -- beigušies baļķi, pārvietots Inputs bloks, inlined orķestra, nevis palaist nosūtīti bez viena."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token as an operator would have written it, for error messages."
msgstr "Operatora marķierierīce būtu to uzrakstījusi kļūdu ziņojumiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token can name a row this ranking no longer has -- the role was removed, a variant was dropped, the filters moved. The start is then the first row the source run got green, which lies inside the same window and so never falls behind it. A run with nothing green and an unresolvable token leaves no anchor at all and starts at the head."
msgstr "Žetonu var nosaukt rindu, kurai vairs nav šīs ranga -- loma tika noņemta, variants tika nomests, filtri pārvietoti. Starts ir tad pirmā rinda avots palaist ieguva zaļo, kas atrodas iekšpusē vienā logā un tāpēc nekad nokrīt aiz tā. Skrējiens ar neko zaļu un neatrisināmu marķieri nepavisam neatstāj enkuru un sākas pie galvas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token each entry carries is the one the deployment issued, not the signed-in caller's own, so reaching an MCP tool server is a grant separate from signing in. The env renders `config.access_grants: []`, which `has_connection_access` reads as administrator-only, and [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) then narrows each entry to the serving role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "Katra ieraksta marķierierīce ir tā, kuru izsniedz izvietošana, nevis paša parakstītā zvanītāja, tāpēc sasniedzot MCP rīku serveri ir dotācija atsevišķi no parakstīšanas. Env renderē `config.access_grants: []`, kas `has_connection_access` lasa tikai kā administratoru un [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) pēc tam sašaurina katru ierakstu apkalpojošo lomu `mcp` RBAC grupa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token each entry carries is the one the deployment issued, not the signed-in caller’s own, so reaching an MCP tool server is a grant separate from signing in. The env renders ``config.access_grants: []``, which ``has_connection_access`` reads as administrator-only, and ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ then narrows each entry to the serving role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "Katra ieraksta marķierierīce ir tā, kuru izsniedz izvietošana, nevis paša parakstītā zvanītāja, tādējādi sasniedzot MCP rīku serveri ir dotācija atsevišķi no parakstīšanas. Env renderē ``config.access_grants: []``, kas ``has_connection_access`` lasa tikai kā administratoru un ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ then narrows each entry to the serving role’s ``mcp`` RBAC grupa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token lifetime is bounded to one hour, and a new token is minted on every workflow run."
msgstr "Žetonu kalpošanas laiks ir ierobežots līdz vienai stundai, un katrā darbplūsmas braucienā tiek kalta jauna marķierierīce."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token lives in the store under the user named by the provider's ``mcp.credential.owner``, keyed by the provider's own ``application_id``. Spelling that out at each call site repeated the owner resolution, the two ``.get`` fallbacks and the trim in eighteen places, so a role that read it slightly differently read a different thing."
msgstr "Žetonu dzīvo veikalā zem lietotāja nosaukts pakalpojuma sniedzēja ``mcp.credential.owner``, atslēgta pēc paša pakalpojumu sniedzēja ``application_id``. Pareizrakstība, ka ārā katrā zvanu vietā atkārtoja īpašnieka izšķirtspēju, abi ``.get`` atkāpšanās un apdares astoņpadsmit vietās, tāpēc lomu, kas lasīt to nedaudz atšķirīgi lasīt citu lietu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token owner; tool calls run with that account's Mattermost permissions"
msgstr "Žetonu īpašnieks; rīks zvani palaist ar šo kontu Mattermost atļaujas"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token owner; tool calls run with that account’s Mattermost permissions"
msgstr "Žetonu īpašnieks; rīks zvani palaist ar šo kontu Mattermost atļaujas"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The token store at ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets/tokens.yml`` survives compose+volumes purges. Matrix-deploy variant transitions wipe an app's persistent state but the stale token would otherwise be reused on the next round (for example matomo's API probe in ``sys-front-inj-matomo``, whose token-empty guard never fires while the prior round's token is still present). The purge orchestrator invokes this module to drop the matching ``users.<user>.tokens.<app_id>`` entries alongside the entity-level wipe."
msgstr "Žetonu veikals ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets/tokens.yml`` izdzīvo komponē+tilpumu attīrīšanās. Matrix-deploy variantu pārejas noslauka lietotnes noturīgo stāvokli, bet strupceļš token citādi tiktu atkārtoti nākamajā kārtā (piemēram, tomātu API zonde ``sys-front-inj-matomo``, kura žetonu iztukšošanas aizsargs nekad nedeg, kamēr vēl atrodas iepriekšējās kārtas marķierierīce). Tīrīšanas orķestra atsaucas šo moduli, lai nomestu atbilstības ``users.<user>.tokens.<app_id>`` ieraksti līdzās vienības līmeņa noslaucīt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The top-level `compose.yml` is scoped to **local development and CI testing only**. It MUST NOT be used to deploy or run a live Infinito.Nexus stack. Production deployments MUST go through the Ansible roles and their own rendered compose files under `roles/<role>/templates/`."
msgstr "Augstākais līmenis `compose.yml` ir attiecināts uz **Vietējā attīstība un tikai KI testēšana**. To nedrīkst izmantot, lai izvietotu vai palaist dzīvu Infinito.Nexus kaudze. Ražošanas izvietošanā ir iet caur Assible lomas un viņu pašu renderēta kompose failus zem `roles/<role>/templates/`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The top-level `env` block sets process environment variables for every Claude Code session. It is currently used to disable GPG signing for agent-created commits via the additive `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` mechanism:"
msgstr "Augstākais līmenis `env` bloks nosaka procesa vides mainīgos katram Claude Code seanss. To pašlaik izmanto, lai atspējotu GPG parakstīšanu aģenta radītas saistības, izmantojot piedevu `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` mehānisms:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The top-level node MUST be a YAML list. A non-list root is a hard error."
msgstr "Augšējā līmeņa mezglam jābūt YAML sarakstam. Ne- saraksta sakne ir cieta kļūda."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The trade-off is that `deny` now carries the full weight of \"what the agent must never do from the shell\". New destructive patterns MUST be added to `deny`. They can no longer be caught implicitly by an absent `allow` entry."
msgstr "Kompromiss ir tāds, ka `deny` tagad veic pilnu svaru \"ko aģents nedrīkst darīt no čaulas\". Jauni destruktīvi modeļi jāpievieno `deny`. Tos vairs nevar netieši nozvejot prombūtnē `allow` ierakstu."

