# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "What the source asked for does not enter that decision: the run's own jobs are the evidence. A suite reached on the ``auto`` default is the common case -- ``call-orchestrator.yml`` reads ``auto`` as global scope off the ``whitelist`` alone, so a ``--failed`` retrigger, which puts its selection on ``priority`` and leaves the whitelist empty, would run every green suite again for as long as the retrigger chain lasts."
msgstr "Tas, ko pieprasīja avots, neievada šo lēmumu: paša uzņēmuma darba vietas ir pierādījums. Uz ``auto`` noklusētais ir parastais gadījums -- ``call-orchestrator.yml`` lasītājs ``auto`` tvērumā, ``whitelist`` vienu, tāpēc ``--failed`` retrigger, kas liek savu izvēli ``priority`` un atstāj balto sarakstu tukšs, būtu palaist katru zaļo suite atkal, kamēr retrigger ķēde ilgst."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "What the token narrows, as the key two tokens are equal under."
msgstr "Ko marķieris sašaurina, jo galvenie divi žetoni ir vienādi zem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "What this does:"
msgstr "Ko tas dara:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "What this gives up is the guarantee the pinned form exists for: the combination that failed may not be among the ones the retrigger draws."
msgstr "Tas, ko tas atsakās, ir garantija pinned forma pastāv: kombinācija, kas neizdevās var nebūt starp tiem retrigger vērš."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "What this role does"
msgstr "Kāda ir šī loma"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "What user problem does this solve?"
msgstr "Kādu lietotāja problēmu tas atrisina?"

