# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] **Group mapping (Decision #5)**: the path-to-roles map is persisted (`apply/oidc_settings.py` writes it to `frappe.db.set_default(\"erpnext_oidc_group_role_map\", …)`), but reconciling the map into Frappe roles on each OIDC login still needs a `hooks.py` `on_session_creation` hook in a small custom Frappe app. Deferred to a follow-up requirement; documented in README."
msgstr "[ ] **Grupu kartēšana (Lēmums #5)**: tiek saglabāts ceļš uz lomu karti (`apply/oidc_settings.py` raksta to `frappe.db.set_default(\"erpnext_oidc_group_role_map\", …)`), bet saskaņojot karti uz Frappe lomas katrā OIDC pieteikšanās joprojām ir nepieciešams `hooks.py` `on_session_creation` āķis nelielā pielāgotu Frappe lietotni. Atlikta pēcpārbaudes prasība; dokumentēta LASĪTUMĀ."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] **Iteration loop.** The agent MUST follow the [Compose Loop](../agents/action/iteration/compose.md) for every change inside `roles/svc-swarm-node/`, `roles/svc-prx-openresty/` (swarm-mode adaptations), `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/`, `roles/svc-storage-nfs-client/`, and `roles/web-app-mediawiki/` (pilot). The agent MUST follow the [Workflow Loop](../agents/action/iteration/workflow.md) for every change to `.github/workflows/test-deploy-swarm-nfs.yml`. The agent MUST NOT skip the loop's debug-locally step in favour of remote CI reruns."
msgstr "[ ] **Iterācijas cilpa.** Aģentam [Komponēt cilpu](../agents/action/iteration/compose.md) par katru iekšējo izmaiņu `roles/svc-swarm-node/`, `roles/svc-prx-openresty/` (bara režīma pielāgojumi), `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/`, `roles/svc-storage-nfs-client/`, un `roles/web-app-mediawiki/` (pilots). Pārstāvim ir jāievēro [Darbplūsmas cilpa](../agents/action/iteration/workflow.md) par katru `.github/workflows/test-deploy-swarm-nfs.yml`. Aģents NEDRĪKST izlaist cilpas atkļūdošanas vietējo soli par labu attālās CI atkārtoti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] **Major** - Breaking change"
msgstr "[ ] **Liela apjoma** - Pārmaiņas"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] **Minor** - New backwards-compatible feature"
msgstr "[ ] **Maza apjoma** - Jauna ar atpakaļsaderīga funkcija"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] **No `ask` prompts mid-run.** The agent MUST NOT trigger any tool call that routes through `permissions.ask` in [.claude/settings.json](../../.claude/settings.json) during implementation. Where a tool would otherwise route through `ask`, the agent MUST select an equivalent already covered by `permissions.allow`, or rephrase the operation to fit the sandbox. The single permitted exception is the final commit at the end of the run."
msgstr "[ ] **Nē `ask` uzvedina vidū.** Aģents NEDRĪKST palaist nevienu instrumentu zvanu ka maršruti caur `permissions.ask` skaits [.claude/settings.json](../../.claude/settings.json) īstenošanas laikā. Ja rīks citādi virzītos cauri `ask`, pārstāvim jāizvēlas ekvivalents, uz kuru jau attiecas `permissions.allow`, vai pārfrāzēt darbību, lai ietilptu smilšu kastē. Vienīgais atļautais izņēmums ir galīgais ieguldījums brauciena beigās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] **No interruptions.** Bug fixes, deploy failures, lint failures, `make test` failures, healthcheck flaps, swarm-init flakes, NFS mount races, workflow reruns until green — every issue MUST be resolved at its root inside this same iteration without prompting the operator. Workarounds, ad-hoc skips, retry-until-green loops, or \"track in a follow-up\" deferrals MUST NOT be used."
msgstr "[ ] **Nekādu pārtraukumu.** Kļūdu labojumi, dislocēt kļūmes, lint neveiksmes, `make test` neveiksmes, veselības pārbaudes atloki, swarm-init pārslas, NFS mount rases, darbplūsmas atsākas līdz zaļa — katrs jautājums ir jārisina pie tās pašas saknes iekšpusē inteerācija, nerosinot operatoru. lidojuma trajektorijas, ad-hoc izlaistāji, retriting-līdz-green cilpas, vai \"turpmākie pasākumi\" atlikšanu NEDRĪKST izmantot."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] **One commit at the end.** ALL changes (role, meta, Playwright spec, documentation, marketplace entry, and the ticked checkboxes in this document) MUST be combined into ONE commit, created only after every Acceptance Criterion above is checked off (`- [x]`) and `make test` is green. The agent MUST NOT push; the operator runs `git-sign-push` outside the sandbox per [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)."
msgstr "[ ] **Viens izdarīt beigās.** VISAS izmaiņas (loma, meta, Playwright spec, dokumentācija, tirgus ieraksts, un atzīmēti rūtiņas šajā dokumentā) Jākombinē vienā solījumā, kas izveidots tikai pēc katra iepriekš minētā pieņemšanas kritērija pārbaudes (`- [x]`) kā arī `make test` zaļš. Aģents NEDRĪKST stumt; operators darbojas `git-sign-push` ārpus smilšu kastes [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] **One commit at the end.** The agent MUST NOT create any intermediate commit. ALL changes (the three new roles, the openresty swarm-mode adaptations, the pilot role updates, the CI workflow, schema entries, group_vars defaults, documentation, and the ticked checkboxes in this document) MUST be combined into ONE commit, created only after every Acceptance Criterion above is checked off (`- [x]`), `make test` is green, and `.github/workflows/test-deploy-swarm-nfs.yml` is green on its first scheduled run. Per-step commits, checkpoint commits, and partial commits MUST NOT be created. The agent MUST NOT push; the operator runs `git-sign-push` outside the sandbox per [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)."
msgstr "[ ] **Viens izdarīt beigās.** Aģents NEDRĪKST radīt starpposma apņemšanos. VISAS izmaiņas (trīs jaunās lomas – akseleratora baroka režīma pielāgojumi, pilota lomu atjauninājumi, CI darbplūsma, shēmas ieraksti, group_vars noklusētās, dokumentācijas un atzīmētās rūtiņas šajā dokumentā) Jākombinē vienā solījumā, kas izveidots tikai pēc katra iepriekš minētā pieņemšanas kritērija pārbaudes (`- [x]`), `make test` ir zaļa un `.github/workflows/test-deploy-swarm-nfs.yml` ir zaļa savā pirmajā plānotajā skrējienā. Katrā posmā saistības, kontrolpunkts saistības, un daļējas saistības NEDRĪKST izveidot. Aģents NEDRĪKST stumt; operators darbojas `git-sign-push` ārpus smilšu kastes [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] **Patch** - Small improvement or compatible adjustment"
msgstr "[ ] **Ielāps** - Nelieli uzlabojumi vai savietojami pielāgojumi"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] **🪙 (commercial) cells are opt-in**: they are declared in `meta/addons/` but remain disabled, and the role README documents the required commercial tier; they are NOT enabled by default and do not block the requirement."
msgstr "[ ] **🪙 (komerciāla) šūnas ir izvēles**: tos deklarē `meta/addons/` bet paliek atspējots, un loma REASTME dokumentus nepieciešamo komerciālo līmeni; tie nav iespējoti pēc noklusējuma un nav bloķēt prasību."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A Playwright OIDC flow (biber + administrator) clicks \"Sign in with Keycloak\", completes the Keycloak chain, and lands on an authenticated Semaphore surface (administrator persona additionally asserts the admin-only `/users` surface)."
msgstr "[ ] Atskaņojams OIDC plūsma (biber + administrators) klikšķi \"Pierakstīties ar Keycloak\", papildina Keycloak ķēdes, un nolaižas uz autentificētas Semaphore virsmas (administrators persona papildus apgalvo tikai admin `/users` virsma)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A Playwright OIDC flow (biber + administrator) passes the oauth2-proxy → Keycloak chain and lands authenticated in the Checkmk GUI (administrator additionally reaches a Setup/admin-only surface)."
msgstr "[ ] Atskaņojams OIDC plūsma (biber + administrators) iet caur auzu2-proksi → Keycloak ķēdes un zemes autentificēšana Checkmk Saskarne (administrators papildus sasniedz Setup / Admin tikai virsmu)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A Playwright spec against a `<sub>.<node>.onion` surface passes through the Tor SOCKS proxy on an onion node; clearnet targets are unaffected."
msgstr "[ ] Playwright spec pret `<sub>.<node>.onion` virsma iet caur Tor SOCKS starpniekserveri sīpola mezglā; cleannet mērķi netiek ietekmēti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A Playwright spec verifies that selecting `auto` in Open WebUI returns an answer."
msgstr "[ ] Playwright spec pārliecinās, ka izvēloties `auto` skaits Open WebUI atgriež atbildi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A `svc-ai-robot` role deploys `web-app-hermes` in privileged embodied mode on a dedicated device and it comes up healthy. **Blocked:** see [Hardware blockers](#hardware-blockers)."
msgstr "[ ] A `svc-ai-robot` loma izvietošanā `web-app-hermes` priviliģētā iemiesota režīmā uz veltītas ierīces, un tas nāk klajā veselīgi. **Bloķēts:** skatīt [Aparatūras blokatori](#hardware-blockers)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A `web-app-openclaw` role deploys OpenClaw and it comes up healthy with at least one connected interface."
msgstr "[ ] A `web-app-openclaw` loma izvietošanā OpenClaw un tas nāk klajā veselīgi ar vismaz vienu savienots interfeiss."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A bridge component exists, gated on both `web-app-atmo` and `web-app-mobilizon` being in `group_names`; absent either, it is not scheduled and the deploy still succeeds."
msgstr "[ ] Pastāv tilta komponents, kas izvietots uz abiem `web-app-atmo` kā arī `web-app-mobilizon` kas atrodas `group_names`; prombūtnē vai nu, tas nav plānots, un izvietošana joprojām izdodas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A created event is visible in the atmo appview after firehose/aggregator catch-up."
msgstr "[ ] Izveidots notikums ir redzams atmo apskatā pēc firehose/agregator catch-up."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A deployment with one MCP server role and one MCP client role executes a deterministic real tool call through the client. Rendering configuration or listing a server does not satisfy this criterion."
msgstr "[ ] Izvietošana ar vienu MCP servera lomu un vienu MCP klienta lomu izpilda deterministisku reālu rīka zvanu caur klientu. Renderēšanas konfigurācija vai servera uzskaitīšana neatbilst šim kritērijam."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A deterministic audit command or test enumerates every role under `roles/` and classifies addon support by `mechanism` (`addon`, `plugin`, `mu_plugin`, `extension`, `module`, `bridge`), `db-extension` (out of scope), or `none`."
msgstr "[ ] Deterministiskā audita komanda vai tests uzskaita katru lomu zem `roles/` un klasificē addon atbalstu ar `mechanism` (`addon`, `plugin`, `mu_plugin`, `extension`, `module`, `bridge`), `db-extension` (ārpus darbības jomas), vai `none`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A grep `process.env\\.BIBER_(USERNAME|PASSWORD)` over the role tree MUST return at least one hit for every in-scope role above once the audit closes its checkbox."
msgstr "[ ] A grep `process.env\\.BIBER_(USERNAME|PASSWORD)` par lomu koks MUST atgriezties vismaz vienu hit par katru in-scope lomu iepriekš, kad audits slēdz savu rūtiņu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A grep `process.env\\.LDAP_SERVICE_ENABLED` over the spec tree (excluding `roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/service-gating.js`) MUST return zero hits, proving every spec routes its LDAP gate through the helper rather than reading the flag directly."
msgstr "[ ] A grep `process.env\\.LDAP_SERVICE_ENABLED` virs speckoka (izņemot `roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/service-gating.js`) Jāatgriežas nulles hits, pierādot katru spec maršrutu tās LDAP vārtiem caur palīgu, nevis lasot karogu tieši."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A grep for `mcp` before implementation is recorded in the implementing PR to show the baseline was empty."
msgstr "[ ] A grep priekš `mcp` pirms īstenošana ir reģistrēta īstenošanas PR, lai parādītu, ka bāzlīnija ir tukša."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A grep for `meta/addons/` before implementation is recorded in the implementing PR to show the baseline was empty."
msgstr "[ ] A grep priekš `meta/addons/` pirms īstenošana ir reģistrēta īstenošanas PR, lai parādītu, ka bāzlīnija ir tukša."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[ ] A per-role upstream-plugin survey is completed for **every** `web-app-*` role, not only the integration hubs, so the ✅/🪙 layer is exhaustive rather than hub-biased. Each survey records, per partner role, the real upstream plugin (or its documented absence) with a source URL; the MediaWiki survey (which surfaced `DiscourseSsoConsumer`, `PeerTubeEmbed`, `MachineTranslation`→libretranslate, `Extension:AWS`→minio, an LLM editor→openwebui) is the template for depth."
msgstr "[ ] Ir pabeigta augšpusējā posma plugin apsekošana attiecībā uz **katru** `web-app-*` loma, ne tikai integrācijas centri, tāpēc ✅/🪙 slānis ir izsmeļošs, nevis objektīvs. Katrs apsekojums ieraksti, pa partnera lomu, reālā augšpusē spraudnis (vai tā dokumentēta neesamība) ar avota URL; MediaWiki apsekojums (kura virsma `DiscourseSsoConsumer`, `PeerTubeEmbed`, `MachineTranslation`→libretranslate, `Extension:AWS`→minio, LLM redaktors→openwebui) ir dziļuma veidne."

