# translation-refused: libretranslate protected-span lost=[] gained=['*']
# nocheck: url
# translation-rejected: [x] [web-app-odoo](../../roles/web-app-odoo/) tiek
msgid "[x] [web-app-odoo](../../roles/web-app-odoo/) is audited for a maintained MCP add-on and is integrated only after the add-on's update cadence, license, authentication, and tool scope are documented. The audit was carried out and its outcome is that no add-on qualifies, so the role ships no MCP surface. Odoo SA publishes none, and a search of the OCA organisation returns zero MCP repositories, so no vendor-backed or community-governed option exists. The leading third party is [`ivnvxd/mcp-server-odoo`](https://github.com/ivnvxd/mcp-server-odoo). **Cadence:** active, `v0.8.0` on 2026-08-26 after `v0.7.1`, `v0.7.0`, `v0.6.0` and `v0.5.2` since 2026-04. **Licence:** MPL-2.0. **Authentication:** an Odoo API key or a username and password, over XML-RPC. **Tool scope:** mutating by design, advertised as create, update and manage, against the read-only default this project requires of every surface. Three findings disqualify it rather than the licence or the cadence. Its contributor list is 197 of 231 commits from one author with no organisational backing, so a single maintainer holds an ERP-wide data path. Its production access control lives in a second module distributed through the Odoo Apps store rather than a pinnable source tag, which the source-pinning rule cannot accommodate. Its module-free fallback is labelled upstream as YOLO mode for development and testing only. The role therefore stays blocked under `unreviewed_third_party`, and re-review is warranted if Odoo SA or the OCA publishes a server."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] [web-app-openproject](../../roles/web-app-openproject/) carries the `licence-gated` classification with its blocker recorded, because the MCP server ships only in the Enterprise edition while this role deploys Community. It is integrated, with the `/mcp` endpoint behind the role's existing auth model, only once an Enterprise token is an operator-supplied precondition."
msgstr "[x] [web-app-openproject](../../roles/web-app-openproject/) nes `licence-gated` klasifikācija ar tās bloķētājs reģistrēts, jo MCP servera kuģi tikai Enterprise izdevumā, kamēr šī loma izvieto Kopienu. Tas ir integrēts ar `/mcp` rezultāts aiz lomas esošo auth modeli, tikai tad, kad uzņēmums marķieris ir operatora nodrošināts priekšnoteikums."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] [web-app-openwebui](../../roles/web-app-openwebui/) registers only compatible authorized servers, applies exact application-group grants, and restores connection state and grants after restart with `ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false`. `mcp_tool_server_connections` drops a server whose auth is neither delegated nor bearer-presentable, emits exactly one `group`/`read` grant naming the provider's own Open WebUI group id, and enables the entry only when that id is known — so the env the container restarts from carries the grant rather than waiting for the next deploy."
msgstr "[x] [web-app-openwebui](../../roles/web-app-openwebui/) reģistrē tikai savietojamus autorizētus serverus, piemēro precīzu pieteikumu grupas dotācijas, un atjauno savienojuma valsts un dotācijas pēc restart ar `ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false`. `mcp_tool_server_connections` piliens serveri, kura auth ir ne deleģēta, ne uzrādītāja reprezentējams, izstaro tieši vienu `group`/`read` dotācijas nosaukšanu pakalpojumu sniedzēja paša Open WebUI grupa id, un ļauj ierakstu tikai tad, kad šis id ir zināms – tāpēc env konteiners atsākas no nes dotāciju, nevis gaida nākamo izvietojumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] [web-app-wordpress](../../roles/web-app-wordpress/) is audited for a maintained MCP plugin and is integrated only after the plugin's update cadence, license, authentication, and tool scope are documented. The plugin is [WordPress/mcp-adapter](https://github.com/WordPress/mcp-adapter), which bridges the Abilities API to MCP. **Maintained:** owned by the WordPress organisation, not archived, last pushed 2026-08-28. **Cadence:** eight releases between 2025-08-14 and 2026-08-13; the role pins `v0.5.0` (2026-04-15) while `v0.6.1` is current, so the pin trails by two minor versions and is the first thing to revisit. **Licence:** GPL-2.0. **Authentication:** a WordPress application password held in the token store, behind `is_user_logged_in()` and a per-ability permission callback. **Tool scope:** the role registers three read abilities of its own — `infinito/search-posts`, `infinito/get-post`, `infinito/list-categories` — rather than exposing core or third-party abilities, and `files/playwright/addons/infinito-mcp-abilities.spec.js` asserts that exactly those are reachable and that an anonymous `tools/list` is refused. The surface ships `enabled: false`, so it is an operator opt-in."
msgstr "[x] [web-app-wordpress](../../roles/web-app-wordpress/) ir auditēts par uzturētu MCP spraudnis un ir integrēta tikai pēc tam, kad spraudnis atjauninājumu cadence, licence, autentifikācija, un rīku darbības joma ir dokumentēti. Spraudnis ir [WordPress/mcp-adapters](https://github.com/WordPress/mcp-adapter), kas savieno iespējas API uz MCP. **Uzturēts:** kas pieder WordPress organizācija, nav arhivēta, pēdējo reizi grūsta 2026-08-28. **Kadence:** astoņas noplūdes starp 2025-08-14 kā arī 2026-08-13; lomu tapas `v0.5.0` (2026-04-15) kamēr `v0.6.1` ir pašreizējais, tāpēc pin pēdas ar divām nelielām versijām un ir pirmā lieta, kas jāpārskata. **Licence:** GPL2.0. **Autentificēšana:** a WordPress pieteikuma paroli tur marķieru veikalā, aiz `is_user_logged_in()` un tiesības atļaujas atsaukšana. **Rīku tvērums:** funkcijas reģistrē trīs lasīt spējas savas – `infinito/search-posts`, `infinito/get-post`, `infinito/list-categories` — tā vietā, lai atklātu galvenās vai trešās puses spējas, un `files/playwright/addons/infinito-mcp-abilities.spec.js` apgalvo, ka tieši tie ir sasniedzami un ka anonīms `tools/list` tiek atteikta. Virszemes kuģi `enabled: false`, tāpēc tas ir operators izvēles ."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `--help` documents every parameter above, including the default value of the output stream file, in the same style as [cli/administration/deploy/dedicated/command.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/runner/command.py)."
msgstr "[x] `--help` dokumentus katru parametru iepriekš, ieskaitot noklusējuma vērtību izejas plūsmas failu, tādā pašā stilā kā [cli/administration/deploy/dedicated/command.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/runner/command.py)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `README.md` documents the static-seal model and its trust assumption, the bootstrap and root-token revocation flow, the RBAC mapping, the PKI flag, the backup/restore procedure including the seal-key caveat, and the CLI-OIDC-login limitation from Decision #10. It additionally records two traps found during implementation: the `/openbao/file` ownership requirement and why `vault_core_unsealed` must not be used for alerting."
msgstr "[x] `README.md` dokumentē statisko zīmoga modeli un tā uzticamības pieņēmumu, bootstrap un root-token atsaukšanas plūsmu, RBAC kartēšanu, PKI karogu, dublēšanas/atjaunošanas procedūru, tostarp plombas atslēgas kaverversiju, un CLI-OIDC žurnalēšanas ierobežojumu saskaņā ar Lēmumu #10. Tā papildus reģistrē divus slazdus, kas atrasti īstenošanas laikā: `/openbao/file` Īpašumtiesību prasība un kāpēc `vault_core_unsealed` Nedrīkst izmantot brīdināšanai."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `apply/api_bot.py` sets `setup_complete=1` on the `System Settings` doctype + writes the global default; verified in matrix r3."
msgstr "[x] `apply/api_bot.py` komplekti `setup_complete=1` par `System Settings` doctype + raksta globālo noklusējuma; pārbaudīts matricā r3."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `auth/oidc/config` is written from `OIDC.CLIENT.*` values only — no hardcoded realm name, issuer URL, endpoint or claim string anywhere in the role."
msgstr "[x] `auth/oidc/config` ir rakstīts no `OIDC.CLIENT.*` tikai vērtības – nav hardcoded realm nosaukuma, emitenta URL, beigu punkts vai prasību virkne jebkur lomu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `auth: oidc` is rejected by static client renderers until a real acquisition, refresh, audience, expiry, and revocation flow is implemented and tested."
msgstr "[x] `auth: oidc` noraida statiskie klientu renderētāji, līdz tiek īstenota un pārbaudīta reāla iegāde, atsvaidzināšana, auditorija, derīguma termiņš un atsaukšanas plūsma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `auth_subject` is validated against the identity actually provisioned in the provider and is not documentation-only."
msgstr "[x] `auth_subject` ir validēts attiecībā pret identitāti, kas faktiski norādīta pakalpojumu sniedzējā, un nav tikai dokumentācija."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `bench install-app erpnext` runs as part of `bench new-site --install-app erpnext` in `tasks/03_bench_bootstrap.yml`; the long-lived Frappe containers are restarted afterwards so their cached app set picks up the new install (otherwise `/login` serves HTTP 500 from a stale app cache)."
msgstr "[x] `bench install-app erpnext` darbojas kā daļa no `bench new-site --install-app erpnext` skaits `tasks/03_bench_bootstrap.yml`; ilgi mūžs Frappe konteineri tiek restartēts pēc tam, lai to kešatmiņas app iestatīts paceļ jauno instalēt (citādi `/login` apkalpo HTTP 500 no strupas programmas kešatmiņas)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `cluster_addr` renders identically in both modes and is not derived from the container name (see the [listener/seal schema note](#templatesopenbaohclj2-shape)). Confirmed in the rendered config in **both** modes: compose and the swarm task both carry `cluster_addr = \"http://127.0.0.1:8201\"`, with raft `path = /openbao/file` and `node_id = openbao-1`."
msgstr "[x] `cluster_addr` atveido vienādi abos režīmos un nav atvasināts no konteinera nosaukuma (skatīt [klausītāja/zīmoga shēmas piezīme](#templatesopenbaohclj2-shape)). Apstiprināts renderēta konfigurācija in **abi** režīmi: komponēt un spodrināt uzdevumu gan veikt `cluster_addr = \"http://127.0.0.1:8201\"`, ar plostu `path = /openbao/file` kā arī `node_id = openbao-1`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `deploy.replicas` defaults to `len(groups[application_id])` so the swarm scheduler is told how many replicas the inventory declares. A per-service `replicas` field in `meta/services.yml` overrides that for cases where the operator wants a different replica count than the host count."
msgstr "[x] `deploy.replicas` noklusētais `len(groups[application_id])` Tātad bara plānotājam ir pateikts, cik kopijas inventāra deklarē. A pakalpojums `replicas` lauks `meta/services.yml` aizstāj tos gadījumus, kad operators vēlas, lai viņu skaits būtu citāds nekā uzņēmējam."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `deploy.update_config` is taken from a per-role variable with documented defaults `parallelism: 1`, `delay: 10s`."
msgstr "[x] `deploy.update_config` ir ņemts no per-roll mainīgajiem ar dokumentētiem noklusējumiem `parallelism: 1`, `delay: 10s`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `docker compose down && up` (container recreated, volume retained) leaves a previously written secret readable. Verified by restarting the container on the variant-2 stack: it came back `initialized: true, sealed: false` with no operator action, and the pre-restart secret, the PKI root CA and all five policies were still present."
msgstr "[x] `docker compose down && up` (konteiners pārbūvēts, saglabātais tilpums) atstāj iepriekš uzrakstītu slepenu lasāmu. Pārbauda, atkārtoti iedarbinot konteineru uz variantu-2 kaudze: tas atgriezās `initialized: true, sealed: false` bez operatora darbības un pirmsrestarta noslēpums, PKI saknes CA un visas piecas politikas joprojām bija klāt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `docs/requirements/027-integration-matrix.md` lists the AI surface of every role in the confirmed table."
msgstr "[x] `docs/requirements/027-integration-matrix.md` uzskaita MI virsmu katrai lomai apstiprinātajā tabulā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `git grep` finds no root token, recovery key or seal key value in the repository."
msgstr "[x] `git grep` repozitorijā neatrod saknes marķieri, atgūšanas atslēgu vai zīmoga atslēgu vērtību."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `implementation: sidecar` or `external` MCP containers attach to the role's existing `networks.local` subnet and add no new top-level network."
msgstr "[x] `implementation: sidecar` vai `external` MCP konteineri papildina lomu esošo `networks.local` apakštīkls un nepievieno jaunu augstākā līmeņa tīklu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `logout_i18n.yml` holds only the English source strings, and the logout panel reads every other language from `core.po`."
msgstr "[x] `logout_i18n.yml` tur tikai angļu avota stīgas, un pieteikšanās panelis lasa katru citu valodu no `core.po`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `make compose-playwright role=web-app-openbao` exits 0 with no stub tests and a clean logged-out final state. Latest deploy run: **13 passed, 2 skipped, 0 failed (30.8 s)**, no retries."
msgstr "[x] `make compose-playwright role=web-app-openbao` izejas 0 bez kurtuļa testiem un tīra pieteicies-out gala stāvoklī. Pēdējā izvietošana: **13 pagājis, 2 izlaists, 0 neizdevās (30.8 s)**Nav retumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `make i18n-extract` writes `locale/<code>/LC_MESSAGES/core.po` for all 183 non-English languages, holding every role description, category title and description, dashboard menu label and logout panel string under the `msgctxt` of its source."
msgstr "[x] `make i18n-extract` raksta `locale/<code>/LC_MESSAGES/core.po` visiem 183 ne-Angļu valodās, turot katru lomu aprakstu, kategorijas nosaukumu un aprakstu, paneļa izvēlnes etiķeti un pieteikšanās paneļa virkne zem `msgctxt` no tā avota."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `make i18n-extract` writes `locale/<code>/LC_MESSAGES/docs.po` for every language LibreTranslate supports, holding the messages of the Sphinx `gettext` build of the documentation."
msgstr "[x] `make i18n-extract` raksta `locale/<code>/LC_MESSAGES/docs.po` katrai valodai LibreTranslate atbalsta, turot Sfinx ziņojumus `gettext` dokumentācijas izstrāde."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `make i18n-translate domain=<domain> languages=<codes>` translates only the listed languages."
msgstr "[x] `make i18n-translate domain=<domain> languages=<codes>` tulko tikai uzskaitītas valodas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `make i18n-translate domain=core` starts a LibreTranslate container with the image and version of `roles/web-svc-libretranslate/meta/services.yml`, and no container of it remains after the target ends, on success and on failure."
msgstr "[x] `make i18n-translate domain=core` sākas a LibreTranslate konteiners ar `roles/web-svc-libretranslate/meta/services.yml`, un neviens konteiners no tā paliek pēc mērķa beigām, par panākumiem un neveiksmes."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] `make test` is green tree-wide (the role passes role-meta lints, services contract lints, playwright-services-parity lints, and the new `test_task_name_length` lint that caps Ansible `name:` strings at 120 chars)."
