msgstr "```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``sso.enabled``, ``logout.enabled`` and ``email.enabled`` to ``false``; the role serves a static single-page wheel with no accounts and no auth layer. There is nothing for the ``biber`` or ``administrator`` persona to log in to, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona un sākotnēji sasniedzami apgalvojumi darbojas bez nosacījumiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``sso.enabled``, ``logout.enabled`` and ``redis.enabled`` to ``false``; the upstream image is a client-side QR generator with no accounts and no server-side session. There is nothing for the ``biber`` or ``administrator`` persona to log in to, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline reachability assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``sso.enabled``, ``logout.enabled`` and ``redis.enabled`` to ``false``; the upstream image is a client-side QR generator with no accounts and no server-side session. There is nothing for the ``biber`` or ``administrator`` persona to log in to, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona un sākotnēji sasniedzami apgalvojumi darbojas bez nosacījumiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```svc-ai-litellm`` <../svc-ai-litellm/>`__ publishes one routing alias. When this service is deployed, the gateway’s pre-call hook asks it which of the eligible models should answer, passing the prompt as the state and the surviving aliases as the options of a single ``choice`` question. ``services.litellm.router.strategy`` follows ``services.s1.enabled``, so deploying this role is what switches the gateway from a weighted score to a System One decision."
msgstr "```svc-ai-litellm`` <../svc-ai-litellm/>`__ publishes one routing alias. When this service is deployed, the gateway’s pre-call hook asks it which of the eligible models should answer, passing the prompt as the state and the surviving aliases as the options of a single ``choice`` question. ``services.litellm.router.strategy`` follows ``services.s1.enabled``, tā izvietojot šo lomu, ir tas, kas pārslēdz vārteju no svērtu rezultātu uz System One lēmumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/01_admin.yml`` <./tasks/01_admin.yml>`__ provisions only the administrator in Shopware’s user table. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``services.sso.flavor: oidc``, so no oauth2-proxy fronts the role and the storefront carries no authenticated surface at all; the Keycloak login provider that ```tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` <./tasks/setup/oidc.yml>`__ configures covers the administration backend alone. ``biber`` therefore has no account in any matrix variant and ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` unconditionally."
msgstr "```tasks/01_admin.yml`` <./tasks/01_admin.yml>`__ provisions only the administrator in Shopware’s user table. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``services.sso.flavor: oidc``, so no oauth2-proxy fronts the role and the storefront carries no authenticated surface at all; the Keycloak login provider that ```tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` <./tasks/setup/oidc.yml>`__ configures covers the administration backend alone. ``biber`` therefore has no account in any matrix variant and ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` bez nosacījumiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` un darbojas katrā variantā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>`__) drives the same admin journey and skips on the same flag."
msgstr "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>` ) vada to pašu admin braucienu un izlaiž ar vienu karogu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` and asserts the provider, the base URL and the model, so an unconfigured surface cannot reach a green deploy."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` un aizstāv pakalpojumu sniedzēju, bāzes URL un modeli, tāpēc nekonfigurēta virsma nevar sasniegt zaļo izvietojumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, unusable password) plus its own workspace, and binds the endpoint to that pair."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, nelietojama parole) plus savu darba vietu, un saista galapunktu ar šo pāri."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona un bāzes apgalvojumi darbojas bez nosacījumiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` un darbojas katrā variantā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` in every matrix variant, because the shared persona helper cannot drive this role’s sign-in in any of them. Three independent reasons, each sufficient on its own:"
msgstr "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` katrā matrices variantā, jo dalītais persona palīgs nevar vadīt šīs lomas pierakstīšanos nevienā no tiem. Trīs neatkarīgi iemesli, katrs atsevišķi pietiekami:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``adapter``:         immutable source contract of a repository-owned adapter. ``category_allowlist`` suits an upstream that switches whole categories and offers no per-tool filter, where a tool allowlist would be unenforceable; ``mcp_passthrough`` fronts an upstream that already speaks MCP instead of translating REST. ``upstream_path`` names that upstream where it lives on the application's own vhost, so the proxy can hide it: reaching it directly walks past the allowlist the adapter exists to enforce. A provider whose upstream is a separate sidecar declares ``upstream_network`` instead and has nothing to hide there."
msgstr "``adapter``: nemaināms avota līgums par repozitorijam piederošu adapteri. ``category_allowlist`` atbilst augšpusējai iekārtai, kas pārslēdz veselas kategorijas un nepiedāvā vienu instrumentu filtru, ja rīku saraksts nebūtu izpildāms; ``mcp_passthrough`` priekšā augšpusē, kas jau runā MCP, nevis tulko REST. ``upstream_path`` norāda, ka augšpus, kur tas dzīvo uz pieteikuma paša vhost, lai starpniekserveris var slēpt to: sasniedzot to tieši iet garām letlist adapteris pastāv, lai īstenotu. Pakalpojumu sniedzējs, kura augšpuse ir atsevišķs blakusvāģis, paziņo ``upstream_network`` vietā un nav nekā slēpjot tur."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``aliases``: list of DNS aliases. Default: ``[entity_name]`` for shared_net, ``[]`` for default_net"
msgstr "``aliases``: DNS segvārdu saraksts. Noklusētais: ``[entity_name]`` aizstāj shared_net, ``[]`` aizstāj default_net"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``allowed`` (default ``True``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MAY be present for a role of this type. Set ``allowed: False`` to forbid the file/entry on roles of this type so the lint layer can surface the offence with a precise reason."
msgstr "``allowed`` (noklusētais ``True``): datne (vai punktētā ceļa ieraksts) VAR būt klāt šāda veida lomu. Komplekts ``allowed: False`` aizliegt datni/ierakstu par šāda veida lomām, lai linta slānis varētu nosegt pārkāpumu ar precīzu iemeslu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible_facts`` only carries ``docker0`` once the daemon has run, and the daemon config is written before that on a fresh node - facts are gathered at play start, and nothing re-gathers them after the install. Reading the fact alone therefore yields nothing on the very run that has to emit the address, which leaves the inner containers pointed at the clearnet resolver and the DinD DNS check failing on a domain only the node dnsmasq knows."
msgstr "``ansible_facts`` tikai nes ``docker0`` kad dēmons ir palaista, un dēmona konfigurācija ir rakstīts pirms ka uz svaigu mezglu - fakti tiek savākti play sākumā, un nekas atkārtoti vāc tos pēc instalēšanas. Lasot faktu vien tāpēc nes neko par pašu palaist, kas ir, lai emitētu adresi, kas atstāj iekšējo konteineru norādīja uz cleannet resolutioner un Dind DNS pārbaudīt nespēju uz domēna tikai mezgla dnsmasq zina."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default)"
msgstr "``ansible`` (noklusētais)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default) wraps `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD runs ~70 upstream sub-roles to deliver Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Element Call, and Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, and disables MDAD’s bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis so the central Infinito services back the stack."
msgstr "``ansible`` (noklusētais) iesaiņojumi `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD darbojas ~70 augšpusē apakšroles piegādāt Synapse, Element, katrs atbalstīts tilts, Element Call, un Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus adatas MDAD ar nodevumu, padara MDAD inventāru no ``services.matrix.*`` pogas, un atspējo MAD bind Traefik / Postgres / Redis Tātad centrālais Infinito pakalpojumi atpakaļ steku."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` is the public S3 endpoint and is reachable without SSO gating."
msgstr "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` ir publiska3 ir sasniedzams bez SSO gabīšanās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` is read from the play variables unless given as ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` names the block instead of ``ports``, for Discourse's launcher file, whose ``expose:`` list is what becomes ``docker run -p`` there."
msgstr "``application_id`` tiek lasīta no atskaņošanas mainīgajiem, ja vien nav norādīts kā ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` norāda bloku, nevis ``ports``, Discourseir palaišanas fails, kura ``expose:`` saraksts ir kas kļūst ``docker run -p`` Tur."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` of the client doing the discovery."
msgstr "``application_id`` no klienta, kas veic atklājumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant tvērums žetonu uz kontu, kas kaltas to. Šī izvietošana kaļ to administratoram, tāpēc pienāk zvans kā administrators, kurš jautāja klientam. Elementu riska darījums joprojām ierobežo sasniegto. Getting uz rīku serveri ir gated par lomu s ``mcp`` RBAC grupa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost ierobežo zvanu konta žetonu pieder. Šī izvietošana naudas kaltuves, ka personīgo piekļuvi žetonu administratora konta, tāpēc zvani ierodas ar šī konta tiesības, kurš lūdza. Sasniedzot rīku serveri ir gated par lomu s ``mcp`` RBAC grupa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: API marķierierīce tiek izsniegta pret administratora kontu, tāpēc katrs zvans ietver šī konta tiesības neatkarīgi no tā, kurš lūdza klientam. Sasniedzot rīku serveri ir gated par lomu s ``mcp`` RBAC grupa, kas ir atsevišķa dotācija no administrēšanas Jenkins."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: personīgā pieeja žetonu kaļ pret ``root`` konts un glabājas zem ``administrator`` atslēga, tāpēc katrs zvans ietver šī konta tiesības neatkarīgi no tā, kurš lūdza klientam. Sasniedzot rīku serveri ir gated par lomu s ``mcp`` RBAC grupa, kas ir atsevišķa dotācija no administrēšanas GitLab."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: tīmekļa pakalpojuma marķierierīce tiek izdota pret administratora kontu, tāpēc zvans nes šī konta tiesības neatkarīgi no tā, kurš lūdza klientam. Pievienotās funkcijas ir tikai lasāms, kas ierobežo to, ko šīs tiesības var darīt šeit. Sasniedzot rīku serveri ir gated par lomu s ``mcp`` RBAC grupa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Zvans ierodas Baserow kā galapunkta īpašnieks neatkarīgi no tā, kurš lūdza klientam, un sasniedz tikai vienu darba vietu, kas pieder šim kontam. Tas ir otrais saistīts zem adaptera letlist, nevis aizstāt to."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC grupa, kas ir atsevišķa dotācija no līdzdalības Nextcloud kontu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject``:    identity MCP calls execute as. ``user`` and ``oidc`` additionally require a ``delegation`` block, because a rendered deployment bearer is a service account no matter what the metadata claims."
msgstr "``auth_subject``: identitātes MCP zvanus izpildīt kā. ``user`` kā arī ``oidc`` nepieciešama ``delegation`` bloķēt, jo sniegtais izvietošanas uzrādītājs ir pakalpojumu konts neatkarīgi no tā, ko metadati apgalvo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_type: bearer`` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "``auth_type: bearer`` ar marķierierīci no meklēšanas datiem"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth``:            authentication scheme guarding the endpoint."
msgstr "``auth``: autentifikācijas shēma, kas aizsargā galapunktu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auto`` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the ``.baudolo-*`` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "``auto`` ir padomdevēja un nekad neizdodas vienība — katrs atteikums ir pieteicies uz žurnālu kā ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, tāpēc pārbaudiet tur, ja resursdators jūs gaidāt momentuzņēmumu nav. A norādīts ``btrfs``/``zfs`` neizpilda vienības vietā, kas ir punkts, norādot to. Pirms katra momentuzņēmuma palaidējs arī noņem ``.baudolo-*`` atstāj nogalināts palaist atstāj iekšpusē datu saknes."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``backend``: ``cloud`` or ``chezmoi``"
msgstr "``backend``: ``cloud`` vai ``chezmoi``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``base_dir`` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "``base_dir`` (virkne): bāzes mape CA failiem"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays the dump in the next, so a consumer that boots in between recreates the schema and the replay dies on its own ``CREATE TABLE``. Hence the refusal while a consumer is up."
msgstr "``baudolo-restore --empty`` iepriekš attīra shēmu vienā psql sesijā un atkārto izgāztuves nākamajā, lai patērētājs, kas zābaki starp atjauno shēmu un atkārtotu spēli mirst pati ``CREATE TABLE``. Līdz ar to atteikums, kamēr patērētājs ir pieaudzis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bench new-site`` uses the central MariaDB’s ``root`` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "``bench new-site`` izmanto centrālo MariaDBir ``root`` izveidot uz vietas DB pirmajā izvietojumā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``biber`` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "``biber`` tikai jebkad pastāv iekšā EspoCRM caur OIDC automātisko piegādi (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` persona, kas darbojas katrā variantā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bond`` states how tightly a role couples to the service it declares: ``>= 1`` keeps the partner on the same host, ``< 1`` lets it live on its own. The value sits on the consumer's side of the relation, so the pair is directed and the two directions of one pair need not agree."
msgstr "``bond`` norāda, cik cieši lomu pāriem pakalpojumu, ko tā paziņo: ``>= 1`` uztur partneri tajā pašā mītnē, ``< 1`` ļauj tam dzīvot vienam pašam. Vērtība atrodas patērētāja pusē attiecībās, tāpēc pāris ir virzīts un viena pāra diviem virzieniem nav jāvienojas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **parent** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"
msgstr "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **vecāks** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` galekss)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ca_cert_host`` is where sys-ca-selfsigned provisions the root CA on the host. The container-side bind-mount targets live in the ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) and reach the standalone runtime scripts as env vars and CLI arguments."
msgstr "``ca_cert_host`` kur sys-ca-selfsigned nodrošina saknes CA uz uzņēmēja. Konteinera puses piesaistes-montēšanas mērķi dzīvo ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) un sasniegt standalone runtime skriptus kā env vars un CLI argumentus."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``canonical_domain`` is the host of ``canonical_url``, not the configured domain, so both follow the onion substitution a Tor deployment applies. A consumer that compares it against what a page actually renders would otherwise never match on an onion host."
msgstr "``canonical_domain`` ir ``canonical_url``, nevis konfigurēto domēnu, tāpēc abi sekot sīpolu aizvietošanu Tor izvietošana attiecas. Patērētājs, kas salīdzina to ar to, ko lapa faktiski renderē citādi nekad nesakristu ar sīpolu saimnieku."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``central_mariadb_root_password``: The root password for the MariaDB server."
msgstr "``central_mariadb_root_password``: root paroli MariaDB serveris."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``cert_host`` (string): host path to Root CA certificate"
msgstr "``cert_host`` (virkne): saimnieka ceļš uz saknes CA sertifikātu"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``classification``:  what this role is in the MCP audit. Required."
msgstr "``classification``: kāda ir šī loma MCP revīzijā. Vajadzīgs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``comments`` is the parsed per-key comment map from default.env (see :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dynamic keys carry their comments via each handler's ``COMMENT`` constant. ``custom.env`` overrides run last (see :func:`apply_custom_env`)."
msgstr "``comments`` ir parsed uz taustiņu komentāru karti no default.env (skatīt :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dinamiskās atslēgas veikt savus komentārus, izmantojot katra apstrādātāja ``COMMENT`` konstanti. ``custom.env`` noklusēt pēdējo (skatīt :func:`apply_custom_env`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose build`` re-bakes the static output whenever the cloned content changes, so deploys are content-driven without any runtime build step."
msgstr "``compose build`` atkārtoti bakes statisko izvades ikreiz, kad klonētā saturs mainās, tāpēc izvieto ir satura virzīta bez palaist laiku veidot soli."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose.cache-consumer.yml.j2``, ``apt.list.j2``, ``npmrc.j2`` and ``pip.conf.j2`` under ``templates/``, and the shell scripts under ``files/``, belong to the development compose stack, which drives them through `render.py <../../utils/cache/render.py>`__ and `compose.py <../../cli/administration/deploy/development/compose.py>`__. The Ansible deployment reads none of them."
msgstr "``compose.cache-consumer.yml.j2``, ``apt.list.j2``, ``npmrc.j2`` kā arī ``pip.conf.j2`` zem ``templates/``, un čaulas skripti zem ``files/``, pieder izstrādes komponēt kaudze, kas vada tos caur `render.py <../../utils/cache/render.py>`__ kā arī `compose.py <../../cli/administration/deploy/development/compose.py>`__. Assible izvietošana nolasa neviens no tiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` (deprecated)"
msgstr "``compose`` (novecojusi)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` is the in-repo Docker Compose stack. It remains installable but receives no new features."
msgstr "``compose`` ir in-repo Docker Compose kaudze. Tas paliek instalējams, bet nesaņem jaunas funkcijas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` or ``swarm`` to pin every image to that track, ``rotate`` to split the images across both."
msgstr "``compose`` vai ``swarm`` lai katru attēlu pievienotu šim celiņam, ``rotate`` sadalīt attēlus pa abiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``composer install`` failed."
msgstr "``composer install`` neizdevās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``config.access_grants: []``, administrator-only rather than public"
msgstr "``config.access_grants: []``, tikai administrators, nevis publiska"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer_not_allowed`` is a decision and simply narrows the result. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` and ``tools_unenforceable`` mean the provider did authorize this consumer and the connection still cannot be rendered, so they abort the run instead of disappearing quietly: a client that silently ends up with fewer tools than the deployment declared is indistinguishable from one that works."
msgstr "``consumer_not_allowed`` ir lēmums un vienkārši sašaurina rezultātu. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` kā arī ``tools_unenforceable`` tas nozīmē, ka pakalpojumu sniedzējs ir pilnvarojis šo patērētāju, un savienojumu joprojām nevar padarīt par tādu, tāpēc viņi pārtrauc skriešanu, nevis klusi pazūd: klients, kuram klusi ir mazāk rīku nekā deklarētajai izvietošanai, nav atšķirams no tāda, kas darbojas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer``: optional override"
msgstr "``consumer``: pēc izvēles izslēgt"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``container system prune -a -f`` to remove unused Docker resources."
msgstr "``container system prune -a -f`` lai izņemtu neizmantotos Docker resursus."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``core`` for every language but the source language, ``docs`` for the languages LibreTranslate supports."
msgstr "``core`` par katru valodu, bet avota valodu, ``docs`` valodām LibreTranslate balstiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential_missing`` is the one authorized rejection that does not abort, because a provider deploying later in the same play has not written its secret yet. That exemption ends at the reconciliation stage, which runs once every provider has: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` treats it as fatal there."
msgstr "``credential_missing`` ir viens pilnvarots noraidījums, kas nav pārtraukt, jo pakalpojumu sniedzējs izvietojot vēlāk tajā pašā lugā vēl nav rakstījis savu noslēpumu. Šis atbrīvojums beidzas saskaņošanas posmā, kurā katrs pakalpojumu sniedzējs: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` pret to ir letāls."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential``:      which principal the provider authenticates as, and where its secret is read from. Replaces the administrator token path."
msgstr "``credential``: kuru principāls pakalpojumu sniedzējs autentificē, kā un kur tās noslēpums ir nolasīts. Aizvieto administratora marķiera ceļu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, sent as ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"
msgstr "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, nosūtīts kā ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``custom.env`` is the operator's untracked override file; its values win over static defaults AND handler-computed values."
msgstr "``custom.env`` ir operatora neatsekots izslēgšanas fails; tā vērtības ir lielākas par statiskajām noklusējumiem UN apstrādātāja aprēķinātajām vērtībām."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_name``: The name of the initial database to create."
msgstr "``database_name``: Nosaukums sākotnējās datubāzes, lai izveidotu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_password``: The password for the database user."
msgstr "``database_password``: Parole datu bāzes lietotājam."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_username``: The username for the database user."
msgstr "``database_username``: Lietotājvārds datu bāzes lietotājam."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``days`` (int): certificate validity"
msgstr "``days`` (int): sertifikāta derīgums"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``default-address-pools`` is where docker takes that address from, so the declaration answers before the daemon exists and answers identically afterwards. That also keeps daemon.json byte-identical across passes, which the fact-derived value could not: it appeared only from the second run on and restarted the container runtime under a live stack."
msgstr "``default-address-pools`` ir kur docker ņem šo adresi no, tāpēc deklarācijas atbildes pirms dēmona pastāv un atbild identiski pēc tam. Tas arī uztur daemon.json baitu-identisks pāri caurlaidēm, kuru faktu atvasinātā vērtība nevarēja: tas parādījās tikai no otrās palaist un restartēja konteineru palaist laiku saskaņā ar dzīvu steku."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``delegation``:      recorded proof, at one exact upstream version, that per-user token acquisition, refresh, audience binding and revocation exist."
msgstr "``delegation``: ierakstīts pierādījums vienā precīzi iepriekšējā versijā par to, ka katram lietotājam ir iegādāšanās, atsvaidzināšana, auditorijas piesaiste un atsaukšana."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``deployment`` restricts to roles present anywhere in ``groups``, which is what a container-network consumer can actually reach; ``all`` returns every declaring role, deployed or not."
msgstr "``deployment`` ierobežo lomas klāt jebkur ``groups``, ko faktiski var sasniegt konteineru tīkla patērētājs; ``all`` atgriež katru deklarēšanas lomu, kas ir vai nav īstenota."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dest``: destination path (required for ``cloud``)"
msgstr "``dest``: mērķa ceļš (nepieciešama ``cloud``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``direction``:       whether the role exposes MCP, consumes it, or both."
msgstr "``direction``: vai loma atklāj MCP, patērē to, vai abi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``discourse``: the WP->Discourse post round-trip scenario. Disabling Discourse skips it; front-page reachability and CSP baselines stay active."
msgstr "``discourse``: WP–>Discourse pēc apļveida brauciena. Atslēdz Discourse izlaiž to; priekšējās lapas sasniedzamība un CSP bāzes palikt aktīvs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``docker_name``    the explicit ``name:`` field (alias for ``name``"
msgstr "``docker_name`` skaidri formulēts ``name:`` lauks (aizstājvārdu ``name``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``domains``: canonical and alias domains"
msgstr "``domains``: kanonisko un segvārdu domēni"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_apply`` (default: ``true``): run ``doli pull`` after adding mappings"
msgstr "``dotlinker_apply`` (noklusētais: ``true``): palaist ``doli pull`` pēc kartēšanas pievienošanas"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (noklusētais: ``doli``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_config_path`` (default: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_config_path`` (noklusētais: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_package_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_package_name`` (noklusētais: ``doli``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_replace`` (default: ``true``): pass ``--replace`` to ``doli add``"
msgstr "``dotlinker_replace`` (noklusētais: ``true``): iet ``--replace`` līdz ``doli add``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_user`` (required): user to run ``doli`` as"
msgstr "``dotlinker_user`` (nepieciešams): lietotājs, lai palaistu ``doli`` kā"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` and ``dsk-gnt-pi`` carry no entry in that map. Cursor is a full editor rather than an extension, and neither vendor publishes an extension on Open VSX, so there is nothing to install into Code for them. Both agents are used from their own binary."
msgstr "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` kā arī ``dsk-gnt-pi`` nav ieraksta šajā kartē. Kursors ir pilns redaktors, nevis paplašinājums, un ne pārdevējs publicē paplašinājumu Open VSX, tāpēc nav nekā uzstādīt Code viņiem. Abi aģenti tiek izmantoti no viņu pašu binārā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``enabled`` (bool)"
msgstr "``enabled`` (bool)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``endpoint``:        connection metadata for clients (server roles only)."
msgstr "``endpoint``: savienojuma metadati klientiem (tikai servera lomas)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``enforced`` onions every capable row, ``disabled`` none, ``exclusive`` drops the rows that cannot take one, ``auto`` rotates."
msgstr "``enforced`` sīpoli katras rindas garumā, ``disabled`` nav, ``exclusive`` nomet rindas, kas nevar veikt vienu, ``auto`` griežas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entries_only=true`` returns those strings as a list instead of the rendered block, for a container that is not described by a compose file at all: ``web-app-discourse`` is built by discourse_docker's ``launcher``, whose only argument surface is ``docker_args:`` in its ``app.yml``, so it needs ``--add-host=<entry>`` lines."
msgstr "``entries_only=true`` atgriež šīs virknes kā sarakstu, nevis renderēto bloku, konteineram, kas vispār nav aprakstīts ar komponēt failu: ``web-app-discourse`` ir būvēts discourse_docker's ``launcher``, kuras vienīgais arguments ir ``docker_args:`` tā ``app.yml``, Tāpēc ``--add-host=<entry>`` rindas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entries`` is a list of dotted-path facts about the file's content. Each entry carries the same ``mandatory`` and ``allowed`` semantics described above and adds a ``marker`` flag (default ``False``): ``marker: True`` declares the path as the type marker for the surrounding type entry. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` walks every ``marker: True`` entry; each marker that resolves to a non-empty value in the role's file adds the surrounding type to the role's type set. ``application_id`` for ``application`` and ``system_service_id`` for ``system-service`` are the canonical markers."
msgstr "``entries`` ir punktētā ceļa faktu saraksts par datnes saturu. Katrs ieraksts satur to pašu ``mandatory`` kā arī ``allowed`` iepriekš aprakstītā semantika un ``marker`` karogs (noklusētais ``False``): ``marker: True`` deklarē ceļu kā tipa marķieri apkārtējam tipa ierakstam. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` iet katru ``marker: True`` ieraksts; katrs marķieris, kas neatgriežas netukšā vērtībā lomu failā, pievieno apkārtējo tipu lomas tipa komplektam. ``application_id`` aizstāj ``application`` kā arī ``system_service_id`` aizstāj ``system-service`` ir kanoniskie marķieri."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` declares a ``run-name:`` that interpolates the dispatch inputs. Once a run has started, that title is the only record of them: the REST API answers ``inputs: null`` for a workflow_dispatch run. Anything that wants to know what a run was dispatched with therefore parses the title — and parsing it against a hand-copied format would drift the moment the workflow changes, silently and without a failing test."
msgstr "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` deklarē a ``run-name:`` kas interpolē nosūtīšanas ieejas. Kad palaist ir sākusies, šis nosaukums ir vienīgais ieraksts par tiem: REST API atbildes ``inputs: null`` tekstu workflow_dispatch palaist. Jebkas, kas vēlas zināt, ko palaist tika nosūtīti ar tāpēc parses nosaukumu - un parsing to pret roku kopēts formāts varētu driftēt brīdi darbplūsmas izmaiņas, klusi un bez neveiksmīga testa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ephemeral`` publishes the container port on a host port docker picks, for a service addressed only through the compose network."
msgstr "``ephemeral`` publicē konteinera portu uz uzņēmējas ostas dokeru cērtes, pakalpojumam, kas adresēts tikai caur kompožu tīklu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposed`` is an explicit per-service opt-in (default false) that makes the service reachable over the node onion: its port gets a dedicated ``HiddenServicePort``. Because ``applications`` is the variant-merged config (base ``meta/services.yml`` deep-merged with the round's ``meta/variants.yml`` override), a service is forwarded only in the variant/config where it sets ``exposed: true`` — which is exactly what lets the two DB variants be tested over Tor (v0 exposed -> reachable, v1 not -> refused)."
msgstr "``exposed`` ir skaidri noteikts katram pakalpojumam (noklusētais false) kas padara pakalpojumu sasniedzams pa mezgla sīpolu: tā osta kļūst veltīta ``HiddenServicePort``. Jo ``applications`` ir ar variantu apvienota konfigurācija (pamats ``meta/services.yml`` dziļi apvienoti ar apaļo ``meta/variants.yml`` noklusētais), pakalpojums tiek pārsūtīts tikai variantā / konfigurācijā, kur tā uzstāda ``exposed: true`` — kas ir tieši tas, kas ļauj testēt abus DB variantus pār Tor (v0 iedarbībai pakļauts -> sasniedzams, v1 nav:)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposure``:        who may reach the endpoint."
msgstr "``exposure``: kas var sasniegt galapunktu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``extra_hosts=``, whatever the call site needs on top: a peer's overlay VIP, or a partner service reachable only on the host."
msgstr "``extra_hosts=``, neatkarīgi no zvana vietā vajadzībām uz augšu: vienaudžu pārklājumu VIP, vai partneris pakalpojums sasniedzams tikai uz uzņēmēja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``false`` while MCP servers are discovered"
msgstr "``false`` kamēr tiek atklāti MCP serveri"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``family`` is the ``os_family`` ansible reports for the host. Callers that have facts (the action plugin) pass it, so distributions outside the CI matrix - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - still resolve through their family. Callers without facts (lints, the availability test) omit it and the family is derived from :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, which only covers the default matrix."
msgstr "``family`` ir ``os_family`` ziņojumi uzņēmējam. Zvanītāji, kam ir fakti (darbības spraudnis) pāriet, tāpēc sadalījums ārpus CI matricas - Manjaro, Monētu kaltuve, Rokijs - joprojām atrisināt ar savu ģimeni. Zvanītāji bez faktiem (Stiepes, pieejamības tests) izlaist to un saime ir iegūta no :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, kas attiecas tikai uz noklusējuma matricu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` serves the filer web UI behind an admin-only oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` apkalpo filera tīmekļa UI aiz admin- tikai oauth2- proksi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (run on the deploy host) completes the first-run wizard (seeds the break-glass admin), installs both plugins via Jellyfin’s own ``/Packages`` installer, writes the plugin configs, and restarts."
msgstr "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (palaist uz izvietošanas resursdatora) pabeidz pirmās kārtas vedni (sēklas stikla spraugas admin), uzstāda abus spraudņus caur Jellyfinpaša ``/Packages`` uzstādītājs, raksta spraudnis konfigurācijas, un restartē."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/playwright.config.js``: shared Playwright configuration"
msgstr "``files/playwright.config.js``: dalīta Playwright konfigurācija"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/python/policy.py`` validates it at startup. A contract missing a limit, carrying an empty allowlist, naming a wildcard path or lacking a pinned schema hash is refused before the process serves anything."
msgstr "``files/python/policy.py`` Apstiprina to, uzsākot darbu. Līgums, kurā trūkst ierobežojuma, ir tukšs letlists, kas nosauc zvaigznītes ceļu vai kam trūkst pinned shēmas hash, tiek noraidīts, pirms process kaut ko kalpo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``flags``: list of flags to AND. Default: ``[enabled, shared]``"
msgstr "``flags``: saraksts ar karogiem uz UN. Noklusētais: ``[enabled, shared]``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``flavor`` picks the probe shape (see utils/docker/healthcheck/); each flavor brings its own interval, timeout, retries and start_period, and any of those may be overridden next to it. Without a ``flavor`` the entry must carry an explicit ``test`` argv. ``port_key`` selects another entry below ``ports.internal`` for services that expose their probe on a second port."
msgstr "``flavor`` izvēlas zondes formu (skatīt utils/docker/healthcheck/); Katra garša nes savu intervālu, noildze, retries un start_period, un jebkuru no tiem var atcelt blakus tam. Bez ``flavor`` uz ieraksta jābūt skaidram ``test`` argv. ``port_key`` izvēlas citu ierakstu zemāk ``ports.internal`` pakalpojumiem, kas pakļauj to zondei otrā ostā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``force_regen`` (bool): if true, remove and regenerate key/cert"
msgstr "``force_regen`` (bool): ja taisnība, noņemt un atjaunot atslēgu/krekli"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``forward[A]`` is the list of provider roles that ``A`` directly depends on (services it embeds). ``reverse[B]`` is the list of roles that directly depend on ``B`` (consumers that embed ``B``)."
msgstr "``forward[A]`` ir pakalpojumu sniedzēja funkciju saraksts, kas ``A`` tieši atkarīgs no (pakalpojumi tā iegulto). ``reverse[B]`` ir saraksts ar lomām, kas ir tieši atkarīgas no ``B`` (patērētāji, kas iegulti ``B``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``galaxy_info.author`` is where a role records who implemented it, so that is where the names are read. A role may credit more than one person, comma separated."
msgstr "``galaxy_info.author`` ir vieta, kur lomu ierakstus, kas īsteno, lai būtu tur, kur nosaukumi tiek lasīti. Loma var ieskaitīt vairāk nekā vienu personu, komats atdalīts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``getent`` honours nsswitch and cannot address a server, so on its own it cannot say which of the resolvers in resolv.conf refused. Where the distro ships a query tool, ask every nameserver directly; where it does not, the per-name verdicts still stand on their own."
msgstr "``getent`` godina nswitch un nevar adrese serveri, tāpēc pats par sevi tas nevar teikt, kurš no resorters in resolv.conf atteikta. Ja distro kuģi vaicājuma rīks, jautājiet katram nameserver tieši; ja tas nav, uz vārdu spriedumi joprojām stāv par savu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` is the single source of truth for host paths. The env layer (utils/env/handlers, exported by scripts/meta/env/load.sh) derives the ``INFINITO_*`` env keys from it; a set env wins so callers can override. When a tool runs outside that layer, e.g. a bare ``subprocess`` that does not inherit the env build, the value is read straight from the group_vars SPOT, so there is still no hardcoded literal default."
msgstr "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` ir vienīgais avots patiesības uzņēmējas ceļu. Env slānis (utils/env/handlers, eksportējis scripts/meta/env/load.sh) iegūst ``INFINITO_*`` env taustiņus no tā; komplekts env uzvar, lai zvanītāji var ignorēt. Ja rīks iziet ārpus šī slāņa, piemēram, tukša ``subprocess`` kas nav mantot env būvēt, vērtība ir lasīt tieši no group_vars SPOT, tāpēc joprojām nav grūti kodēts burtisks noklusējuma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``host_alias=true``, which pins ``host.docker.internal`` at whatever reaches the host in the effective mode. A container that must talk to a service the host publishes -- msmtp relaying through the swarm ingress on :587, for instance -- needs the alias, and it must not hardcode ``host-gateway`` because that breaks under swarm for the reason below."
msgstr "``host_alias=true``, kas tapas ``host.docker.internal`` pie kāda sasniedz saimnieks faktiskajā režīmā. Konteiners, kas runā ar pakalpojumu uzņēmējas publicē -- msmtp relaying caur barm ingress par :587, piemēram -- nepieciešams segvārds, un tas nedrīkst hardcode ``host-gateway`` jo tas pārtraukumiem zem bars par iemeslu zemāk."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, own network only"
msgstr "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, tikai savs tīkls"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` on the shared MCP overlay"
msgstr "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` par kopīgoto MCP pārklājumu"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``implementation``:  how the surface is provided, ordered by precedence."
msgstr "``implementation``: kā tiek nodrošināta virsma, sakārtota pēc prioritātes."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``in_container`` exists because one template serves two consumers. The host's /root/.msmtprc is read by the host and loopback is right for it; the copy mounted at /etc/msmtprc is read inside a container, where 127.0.0.1 is that container's own loopback and nothing listens on it. Such a service must also emit ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` so the alias resolves."
msgstr "``in_container`` pastāv, jo viena veidne kalpo diviem patērētājiem. Datora / root /.msmtprc to nolasa resursdators, un tā vietā ir atgriezums; kopiju piemontētu pie /etc / msmtprc nolasa konteinerā, kur 127.0.0.1 Tas konteiners ir paša cilpains un nekas tajā neklausās. Šādam pakalpojumam arī jāizsniedz: ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` tā segvārds atrisina."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``indent=0`` collapses everything to the left edge - useful when the lookup is rendered into top-level YAML (no service wrapper)."
msgstr "``indent=0`` sabrūk viss uz kreiso malu - noderīga, kad lookup tiek renderēta augšējā līmenī YAML (Nav pakalpojuma iesaiņojuma)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ingress`` (default) emits the short ``\"host:published:container\"`` string; ``host`` emits the long block with ``mode: host``, which is what an edge role needs in swarm so the client address survives the hop."
msgstr "``ingress`` (noklusētais) emitē īso ``\"host:published:container\"`` virkne; ``host`` izstaro garo bloku ar ``mode: host``, kas ir tas, ko malas loma nepieciešama bars, lai klienta adrese izdzīvo hop."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``internal`` (default) reads ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` reuses the published port, for services that cannot remap (STUN/TURN, media relays)."
msgstr "``internal`` (noklusētais) lasītājs ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` atkārtoti izmanto publicēto portu, par pakalpojumiem, kas nevar pārkārtot (STUN/TURN, datu nesēju releji)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``internal``, container network only"
msgstr "``internal``, tikai konteineru tīkls"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``kas`` (Kubernetes agent server, workspaces), ``pages``, ``registry`` and ``mailroom`` are not deployed; ``gitlab.yml`` disables them."
msgstr "``kas`` (Kubernetes aģentu serveris, darba vietas), ``pages``, ``registry`` kā arī ``mailroom`` netiek izmantoti; ``gitlab.yml`` izslēdz tos."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key_bits`` (int): RSA key size"
msgstr "``key_bits`` (int): RSA atslēgas izmērs"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key_host`` (string): host path to Root CA private key"
msgstr "``key_host`` (virkne): saimnieka ceļš uz Saknes CA privāto atslēgu"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key`` names the pinned key and defaults to ``version``; an entity with several pins declares a list of such blocks. The types are ``git_tags`` (repository), ``registry_tags`` (image), ``npm`` (package), ``http_regex`` (url, pattern) and ``script`` (path, run with the current version and printing the latest one)."
msgstr "``key`` nosauc pinned taustiņu un noklusējuma uz ``version``; uzņēmums ar vairākām tapām paziņo sarakstu ar šādiem blokiem. Šie veidi ir: ``git_tags`` (repozitorijs), ``registry_tags`` (attēls), ``npm`` (Iepakojums), ``http_regex`` (url, raksts) kā arī ``script`` (ceļš, palaist ar pašreizējo versiju un drukāšana pēdējā)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key``: services.<key>.* lookup base. Default: provides or entity_name"
msgstr "``key``: pakalpojumi.<key>.* Lookup bāze. Noklusētais: nodrošina vai entity_name"

# ``database`` י ``mcp_client`` י ``web_facing`` י ``onion_sso``.
# ``mcp_client`` atzīst lomu tikai tad, ja ``mcp.direction`` ir ``client`` vai
# ``both`` UN tā paziņo: ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true``
# pakalpojumu sniedzējs to neatsaka, ``mcp_consumer: false`` tajā pašā
# ierakstā, tādējādi pakalpojumu sniedzēja tīkls nes klientus, kurus tas
# uzņēmies, nevis katru klientu izvietošanā. Būt klientam nav uzņemšana: bez
# otrā nosacījuma viena uzņemšana jebkur sasniedz katru pakalpojumu sniedzēju,
# kas atver savu pārklājumu.
# translation-refused: libretranslate stutter
# nocheck: url
# translation-rejected: ``kind``: ``services_flags`` (noklusētais) י
msgid "``kind``: ``services_flags`` (default) | ``database`` | ``mcp_client`` | ``web_facing`` | ``onion_sso``. ``mcp_client`` admits a role only when its ``mcp.direction`` is ``client`` or ``both`` AND it declares ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true`` without the provider refusing it through ``mcp_consumer: false`` on that same entry, so a provider's network carries the clients it admitted rather than every client in the deployment. Being a client is not an admission: without the second condition one admission anywhere reaches every provider that opens its overlay."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``last`` seeds the OCI pagination cursor: only tags sorting lexically after it are returned. Repos like GitLab CNG carry tens of thousands of commit-sha tags before the ``v*`` release tags, so an unseeded scan exhausts ``max_pages`` without ever reaching them."
msgstr "``last`` sēklas OCI pagination kursors: tikai birkas šķirošanas leksiski pēc tam, kad tas tiek atgriezts. Repo līdzīgi GitLab SDG pirms ``v*`` atbrīvot tagus, tāpēc bez sēklām skenēt izplūdes ``max_pages`` nesasniedzot tos."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``latest`` is the last commit of the default branch. It is built at start and rebuilt whenever a fetch finds a new commit; the previous build stays online until the new one replaces it."
msgstr "``latest`` ir saistību neizpildes filiāles pēdējais nodevums. Tas ir būvēts sākumā un pārbūvēts ikreiz, kad atnesums atrod jaunu nodevumu; iepriekšējā būvē paliek tiešsaistē, līdz jaunais to aizstāj."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``laya``, ``torch`` or ``onnx``; the role refuses anything else"
msgstr "``laya``, ``torch`` vai ``onnx``; loma atsakās jebko citu"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ldap``: the three RBAC scenarios additionally depend on LDAP group sync; disabling LDAP skips them alongside OIDC."
msgstr "``ldap``: trīs RBAC scenāriji papildus ir atkarīgi no LDAP grupas sinhronizācijas; LDAP atspējošana tos izlaiž līdzās OIDC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ldapauth`` is the only path that materialises a ``friendica.user`` row, so its enablement derives directly from the ``ldap`` service flag. The oauth2-proxy ``sso`` gate in front of the vhost is a front-door auth gate, not an addon bridge, and stays in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. The LDAP login path is covered by the existing LDAP Playwright spec (requirement 018), so no addon-specific spec is added."
msgstr "``ldapauth`` ir vienīgais ceļš, kas īsteno a ``friendica.user`` rindu, tāpēc tā iespējošana izriet tieši no ``ldap`` dienesta karogs. Zvaigzne2- proksijs ``sso`` vārti priekšā vhost ir priekšā durvju auth vārti, nevis addon tilts, un paliek ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>` . LDAP pieteikšanās ceļu aptver esošā LDAP Playwright spec (prasība 018), tāpēc nav pievienots addonam specifisks spec."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``libaacs`` (AACS decryption library)"
msgstr "``libaacs`` (AACS atšifrēšanas bibliotēka)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``libbluray`` (Blu-ray playback support library)"
msgstr "``libbluray`` (Blu-ray atskaņošanas atbalsta bibliotēka)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lifecycle``  — maturity marker filtered by ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."
msgstr "``lifecycle`` — termiņu marķieris, ko filtrē ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``limits``:          the request, response, timeout, concurrency, pagination and stream ceilings the surface enforces."
msgstr "``limits``: pieprasījums, atbilde, noildze, concurity, pagination un plūsmu griesti virsmas nodrošina."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale-gen`` only re-runs when the template changes"
msgstr "``locale-gen`` Atjaunina tikai tad, kad mainās veidne"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale.conf``: sets ``LANG`` and ``LANGUAGE`` environment variables"
msgstr "``locale.conf``: komplekti ``LANG`` kā arī ``LANGUAGE`` Vides mainīgie"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale.gen``: uncomment or specify the locales you need"
msgstr "``locale.gen``: atkomentēt vai norādīt lokālos jums nepieciešams"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('guide_role', application_id)`` picks the first invokable app the round deployed beside ``application_id``. Invokability comes from :func:`utils.roles.validation.invokable.list_invokable_app_ids`, so no caller re-derives it from role-name prefixes."
msgstr "``lookup('guide_role', application_id)`` izvēlas pirmo piesakās app kārtā izvietoto blakus ``application_id``. Neapsūdzība nāk no :func:`utils.roles.validation.invokable.list_invokable_app_ids`, tāpēc neviens zvanītājs atkārtoti nošķir to no lomu nosaukumu priedēkļiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('users', user_key).authorized_keys`` (list; may be empty)"
msgstr "``lookup('users', user_key).authorized_keys`` (saraksts; var būt tukšs)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('users', user_key).username`` (defaults to ``user_key``)"
msgstr "``lookup('users', user_key).username`` (noklusētais ``user_key``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``lookup('volume', application_id)`` — return the WHOLE canonical registry as a dict keyed by semantic name. Useful for tasks that loop over every declared volume (e.g. NFS subdir pre-creation). Returns ``{}`` for roles with no meta/volumes.yml."
msgstr "``lookup('volume', application_id)`` — atgriež WHOLE kanonisko reģistru kā diktātu, kas ir atslēgts ar semantisku nosaukumu. Noderīga uzdevumiem, kas cilpa pār katru deklarēto skaļumu (Piemēram, NFS subdir pirms radīšanas). Atgriešanās ``{}`` lomas bez meta/volumes.yml."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('volume', application_id, name)`` — return the normalised dict for a single semantic entry. The returned dict always carries:"
msgstr "``lookup('volume', application_id, name)`` — atgriež normalizēto diktātu par vienu semantisku ierakstu. Atgrieztais diktāts vienmēr satur:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``main.yml``: The main task file that handles the installation of GnuCash."
msgstr "``main.yml``: Galvenais uzdevums datne, kas apstrādā uzstādīšanu GnuCash."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``main`` unless ``repo_root`` is a linked git worktree, whose branch is lowercased and every character outside ``[a-z0-9_-]`` replaced by ``-``; ``None`` when the worktree's git directory is not reachable, as inside a container that mounts only the checkout."
msgstr "``main`` ja vien ``repo_root`` ir saistīts git worktree, kura zars ir mazāks un katra rakstzīme ārpus ``[a-z0-9_-]`` aizstāts ar ``-``; ``None`` kad worktree git direktorija nav sasniedzama, jo iekšpusē konteiners, kas piemontē tikai izrakstīšanās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``make install-lint`` used to ask GitHub for each tool’s latest tag at install time. That made every installation depend on the network resolving ``api.github.com``, and it silently changed the linter version between two runs of the same commit. Pinning moves the version into the repository, where it is reviewable and reproducible."
msgstr "``make install-lint`` izmanto, lai lūgtu GitHub katra rīka jaunāko tagu uzstādīšanas laikā. Tas padarīja katru iekārtu atkarīga no tīkla izšķirt ``api.github.com``, un tas klusi mainīja linter versiju starp diviem braucieniem no vienas saistības. Pinning pārceļ versiju uz repozitoriju, kur tā ir pārskatāma un reproducējama."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``make install`` completed on the control machine (installs Ansible and Python dependencies)."
msgstr "``make install`` Aizpilda uz kontroles iekārtas (Uzstāda Ansible un Python atkarības)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mandatory`` (default ``False``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MUST be present and non-empty for a role of this type. Implies ``allowed: True``; setting ``mandatory: True`` together with ``allowed: False`` is a schema error."
msgstr "``mandatory`` (noklusētais ``False``): datne (vai punktētā ceļa ieraksts) Jābūt klāt un nav tukšums par šāda veida lomu. Nosacījumi ``allowed: True``; iestatījums ``mandatory: True`` kopā ar ``allowed: False`` ir shēmas kļūda."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``master.seaweedfs.s3.*`` serves the master web UI behind the same admin-only oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "``master.seaweedfs.s3.*`` kalpo galvenais web UI aiz vienas un tās pašas administrācijas tikai oauth2- proksi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``match`` keeps only the versions carrying that prefix, and ``strip`` removes it again, so a pin without the upstream's ``v`` stays without it."
msgstr "``match`` tur tikai versijas, kas pārvadā šo prefiksu, un ``strip`` noņem to atkal, tāpēc pin bez augšpusē s ``v`` paliek bez tā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mcp-server`` pinned to ``0.190.ve5a_6581ffc96`` in ```files/plugins.txt`` <./files/plugins.txt>`__"
msgstr "``mcp-server`` piestiprināts pie ``0.190.ve5a_6581ffc96`` skaits ```files/plugins.txt`` <./files/plugins.txt>`"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mcp.enabled`` resolves to ``true`` only when ``web-app-hermes``, ``web-app-openclaw`` or ``web-app-openwebui`` is part of the same deployment, and is ``false`` otherwise. While it is ``true`` the deploy:"
msgstr "``mcp.enabled`` atrisina ``true`` tikai tad, ja ``web-app-hermes``, ``web-app-openclaw`` vai ``web-app-openwebui`` ir daļa no vienas izvietošanas un ir ``false`` citādi. Kamēr tas ir ``true`` izvietošana:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mcp`` declares the Model Context Protocol surface GitLab serves natively from its Rails API."
msgstr "``mcp`` deklarē konteksta protokola parauga virsmu GitLab kalpo natively no tās sliedes API."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``meta/addons/`` is also the download list: ``MEDIAWIKI_EXT_NAMES`` keeps only the addons whose ``enabled`` resolves true, so a deployment without the matching service never pulls that tarball or runs composer for it."
msgstr "``meta/addons/`` ir arī lejupielādes saraksts: ``MEDIAWIKI_EXT_NAMES`` saglabā tikai addonus, kuru ``enabled`` atrisina taisnība, tāpēc izvietošana bez saskaņošanas pakalpojums nekad velk, ka tarball vai vada komponists par to."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``meta/categories.yml`` at the repository root declares the nested category tree every role name is derived from: the dash-joined path of a node is the role's category prefix (``web`` -> ``app`` yields ``web-app-*``), and nodes carry the ``invokable``, ``stage``, ``modes`` and ``run_after`` policy the dispatcher, the stage lookup and the inventory generator read."
msgstr "``meta/categories.yml`` krātuvē saknes deklarē ieligzdotā kategorijas koku katru lomu nosaukums ir atvasināts no: mezglpunkta blakus esošais ceļš ir lomas kategorijas prefikss (``web`` - BAR ``app`` ražība ``web-app-*``), un mezgli nes ``invokable``, ``stage``, ``modes`` kā arī ``run_after`` politika dispečers, skatuves lookup un inventāra ģenerators lasīt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``meta/categories.yml`` declares the ordered ``stages`` (constructor -> workstation -> server -> destructor, matching ``tasks/stages/0*.yml``) and a ``stage`` per top-level category. This module resolves a role to its stage and exposes the canonical stage order, so both the CLI (``cli.meta.roles.order``) and the ``stage_order`` / ``role_stage`` lookups read one source of truth."
msgstr "``meta/categories.yml`` paziņo pasūtīto ``stages`` (konstruktors -> darbstacija -> serveris -> destructor, saskaņošana ``tasks/stages/0*.yml``) un a ``stage`` katrā augstākā līmeņa kategorijā. Šis modulis atrisina lomu uz savu posmu un atklāj kanonisko posmu kārtību, tāpēc abi CLI (``cli.meta.roles.order``) un ``stage_order`` / ``role_stage`` lookups lasīt vienu avotu patiesību."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``meta/distros.yml`` declares every distribution the project builds, tests and deploys on: the id used as ``INFINITO_DISTRO``, the ``os_family`` ansible reports for it, the Galaxy platform name, the upstream base image the development-environment matrix boots it from, and the templates the pkgmgr base image and the environment image references are rendered from."
msgstr "``meta/distros.yml`` paziņo par katru projekta izveidoto, testēto un izmantoto distribūciju: ``INFINITO_DISTRO``, ``os_family`` par to ir pieejami ziņojumi, Galaxy platformas nosaukums, augšpusējais bāzes attēls, no kā tiek ielādēta attīstības vides matrica, un no tā tiek renderēts pkgmgr bāzes attēls un vides attēlu atsauces."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``meta/variants.yml`` defines three variants (mirrors the ``web-app-kix`` / ``web-app-zammad`` pattern):"
msgstr "``meta/variants.yml`` definē trīs variantus (tā kā ``web-app-kix`` / ``web-app-zammad`` modelis):"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mode`` selects placement semantics:"
msgstr "``mode`` izvēlas izvietojuma semantiku:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``modes`` in ``meta/services.yml`` states where a role RUNS; ``skip`` in ``meta/tests.yml`` deactivates TESTING a mode without touching that capability."
msgstr "``modes`` skaits ``meta/services.yml`` valstis, kurās ir RUNS loma; ``skip`` skaits ``meta/tests.yml`` deaktivizē režīmu, nepieskaroties šai iespējai."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``modes``: list of DEPLOYMENT_MODE values where this overlay applies"
msgstr "``modes``: saraksts DEPLOYMENT_MODE vērtības, uz kurām attiecas šis pārklājums"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mounts``         the raw mounts list, ``[]`` if absent"
msgstr "``mounts`` neapstrādāto stiprinājumu saraksts, ``[]`` ja nav"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``msgctxt`` prefixes of the messages to include, e.g. ``role:``."
msgstr "``msgctxt`` ietveramo ziņojumu prefiksi, piem. ``role:``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mutating_proofs``: required once ``tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` is true. Names the artifact proving each of confirmation, authorization, idempotency, audit and reversal for the mutating variant, separately from the read-only one."
msgstr "``mutating_proofs``: obligāti vienu reizi ``tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` ir taisnība. Norāda artefaktu, kas pierāda katru apstiprinājumu, atļauju, atsaukumu, revīziju un apvērsi mutatis mutandis, atsevišķi no lasāmā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``name``           the EFFECTIVE docker volume name"
msgstr "``name`` EFTI docker sējuma nosaukums"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``name``: unique mapping id"
msgstr "``name``: unikāls kartēšanas id"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``networks.internet.dns`` arrives through ``-e @inventories/...`` and is read straight out of ``variables``, which hands back whatever the file contains. While that was a literal address nobody noticed; an expression there reached the daemon as its own source text and docker refused the config with ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."
msgstr "``networks.internet.dns`` ierodas caur ``-e @inventories/...`` un to nolasa ``variables``, kas rokas atpakaļ, neatkarīgi no faila satur. Lai gan tas bija burtisks adrese neviens pamanīja; izteiksme tur sasniedza dēmonu kā savu avota tekstu un dokeris atteicās konfigurācija ar ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``new_text_or_None`` is ``None`` when nothing changed."
msgstr "``new_text_or_None`` ir ``None`` kad nekas nav mainījies."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``nfs``            NFS opt-in (bool or dict), ``None`` if absent"
msgstr "``nfs`` NFS izvēles iespēja (bool vai dict), ``None`` ja nav"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``noqa`` and ``nocheck`` are accepted as synonyms (case-insensitive) by this parser. By repo convention every project rule from ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` MUST use ``nocheck:`` because ``# noqa: <code>`` is also parsed by ruff as a flake8 directive and triggers ``invalid-noqa-code`` warnings on every project-specific rule key. ``noqa:`` is reserved for real flake8 / ruff codes (``E402``, ``F401``, …). The ``direct-yaml`` lint enforces the convention by hard-rejecting the ``noqa:`` form."
msgstr "``noqa`` kā arī ``nocheck`` tiek pieņemti kā sinonīmi (Nejutīgs) ar šo parsētājs. Ar repo līgumu katru projekta noteikumu ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` JĀIEVĒRO ``nocheck:`` jo ``# noqa: <code>`` tiek arī parsēts ar ruff kā pārslu8 Direktīva un kritēriji ``invalid-noqa-code`` brīdinājumi par katru konkrēta projekta noteikumu atslēgu. ``noqa:`` ir rezervēta īstām pārslām8 / Rifa kodi (``E402``, ``F401``, ...). ``direct-yaml`` tiek īstenota konvencija, noraidot ``noqa:`` forma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``offset`` moves that start deliberately: it is how an operator reaches the tail without waiting for anything. It defaults to 0, so every run that does not ask for it deploys the same head and can be compared against the last one. This used to be derived from the sweep number instead, which bought tail coverage at the price of the head -- chunk 0 began wherever the arithmetic pointed, the rows that matter most ran only every few sweeps, and no two runs were comparable."
msgstr "``offset`` kustības, kas sākas apzināti: tas ir, kā operators sasniedz asti, negaidot neko. Tas noklusē līdz 0, tāpēc katru skrējiens, kas neprasa, lai tas izvietotu to pašu galvu un var salīdzināt ar pēdējo. Tas bija atvasināts no slaucīšanas numura, kas iegādājās astes pārklājumu par galvas cenu -- gabaliņš 0 sākās, kur aritmētiskā norādīja, rindas, kas bija svarīgi, ilga tikai ik pēc pāris slaucīšanu, un neviens divas trases bija salīdzināmas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``oidc-authenticator`` and ``ldap-authenticator`` are mutually exclusive auth backends (only one may be enabled; see ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` carries only the installer coordinate."
msgstr "``oidc-authenticator`` kā arī ``ldap-authenticator`` ir savstarpēji izslēdzošas auth aizmugures (var iespējot tikai vienu; skat. ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` veic tikai uzstādītāja koordinātas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``oidc``: baseline admin OIDC round-trip plus the three RBAC scenarios (subscriber/editor/administrator)."
msgstr "``oidc``: bāzes līnijas admin OIDC apļa posms plus trīs RBAC scenāriji (subscriber/editor/administrator)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``openssl_conf_host`` (string): host path for generated openssl.cnf"
msgstr "``openssl_conf_host`` (virkne): resursdatora ceļš ģenerēts openssl.cnf"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``out`` itself lives under the dump dir (both derive from INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), so the walk must skip its own output subtree or copytree recurses into the growing destination until ENAMETOOLONG."
msgstr "``out`` pats dzīvo zem dump dir (abi izriet no INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), tāpēc pastaiga ir izlaist savu produkciju apakškoku vai kopēttree atkārtojas uz pieaugošo galamērķi līdz ENAMETOOLONG."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``owner/repo`` the branch lives on."
msgstr "``owner/repo`` filiāles darbība."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``owner/repo`` the run lives in."
msgstr "``owner/repo`` bēgšana dzīvo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``package.json`` and ``playwright.config.js`` are provided centrally by this role:"
msgstr "``package.json`` kā arī ``playwright.config.js`` ko centrāli nodrošina šī funkcija:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``package_name`` (string) Name of the Python package to install (e.g., ``dockreap``, ``backup-docker-to-local``)."
msgstr "``package_name`` (virkne) Uzstādāmās Python pakotnes nosaukums (piem., ``dockreap``, ``backup-docker-to-local``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``password`` (should come from vault/credentials)"
msgstr "``password`` (jānāk no velvēm/krātiņiem)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``path``           the legacy ``path:`` field, ``''`` if absent"
msgstr "``path`` mantojums ``path:`` lauks, ``''`` ja nav"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``phpunit/phpunit`` declares ``_PHPUNIT_EXTENSIONS`` as platform requirements and Composer refuses to resolve the vendor tree without them, so they are part of the toolchain rather than of the suite consuming it. A distro ships them as packages separate from the interpreter, which is why a present ``php`` binary does not imply they are there."
msgstr "``phpunit/phpunit`` deklarē ``_PHPUNIT_EXTENSIONS`` kā platformas prasības un Composer atsakās atrisināt pārdevēja koks bez tām, tāpēc tie ir daļa no instrumentu ķēdes, nevis no suite patērē to. Distro kuģi tos kā paketes atsevišķi no tulka, kas ir iemesls, kāpēc dāvana ``php`` binārs nenozīmē, ka tie ir tur."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``playwright.spec.js`` — orchestrator: TLS baseline, project creation, image asset upload, and the ``guest``/``biber``/``administrator`` personas. The ``biber`` / ``administrator`` personas are declared blocked via ``PERSONA_*_BLOCKED`` (mirroring ``web-app-taiga``): Penpot’s in-app “OpenID” entry and SPA user-menu logout aren’t driveable by the generic persona helper, so both users’ real auth is exercised by the dedicated login companions above."
msgstr "``playwright.spec.js`` — orķestrs: TLS bāzes scenārijs, projekta izveide, attēlu augšupielāde un ``guest``/``biber``/``administrator`` personas. E ir o pa s ``biber`` / ``administrator`` personas tiek deklarētas bloķētas, izmantojot ``PERSONA_*_BLOCKED`` (spogulis ``web-app-taiga``): Penpot ir in-app “OpenID” ieraksts un SPA lietotāja-izvēlnes pieteikšanās nav vadāms ar ģenērisko persona palīgs, tāpēc gan lietotāju reālā auth tiek izmantota ar īpašu pieteikšanās pavadoņi iepriekš."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``playwright.version`` in ``meta/services.yml`` is the single source of truth for the default Playwright version; the central ``templates/package.json.j2`` pins it via the ``image_version`` filter."
msgstr "``playwright.version`` skaits ``meta/services.yml`` ir viens avots patiesības noklusējuma Playwright versija; centrālā ``templates/package.json.j2`` ieduriet to caur ``image_version`` filtrs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``plg_system_keycloak`` is built imperatively inside the Joomla container and speaks OIDC against Keycloak. Its enablement derives directly from the ``sso`` service flag, and its OIDC runtime contract (issuer, client id/secret, redirect/end-session URLs, fallback toggle, and RBAC group paths) lives under the addon’s ``config:`` block, which ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders into the ``JOOMLA_OIDC_*`` plugin environment."
msgstr "``plg_system_keycloak`` ir būvēts obligāti iekšpusē Joomla tvertnes un runā OIDC pret Keycloak. Tā iespēja izriet tieši no ``sso`` pakalpojuma pazīme un tās OIDC darba laika līgums (Emitents, klienta id/secret, pāradresēt/beigas URL, pārslēgties un RBAC grupas ceļi) dzīvo zem addon ir ``config:`` bloku, kas ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders into the ``JOOMLA_OIDC_*`` spraudņa vide."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``poll: 0`` makes a task fire and forget, so its own ``changed_when`` and ``failed_when`` never see an outcome. The outcome only exists once the job is collected with ``async_status``, and collecting it is where the verdict has to be made -- for a whole batch at once, so one run reports every broken job rather than the first."
msgstr "``poll: 0`` padara uzdevumu uguns un aizmirst, tāpēc savu ``changed_when`` kā arī ``failed_when`` nekad neredzi iznākumu. Rezultāts pastāv tikai tad, kad darbs ir savākts ar ``async_status``, un savākt to ir tur, kur spriedums ir jāpieņem -- par visu partiju uzreiz, tāpēc viens palaist ziņo katru bojāto darbu, nevis pirmo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ports.onion`` is a category-keyed map of booleans alongside ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: it names which of a service's already-declared ports should answer on the node onion, and nothing else. The port number comes from ``ports.local`` when that category is declared there and from ``ports.public`` otherwise, which is the precedence ``container_ports`` publishes by, so the forward always targets the port the service is actually reachable on."
msgstr "``ports.onion`` ir kategorijas atslēga karte booleans līdzās ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: tas norāda, kuras no pakalpojuma jau deklarētajām ostām vajadzētu atbildēt uz mezgla sīpolu, un nekas cits. Ostas numurs ir no ``ports.local`` ja šī kategorija ir deklarēta tur un no ``ports.public`` pretējā gadījumā, kas ir prioritāte ``container_ports`` publicē, tāpēc uz priekšu vienmēr mērķē osta pakalpojums ir faktiski sasniedzams."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``priority`` IS the retrigger: it names what failed. ``offset`` is recomputed rather than carried, but from the carried value up: the source run got a stretch behind its own offset green before its budget ran out, so the regular line resumes behind that stretch (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) instead of repeating it, and never falls back behind where that run started. Everything else is carried verbatim, including ``whitelist``, so a retrigger of a scoped run stays inside that scope instead of quietly widening to the whole repository."
msgstr "``priority`` IR retrigger: tas nosauc to, kas neizdevās. ``offset`` ir recomputed nevis veic, bet no uzskaites vērtību uz augšu: avots palaist got stiept aiz savas ofseta zaļā pirms tās budžets beidzās, tāpēc regulāra līnija atsāk aiz ka stiept (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) tā vietā, lai atkārtot to, un nekad atkrīt atpakaļ, kur tas palaist. Viss pārējais tiek veikts burtiski, ieskaitot ``whitelist``, tāpēc retrigger no tvēruma palaist paliek šajā jomā, nevis klusi paplašinot uz visu repozitoriju."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``provider`` / ``provider_key``: for ``onion_sso``, the app whose"
msgstr "``provider`` / ``provider_key``: ``onion_sso``, kas"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``provides`` matching runs in both directions, so a provider (e.g. openldap ``provides: ldap``) is picked up even when the consuming flag uses a ``groups[...]`` form the ``group_names`` regex cannot read."
msgstr "``provides`` saskaņošana notiek abos virzienos, lai pakalpojumu sniedzējs (Piemēram, openldap ``provides: ldap``) tiek uzņemts pat tad, ja patērē karoga izmanto ``groups[...]`` sagatavo ``group_names`` regex nevar lasīt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_aliases``: aliases the beacon exposes for harvesting; falls back"
msgstr "``proxy_aliases``: pieņem, ka bākas atsedz ražas novākšanai; atkrīt"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_pass`` directive; swarm prepends a ``set`` line (request-time DNS)."
msgstr "``proxy_pass`` Direktīva ``set`` rinda (pieprasījuma laika DNS)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_resolvable``: beacon flag - the harvested aliases get attached to"
msgstr "``proxy_resolvable``: bākas karogs - novāktie segvārdi saņemt pievienots"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``quay.io/centos/centos:latest`` becomes ``centos:latest``; a two-segment image such as ``debian:13`` is returned unchanged."
msgstr "``quay.io/centos/centos:latest`` kļūst ``centos:latest``; divu segmentu attēlu, piemēram, ``debian:13`` tiek atgriezta nemainītā veidā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``reason``:          why a non-deployable classification cannot serve."
msgstr "``reason``: kāpēc nevar izmantot neizmanāmu klasifikāciju."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``relay`` and ``media`` are UDP. ``stun_turn`` and its TLS variant do speak TCP, but the allocation they hand out is a UDP relay address the onion client can never receive on, so forwarding the signalling port buys nothing."
msgstr "``relay`` kā arī ``media`` ir UDP. ``stun_turn`` un tā TLS variants do runāt TCP, bet sadalījums viņi nodod ir UDP releja adresi sīpolu klients nekad nevar saņemt, tāpēc nosūtot signalizācijas ports pērk neko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``repo`` carries the repository the names come from, defined inline on the entry that needs it: a full definition (``name``/``description``/ ``baseurl``/``gpgkey``) rendered as a yum repo, ``bootstrap_package`` for a repo shipped as a package such as ``epel-release``, ``enable_existing`` to switch on a repo the distro already ships, ``pacman_section`` to uncomment a section of ``pacman.conf`` such as ``multilib``, ``copr``/``ppa`` for a community repository, or ``managed_externally`` when the role sets it up itself."
msgstr "``repo`` glabā repozitoriju nosaukumus, kas ir iegūti: pilna definīcija (``name``/``description``/ ``baseurl``/``gpgkey``) repo veidā, ``bootstrap_package`` par repo, kas nosūtīts kā pakete, piemēram, ``epel-release``, ``enable_existing`` ieslēgt repo jau kuģi, ``pacman_section`` atkomentēt ``pacman.conf`` piemēram: ``multilib``, ``copr``/``ppa`` Kopienas repozitorijam vai ``managed_externally`` kad tā pati ir izveidota."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``repos`` or ``upstreams``."
msgstr "``repos`` vai ``upstreams``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``required`` (always installed)"
msgstr "``required`` (vienmēr instalēts)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``required`` (always installed, vendored)"
msgstr "``required`` (vienmēr uzstādīta, pārdevēja)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``requirepass`` for the ``default`` (admin) user, sourced from the ``REDIS_PASSWORD`` credential."
msgstr "``requirepass`` tekstu ``default`` (admin) lietotājs, ``REDIS_PASSWORD`` credential."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``retries`` counts CONSECUTIVE failures, and a request that leaves the container is load balanced across the service VIP. With N replicas and one of them alive, a round robin never produces more than N-1 failures in a row, so a streak based check is arithmetically blind to losing all but one backend. Chaining ``samples`` requests into a single probe makes one probe cover the whole pool instead."
msgstr "``retries`` skaita CONSECUTIVE neveiksmes, un pieprasījums, kas atstāj konteineru ir slodze līdzsvarota visā pakalpojuma VIP. Ar N imitācijām un vienu no tām dzīvu, apaļš robin nekad ražo vairāk nekā N-1 neveiksmes pēc kārtas, tāpēc svītrām balstīta pārbaude ir aritmētiski akls zaudēt visu, izņemot vienu aizmuguri. Ķēdes ``samples`` pieprasījumi vienā zondē padara vienu zondi aptver visu baseinu tā vietā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``role`` may be a role name (relative to ``roles/``) or an absolute path to a role directory. Pass ``role_name`` explicitly when ``role`` is an arbitrary path whose basename is not the canonical role name."
msgstr "``role`` var būt lomu nosaukums (attiecībā pret ``roles/``) vai absolūts ceļš uz lomu direktoriju. Caurlaide ``role_name`` skaidri noteikts, kad ``role`` ir patvaļīgs ceļš, kura pamatnosaukums nav kanonisko lomu nosaukums."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/<app>/meta/server.yml`` declares ``status_codes`` keyed like ``domains.canonical``; it is the single source of truth for every prober."
msgstr "``roles/<app>/meta/server.yml`` deklarē ``status_codes`` Taustiņš ``domains.canonical``; tas ir viens avots patiesības katram probder."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` Follow `Contributing ``playwright.env.j2`` <../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md>`__ and `Contributing ``playwright.spec.js`` <../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md>`__ while creating them."
msgstr "``roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` Sekot `Contributing ``playwright.env.j2`` <../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md>`__ kā arī `Contributing ``playwright.spec.js`` <../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md>`__ radot tos."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/sys-lint/meta/services.yml`` is the SPOT for both the repository and the version of every GitHub-release lint tool. Each entry carries the ``repository`` / ``ref`` pair that ``utils.update.repository`` already scans, so the existing ``update-repository-refs`` CI job bumps the pins to the latest semver tag and opens a PR -- the same machinery that keeps ``roles/pkgmgr`` current."
msgstr "``roles/sys-lint/meta/services.yml`` ir SPOT gan repozitoriju un versiju katru GitHub atbrīvošanas lint rīks. Katrs ieraksts satur ``repository`` / ``ref`` pāri ka ``utils.update.repository`` jau skenē, tāpēc esošo ``update-repository-refs`` CI darbs izsit tapas uz jaunāko semver tagu un atver PR -- tā pati mašīna, kas uztur ``roles/pkgmgr`` straume."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js`` (copied as-is)"
msgstr "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js`` (kopēt kā ir)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/templates/package.json.j2`` (rendered per-deploy; pins ``@playwright/test`` from ``meta/services.yml.playwright.version``)"
msgstr "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/templates/package.json.j2`` (izvirpošanas instrumenti ``@playwright/test`` no ``meta/services.yml.playwright.version``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles_with_service('mcp', direction='server')`` entries."
msgstr "``roles_with_service('mcp', direction='server')`` ierakstus."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``run_after``  — project-specific role-load-order list."
msgstr "``run_after`` — ar projektu saistītu uzdevumu saraksts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``run_after`` is deliberately NOT read: it is a deploy-ordering hint, not a runtime dependency. The wider cosmos (federation peers, external bridged networks) cannot be derived from metadata and is left for the author to add."
msgstr "``run_after`` ir apzināti NELIETOT: tas ir izvietošana-kārtojot mājienu, nevis runtime atkarība. Plašāks kosmoss (Līdzdalībnieku federācija, ārējie tilti) nevar tikt atvasināts no metadatiem, un autors to var pievienot."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` validates the generated packaging metadata with each ecosystem's native parser. This installer provisions those parsers wherever the platform's package manager can: on Debian (apt) the lint container gets ``dpkg-parsechangelog`` (``dpkg-dev``), ``rpmspec`` (``rpm``) and ``rpmlint``; on Arch (pacman) a dev host gets ``namcap``."
msgstr "``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` validē ģenerētos iepakojuma metadatus ar katras ekosistēmas vietējo parseri. Šis uzstādītājs paredz šos parsers kur platformas paketes vadītājs var: uz Debian (apt) tvertnes kļūst ``dpkg-parsechangelog`` (``dpkg-dev``), ``rpmspec`` (``rpm``) kā arī ``rpmlint``; uz arkas (pakmens) dev host saņem ``namcap``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``semantic_name``  the YAML key from ``meta/volumes.yml``"
msgstr "``semantic_name`` YAML atslēga no ``meta/volumes.yml``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.<provider_key>.enabled`` must also hold. Default provider_key ``tor``"
msgstr "``services.<provider_key>.enabled`` jātur arī. Noklusētais provider_key ``tor``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.code.flavor`` picks one of ``code-oss``, ``vscodium`` or ``vscode``. The three builds conflict at package level, so the role removes the other two before installing the chosen one."
msgstr "``services.code.flavor`` izvēlas vienu no ``code-oss``, ``vscodium`` vai ``vscode``. Trīs veido konfliktu paketes līmenī, tāpēc loma noņem pārējos divus pirms uzstādīšanas izvēlēto vienu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.libretranslate``: image and version"
msgstr "``services.libretranslate``: attēls un versija"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.litellm.remote_models`` already narrowed to the providers this host holds a key for. An entry whose provider is ``mock`` answers from its own ``response`` and calls nothing."
msgstr "``services.litellm.remote_models`` jau sašaurināts uz pakalpojumu sniedzējiem šis saimnieks ir atslēga. Ieraksts, kura sniedzējs ir ``mock`` atbildes no saviem ``response`` un nesauc neko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.matomo``: enable analytics"
msgstr "``services.matomo``: dod iespēju analītiski"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.matrix.conferencing.element_call`` and ``services.matrix.conferencing.jitsi`` toggle MDAD’s Element Call / Jitsi stacks (ansible flavor only). Both default to true."
msgstr "``services.matrix.conferencing.element_call`` kā arī ``services.matrix.conferencing.jitsi`` Pārslēgt MDAD elementu zvanu / Jitsi stekus (tikai garša). Abi noklusējuma taisnība."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.openwebui.embedding_model``, ``.image_model``, ``.speech_to_text_model`` and ``.text_to_speech_model`` route embeddings, images, speech recognition and speech synthesis through the gateway; an embedding model set here also replaces the sentence-transformer the image otherwise downloads from Hugging Face on first start"
msgstr "``services.openwebui.embedding_model``, ``.image_model``, ``.speech_to_text_model`` kā arī ``.text_to_speech_model`` maršrutu iegultnes, attēli, runas atpazīšana un runas sintēze caur vārteju; iegultais modelis šeit arī aizstāj teikumu transformatoru attēlu citādi lejupielādē no Hagging Face pirmajā startā"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.redis``: enable Redis backend"
msgstr "``services.redis``: ieslēgt Redis aizmugure"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.s1.flavor`` selects which implementation answers that contract. ``laya`` runs `Laya <https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya>`__, the default; ``torch`` and ``onnx`` run `jeff <https://github.com/logan-markewich/jeff>`__ over a GLiFormer encoder, which is what the role carried before. Neither upstream ships a container image, so the role builds one and bakes the checkpoints into it. Baking keeps the deploy free of a download at container start, which is the failure mode a sibling role’s model pull already hit."
msgstr "``services.s1.flavor`` izvēlas, kura īstenošana atbild uz minēto līgumu. ``laya`` iet `Laya <https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya>`__, saistību neizpilde; ``torch`` kā arī ``onnx`` palaist `jeff <https://github.com/logan-markewich/jeff>`__ virs GLiFormer kodētājs, kas ir tas, ko loma veikta pirms. Nevienam no augšējiem kuģiem nav konteinera attēla, tāpēc tas veido vienu un tajā ieliek kontrolpunktus. Cepšana uztur izvietot bez lejupielādes pie konteinera sākuma, kas ir neveiksmes režīmā māsa loma modelis vilkt jau hit."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.volume-2-local.snapshot_mode`` (declared in ``meta/services.yml``, overridable per host from the inventory) decides whether a run uses baudolo’s ``--snapshot`` mode. **Quote the value** — YAML reads a bare ``off``/``no``/``false`` as a boolean, and the deploy asserts on the result."
msgstr "``services.volume-2-local.snapshot_mode`` (deklarēti ``meta/services.yml``, maināms uz resursdatoru no inventāra) izlemt, vai palaist izmanto baudolo s ``--snapshot`` režīms. **Citēt vērtību** — YAML skan tukša ``off``/``no``/``false`` kā boolean, un izvietošana apgalvo par rezultātu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``set hostname to {{ inventory_hostname }}`` Applies the desired hostname."
msgstr "``set hostname to {{ inventory_hostname }}`` Piemēro vēlamo datora nosaukumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``setdefault`` falls back to the supplied value only when the process env has no non-empty value for the key. ``set`` is unconditional. ``get`` reads from the builder, falling back to the process env so derived values (e.g. ``INFINITO_CONTAINER``) can be composed off previously-set keys."
msgstr "``setdefault`` Atgriežas pie piegādātās vērtības tikai tad, ja procesam env nav netukšas vērtības atslēgai. ``set`` ir beznosacījumu. ``get`` lasīt no celtnieka, krītot atpakaļ uz procesu env tik atvasinātas vērtības (Piemēram, ``INFINITO_CONTAINER``) var sastāvēt no iepriekš iestatītām atslēgām."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``source_url``:      upstream documentation or source of the MCP surface."
