msgid "`actions/create-github-app-token` declares both inputs as required and fails with `Error: Input required and not supplied: client-id`."
msgstr "`actions/create-github-app-token` deklarē gan ieejas, kā prasīts, un neizdodas ar `Error: Input required and not supplied: client-id`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`active_variants` is the per-app variant index for the round this folder represents. Apps absent from the mapping (or with an out-of- range index) fall back to variant 0. The resolved variant payload for every app in `include` is baked into the inventory as an `applications.<app>` override, so the deploy stage no longer needs a runtime variant selector — the inventory itself is variant-resolved."
msgstr "`active_variants` ir per-app varianta indekss apaļai šai mapei. Aplikāciju nav (vai ar ārpus diapazona indeksu) Atgriezties pie varianta 0. Izšķirtā varianta derīgās kravas par katru lietotni `include` tiek cepts inventārā kā `applications.<app>` izslēgt, tāpēc izvietošanas posmā vairs nav nepieciešams runtime varianta selektors — pats inventāra veids ir atrisināts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`addon` / `plugin` / `mu_plugin` / `extension` / `module` / `bridge`. Selects the install path. `bridge` denotes a network/appservice bridge addon (distinct from the `bridges:` field)."
msgstr "`addon` / `plugin` / `mu_plugin` / `extension` / `module` / `bridge`. Atlasa instalēt ceļu. `bridge` apzīmē tīkla/appservice tilta addon (atšķiras no `bridges:` lauks)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`addons` is **not inlined** under the primary entity: role-level extensions are a first-class, per-file topic under `meta/addons/` (see [Unified Addons](#unified-addons-metaaddons-)). The same applies to a role that spells the concept `plugins`/`extensions`/`modules`/`mu_plugins`: those declarations live under `meta/addons/`."
msgstr "`addons` ir **nav iekļauti** saskaņā ar primāro vienību: lomu līmeņa paplašinājumi ir pirmās klases, par failu tēmu saskaņā `meta/addons/` (skatīt [Apvienotie papildinājumi](#unified-addons-metaaddons-)). Tas pats attiecas uz lomu, kas raksturo jēdzienu `plugins`/`extensions`/`modules`/`mu_plugins`: šīs deklarācijas tiešraidē `meta/addons/`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`administrator`: single-app authenticated journey"
msgstr "`administrator`: autentificēts brauciens ar vienu lietotni"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`akaunting`, `decidim`, `fider`, `listmonk`, `pretix`, `snipe-it`, `taiga`, `penpot`, `joomla`, `suitecrm`, `kix`, `opencloud`, `opentalk`, `jitsi`, `bigbluebutton`, `erpnext` show no first-party AI surface with a configurable endpoint; revisit when upstream adds one"
msgstr "`akaunting`, `decidim`, `fider`, `listmonk`, `pretix`, `snipe-it`, `taiga`, `penpot`, `joomla`, `suitecrm`, `kix`, `opencloud`, `opentalk`, `jitsi`, `bigbluebutton`, `erpnext` nav pirmās puses AI virsmas ar konfigurējamu beigu punktu; skaties, kad augšupejošā stāvoklī pievieno vienu"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`algorithm:` defaults to `plain` when omitted."
msgstr "`algorithm:` noklusētais `plain` kad izlaists."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`alicloudkms`, `awskms`, `azurekeyvault`, `gcpckms`, `kmip`, `ocikms`, `ovhcloud`, `pkcs11`, **`static`**, `tcloudpublic`, `transit`. From v2.7.0 many become external plugins; `static` and `transit` stay built in."
msgstr "`alicloudkms`, `awskms`, `azurekeyvault`, `gcpckms`, `kmip`, `ocikms`, `ovhcloud`, `pkcs11`, **`static`**, `tcloudpublic`, `transit`. No v2.7.0 daudzi kļūst par ārējiem spraudņiem; `static` kā arī `transit` palikt iebūvēts."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`all.sh` covers every discovered application; `selection.sh` covers one or more apps passed via `apps` (or a positional argument)."
msgstr "`all.sh` attiecas uz katru atklāto pieteikumu; `selection.sh` attiecas uz vienu vai vairākām lietotnēm, kas nodotas caur `apps` (vai pozicionāls arguments)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`all.sh` discovers applications on the host via `scripts/meta/resolve/apps.sh` and runs against the full list."
msgstr "`all.sh` atklāj programmas uz resursdatora caur `scripts/meta/resolve/apps.sh` un iet pret pilnu sarakstu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`all.sh` requires:"
msgstr "`all.sh` prasa:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`all` (default)"
msgstr "`all` (noklusētais)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`allow`: pre-authorized. Additionally, `sandbox.autoAllowBashIfSandboxed: true` pre-authorizes any Bash command that runs sandboxed and matches no `deny`/`ask` rule. Agents without an equivalent OS-level sandbox MUST treat unmatched Bash as `ask`."
msgstr "`allow`: pirms atļaujas. Turklāt: `sandbox.autoAllowBashIfSandboxed: true` pirms-authorizē jebkuru Bash komandu, kas darbojas smilšu kastē un atbilst nē `deny`/`ask` noteikums. Aģentiem bez līdzvērtīga OS līmeņa smilšu kastes ir jāuztver nepārspējams Bash kā `ask`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`ansible.builtin.package` ships as a documentation-only stub; its logic lives in Ansible's action plugin. The action plugin here executes modules directly, so it must swap this marker for the host's `ansible_facts.pkg_mgr`."
msgstr "`ansible.builtin.package` kuģi kā tikai dokumentācija; tā loģika dzīvo Ansible darbības spraudnis. Darbību spraudnis šeit izpilda moduļus tieši, tāpēc tam ir jāmaina šis marķieris `ansible_facts.pkg_mgr`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`ansible` (default)"
msgstr "`ansible` (noklusētais)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`ansible` (default) wraps [matrix-docker-ansible-deploy](https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy) (MDAD). MDAD runs ~70 upstream sub-roles to deliver Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Element Call, and Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from `services.matrix.*` knobs, and disables MDAD's bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis so the central Infinito services back the stack."
msgstr "`ansible` (noklusētais) iesaiņojumi [ar matricu darbināms](https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy) (MDAD). MDAD darbojas ~70 augšpusē apakšroles piegādāt Synapse, Element, katrs atbalstīts tilts, Element Call, un Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus adatas MDAD ar nodevumu, padara MDAD inventāru no `services.matrix.*` kloķi, un atspējo MAD bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis Tātad centrālais Infinito pakalpojumi atpakaļ steku."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`api.seaweedfs.s3.*` is the public S3 endpoint and is reachable without SSO gating."
msgstr "`api.seaweedfs.s3.*` ir publiska3 ir sasniedzams bez SSO gabīšanās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`application_id` MUST refer to a role that declares an `rbac:` block in its `meta/services.yml`. The role may be tenant-aware (`rbac.tenancy.axis == \"domain\"`) or not (default)."
msgstr "`application_id` UZMANĪBU! `rbac:` bloka `meta/services.yml`. Loma var būt īrniekiem-aware (`rbac.tenancy.axis == \"domain\"`) vai nav (noklusētais)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`applications['<application_id>'].compose.services.email.<key>`, applied only when an `application_id` is passed."
msgstr "`applications['<application_id>'].compose.services.email.<key>`, piemēro tikai tad, ja: `application_id` ir pagājis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`applications['<application_id>'].services.email.<key>`, only when an `application_id` is passed."
msgstr "`applications['<application_id>'].services.email.<key>`, tikai tad, ja `application_id` ir pagājis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`applications_if_group_and_all_deps`. Recursive walk over Ansible meta `dependencies:` plus shared-service deps."
msgstr "`applications_if_group_and_all_deps`. Rekursīva pastaiga pa Ansible meta `dependencies:` plus dalīta pakalpojuma deps."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`applications` lookup 📦"
msgstr "`applications` Lookup 📦"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`apply` MUST take `(eb, ctx)` and return `None`."
msgstr "`apply` JĀŅEM `(eb, ctx)` un atpakaļ `None`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`apt-get install` (Ansible task in runner)"
msgstr "`apt-get install` (Aktīvs uzdevums skrējienā)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`apt/${INFINITO_DISTRO}.list` URL-rewrite to `package-cache:8081`"
msgstr "`apt/${INFINITO_DISTRO}.list` URL- pārrakstīt uz `package-cache:8081`"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`apt/<distro>.list`: apt sources, one file per `INFINITO_DISTRO`. The matching file is mounted at `/etc/apt/sources.list.d/package-cache.list`. `apt/debian.list` routes apt through `apt-debian`, `apt/ubuntu.list` through `apt-ubuntu`; the pacman/dnf distros get an empty file, because `apt-get update` fails as a whole on a single unreachable source and must not carry a foreign distro's entry."
msgstr "`apt/<distro>.list`: apt avoti, viens fails katram `INFINITO_DISTRO`. Atbilstošs fails ir montēts `/etc/apt/sources.list.d/package-cache.list`. `apt/debian.list` caurceļiem `apt-debian`, `apt/ubuntu.list` caur `apt-ubuntu`; Pacman / dnf distros saņemt tukšu failu, jo `apt-get update` neizdodas kopumā vienā nesasniedzamā avotā un nedrīkst veikt ārvalstu distro ierakstu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`apt` (mirrors)"
msgstr "`apt` (spoguļi)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`architecture` is an axis of the matrix row, assigned per row by [axes.py](../../../utils/github/variant/axes.py) next to `mode`, `tor`, `distro` and `filesystem`."
msgstr "`architecture` ir matricas rindas ass, ko rindā piešķir [axes.py](../../../utils/github/variant/axes.py) blakus `mode`, `tor`, `distro` kā arī `filesystem`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`ask`: requires per-invocation operator confirmation in the current conversation. A prior confirmation from another conversation MUST NOT be reused."
msgstr "`ask`: prasa per-uzaicinājuma operatora apstiprinājumu pašreizējā sarunā. Iepriekšēju apstiprinājumu no citas sarunas NEDRĪKST izmantot atkārtoti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth: none` MUST fail lint unless the endpoint is bound to localhost or an internal-only network and the role README documents why authentication is impossible upstream."
msgstr "`auth: none` MUST neizdoties lint ja vien galapunkts ir saistīts ar localhost vai tikai iekšējais tīkls un lomu LASĪTME dokumentus, kāpēc autentifikācija nav iespējama augšpus."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth: none` requires `exposure: internal`."
msgstr "`auth: none` prasa `exposure: internal`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: Home Assistant tvērums žetonu uz kontu, kas kaltas to. Šī izvietošana kaļ to administratoram, tāpēc pienāk zvans kā administrators, kurš jautāja klientam. Elementu riska darījums joprojām ierobežo sasniegto. Nokļūšana rīku serverī ir ieslēgta uz lomas `mcp` RBAC grupa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account's rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: Mattermost ierobežo zvanu konta žetonu pieder. Šī izvietošana naudas kaltuves, ka personīgo piekļuvi žetonu administratora konta, tāpēc zvani ierodas ar šī konta tiesības, kurš lūdza. Instrumentu servera sasniegšana ir atkarīga no lomas `mcp` RBAC grupa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account's rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: API marķieris tiek izsniegts administratora kontā, tāpēc katrs zvans nes šī konta tiesības neatkarīgi no tā, kurš lūdza klientam. Instrumentu servera sasniegšana ir atkarīga no lomas `mcp` RBAC grupa, kas ir atsevišķa dotācija no administrēšanas Jenkins."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: the personal access token is minted against the `root` account and stored under the `administrator` key, so every call carries that account's rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: personīgā pieeja žetonu kaļ pret `root` konts un glabājas zem `administrator` atslēgu, tāpēc katrs zvans ietver šī konta tiesības neatkarīgi no tā, kurš lūdza klientam. Instrumentu servera sasniegšana ir atkarīga no lomas `mcp` RBAC grupa, kas ir atsevišķa dotācija no administrēšanas GitLab."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: administrator`: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account's rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group."
msgstr "`auth_subject: administrator`: tīmekļa pakalpojuma marķierierīce tiek izdota pret administratora kontu, tāpēc zvans nes šī konta tiesības neatkarīgi no tā, kurš lūdza klientam. Pievienotās funkcijas ir tikai lasāms, kas ierobežo to, ko šīs tiesības var darīt šeit. Instrumentu servera sasniegšana ir atkarīga no lomas `mcp` RBAC grupa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: service_account | administrator` requires an explicit `tools.mutating_tools_enabled: false`."
msgstr "`auth_subject: service_account | administrator` pieprasa skaidru `tools.mutating_tools_enabled: false`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: service_account`. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter's allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "`auth_subject: service_account`. Zvans ierodas Baserow kā galapunkta īpašnieks neatkarīgi no tā, kurš lūdza klientam, un sasniedz tikai vienu darba vietu, kas pieder šim kontam. Tas ir otrs posms zem adaptera letlista, nevis tā aizstājējs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: service_account`: [`tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml) creates the account `NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME` with `occ user:add` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under `mcp.credential.owner`. Every call carries that account's rights, not the administrator's, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role's `mcp` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "`auth_subject: service_account`: [`tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml) izveido kontu `NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME` kur: `occ user:add` ja tā ir pazudusi, izkaltē lietotnes paroli pret šo kontu un glabā to zem `mcp.credential.owner`. Katrs zvans ietver šī konta tiesības, nevis administratora, neatkarīgi no tā, kurš lūdza klientam. Instrumentu servera sasniegšana ir atkarīga no lomas `mcp` RBAC grupa, kas ir atsevišķa dotācija no līdzdalības Nextcloud kontu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: user` and `auth: oidc` claim that an MCP call executes with the requesting end user's permissions. A `delegation:` block records the audit that backs the claim; without it, [`test_mcp_schema.py`](../../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_schema.py) rejects the role."
msgstr "`auth_subject: user` kā arī `auth: oidc` apgalvo, ka MCP izsaukums tiek izpildīts ar pieprasītā gala lietotāja atļaujām. A `delegation:` bloks dokumentē revīziju, kas atbalsta prasījumu; bez tā, [`test_mcp_schema.py`](../../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_schema.py) noraida lomu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: user` may be set only after the exact client and server prove authorization-code or token-exchange behaviour, token refresh, audience binding, revocation and expiry. A static bearer issued to the deployment is not on-behalf-of and stays `service_account`. Client-side group gating controls access to that service account; it does not recreate the caller's permissions."
msgstr "`auth_subject: user` var iestatīt tikai pēc tam, kad precīzs klients un serveris pierāda autorizācijas kodu vai marķieru apmaiņas uzvedību, marķieri atsvaidzināšanu, auditorijas piesaisti, atsaukšanu un derīguma termiņu. Statiskais uzrādītājs, kas izdots izvietošanai, nav puse no un paliek `service_account`. Klienta puses grupas žetonu kontrolē piekļuvi šim pakalpojuma kontam; tas nerada atpakaļ zvanītāja atļaujas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject: user` or `auth: oidc` requires a `delegation` block; see [delegation.md](mcp/delegation.md)."
msgstr "`auth_subject: user` vai `auth: oidc` nepieciešama `delegation` bloku; sk. [delegation.md](mcp/delegation.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_subject` MUST be `user` where upstream supports per-user authorization. `service_account` and `administrator` MUST keep mutating tools disabled by default."
msgstr "`auth_subject` Jābūt `user` ja iepriekšējā posma atbalsts katram lietotājam atļaujas. `service_account` kā arī `administrator` Pēc noklusējuma ir jātur mutatis mutandis atslēgti rīki."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth_type: bearer` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "`auth_type: bearer` ar marķierierīci no meklēšanas datiem"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auth` reads `environment` and `tls`."
msgstr "`auth` lasītājs `environment` kā arī `tls`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`auto` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as `baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>`, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated `btrfs`/`zfs` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the `.baudolo-*` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "`auto` ir padomdevēja un nekad neizdodas vienība — katrs atteikums ir pieteicies uz žurnālu kā `baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>`, tāpēc pārbaudiet tur, ja resursdators jūs gaidāt momentuzņēmumu nav. A norādīts `btrfs`/`zfs` neizpilda vienības vietā, kas ir punkts, norādot to. Pirms katra momentuzņēmuma palaidējs arī noņem `.baudolo-*` atstāj nogalināts palaist atstāj iekšpusē datu saknes."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`backend`: `cloud` or `chezmoi`"
msgstr "`backend`: `cloud` vai `chezmoi`"

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, no-python-format, python-brace-format
msgid "`base.yml.j2` embeds an engine sidecar only `{% if enabled and not shared %}`."
msgstr "`base.yml.j2` iebūvēti tikai dzinēja blakusvāģi `{% if enabled and not shared %}`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`base_dir` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "`base_dir` (virkne): bāzes mape CA failiem"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`base` prepares the workspace and is a prerequisite for the other two. `compose` and `swarm` are independent of each other, which is what lets CI run them as separate jobs with a budget each."
msgstr "`base` sagatavo darba vietu un ir priekšnoteikums pārējiem diviem. `compose` kā arī `swarm` ir neatkarīgi viens no otra, kas ļauj CI vadīt tos kā atsevišķas darba vietas ar budžetu katram."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`bash roles/svc-cache-package/files/shell/bootstrap.sh` (after `make dotenv` or sourcing `scripts/meta/env/load.sh`)"
msgstr "`bash roles/svc-cache-package/files/shell/bootstrap.sh` (pēc `make dotenv` vai iegūšanas `scripts/meta/env/load.sh`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`bench new-site` uses the central MariaDB's `root` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "`bench new-site` izmanto centrālo MariaDB's `root` izveidot uz vietas DB pirmajā izvietojumā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`biber` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (`ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true`, [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2)); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the `services.sso.enabled: false` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native `biber` user exists, so [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) renders `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`. The `administrator` and `guest` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "`biber` tikai jebkad pastāv iekšā EspoCRM caur OIDC automātisko piegādi (`ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true`, [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2)); pati loma sēklas tikai administratora kontu. Divos `services.sso.enabled: false` matricas varianti, ka nodrošinājuma ceļš ir pagājis un nav dzimtā `biber` lietotājs eksistē, tāpēc [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) atveidojumi `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`. `administrator` kā arī `guest` persona, kas darbojas katrā variantā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`biber`: single-app authenticated journey"
msgstr "`biber`: autentificēts brauciens ar vienu lietotni"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`branch_prefix.sh` validates that the PR branch prefix matches the detected scope; see [branch.md](../../../../docs/contributing/artefact/git/branch.md) for the authoritative list of valid prefixes and their CI impact"
msgstr "`branch_prefix.sh` apstiprina, ka PR filiāles prefikss atbilst noteiktajai jomai; skatīt [branch.md](../../../../docs/contributing/artefact/git/branch.md) spēkā esošo prefiksu autoritatīvajam sarakstam un to ietekmei uz KI"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`bridges` (optional) MUST be a non-empty list when present. Each entry MUST name a service key that exists in the same role's `meta/services.yml`. Omit the key entirely when the addon has no cross-role dependency."
msgstr "`bridges` (Pēc izvēles) Jābūt netukšam sarakstam, ja tāds ir. Katram ierakstam jānosauc pakalpojuma atslēga, kas pastāv vienā lomā `meta/services.yml`. Omit galvenais pilnībā, ja addon nav savstarpējas atkarības."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`build.extra_hosts` DNS-hijack + frontend HTTP"
msgstr "`build.extra_hosts` DNS-hibrīds + HTTP priekšpuse"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`build_dev_inventory` is the SPOT that turns a `DevInventorySpec` into a fully baked inventory folder via the `infinito administration inventory provision` CLI. `build_dev_inventory_matrix` is the orchestrator: it runs the planner and builds every round's folder."
msgstr "`build_dev_inventory` ir SPOT, kas kļūst a `DevInventorySpec` uz pilnībā izceptu inventāra mapi, izmantojot `infinito administration inventory provision` CLI. `build_dev_inventory_matrix` ir orķestru: tas vada plānotāju un veido katra raunda mapi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`build_dev_inventory` reads `spec.variant_selectors()` from the planner. When the round pins any variant, it appends `--app-variants <JSON>` to the `infinito administration inventory provision` invocation with the per-app `{app_id: variant_index}` mapping."
msgstr "`build_dev_inventory` lasītājs `spec.variant_selectors()` no plānotāja. Kad apaļas tapas jebkuru variantu, tas papildina `--app-variants <JSON>` uz `infinito administration inventory provision` atsaukums ar vienu lietotni `{app_id: variant_index}` kartēšana."

# translated-by: libretranslate
