msgstr "`resource_readonly`: pārbaudītie noteikumi par ierobežota, neslepena, publicēta satura, kas noteikts kā MCP resursi, atklāšanu, nevis izlikšanos par to API."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`role` MUST appear under `rbac.roles.<role>` or be the implicit `administrator` that the role-list contract auto-adds."
msgstr "`role` JĀATKAR `rbac.roles.<role>` vai netieši `administrator` ka lomu sarakstu līgumu automātiski pievieno."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`role` is the directory under ``roles/``, `app` the role's application_id -- the value the deployment whitelist and `application_allowed` speak in."
msgstr "`role` ir direktorija zem ``roles/``, `app` loma application_id -- vērtība izvietošanas balto sarakstu un `application_allowed` runā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` Follow [Contributing `playwright.env.j2`](../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md) and [Contributing `playwright.spec.js`](../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md) while creating them."
msgstr "`roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` Sekot [Palīdzība `playwright.env.j2`](../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md) kā arī [Palīdzība `playwright.spec.js`](../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md) radot tos."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` exists."
msgstr "`roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` pastāv."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/<role>/meta/services.yml` for anything an operator may override, because the inventory's `applications.<role>` block is deep-merged on top of it and `lookup('config', application_id, '<path>')` reads the result."
msgstr "`roles/<role>/meta/services.yml` par jebko operators var ignorēt, jo inventāra `applications.<role>` bloks ir dziļi apvienoti uz tā un `lookup('config', application_id, '<path>')` lasa rezultātu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/<role>/vars/main.yml` for values derived from that configuration, and for those the role fixes. Role vars outrank inventory variables, so a value placed here cannot be overridden per host."
msgstr "`roles/<role>/vars/main.yml` vērtībām, kas iegūtas no minētās konfigurācijas, un tām, kas noteiktas lomu noteikšanā. Loma vars pārspēja inventāra mainīgos, tāpēc šeit novietoto vērtību nevar ignorēt uz resursdatoru."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/sys-ca-selfsigned/`. generates the self-signed Root CA inside the container"
msgstr "`roles/sys-ca-selfsigned/`. ģenerē pašparakstīto saknes CA konteinera iekšpusē"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/sys-ca-selfsigned/`. role that generates the self-signed Root CA inside the container"
msgstr "`roles/sys-ca-selfsigned/`. loma, kas rada pašparakstīto saknes CA konteinera iekšpusē"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/test-e2e-playwright/defaults/main.yml` reads the host value into `test_e2e_playwright_keep` via `lookup('env', 'INFINITO_PLAYWRIGHT_KEEP')`. Inventory MAY override the role variable per environment in `group_vars` or `host_vars`."
msgstr "`roles/test-e2e-playwright/defaults/main.yml` nolasa resursdatora vērtību `test_e2e_playwright_keep` caur `lookup('env', 'INFINITO_PLAYWRIGHT_KEEP')`. Inventarizācija var ignorēt lomu mainīgo atkarībā no vides `group_vars` vai `host_vars`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js` (copied as-is)"
msgstr "`roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js` (kopēt kā ir)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js` switches `trace`, `screenshot`, and `video` to `on` when the container value is `true`. It otherwise leaves the failure-only defaults (`retain-on-failure` for trace and video, `only-on-failure` for screenshot)."
msgstr "`roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js` slēdži `trace`, `screenshot`, un `video` līdz `on` ja konteinera vērtība ir `true`. Citādi atstāj tikai neveiksmes noklusējuma (`retain-on-failure` mikrofoniem un video, `only-on-failure` ekrānattēlam)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/test-e2e-playwright/tasks/02_run_one.yml` forwards the resolved value into the Playwright container as `-e INFINITO_PLAYWRIGHT_KEEP={{ test_e2e_playwright_keep }}`."
msgstr "`roles/test-e2e-playwright/tasks/02_run_one.yml` pāradresē izšķirto vērtību Playwright konteinerā kā `-e INFINITO_PLAYWRIGHT_KEEP={{ test_e2e_playwright_keep }}`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/test-e2e-playwright/templates/package.json.j2` (rendered per-deploy; pins `@playwright/test` from `meta/services.yml.playwright.version`)"
msgstr "`roles/test-e2e-playwright/templates/package.json.j2` (izvirpošanas instrumenti `@playwright/test` no `meta/services.yml.playwright.version`)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles/web-app-taiga/templates/style.css.j2` is the Taiga role override."
msgstr "`roles/web-app-taiga/templates/style.css.j2` ir Taiga lomu pārslēgšana."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`roles` (**required**) — the set of roles to deploy onto the runner (accepts space- and comma-separated lists, matching the normalisation used by [cli/administration/deploy/dedicated/command.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/runner/command.py))."
msgstr "`roles` (**nepieciešams**) — lomu kopums, ko izvietot skrējējam; (pieņem ar atstarpi un komatu atdalītus sarakstus, kas atbilst normalizēšanai, ko izmanto [cli/administration/deploy/dedicated/command.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/runner/command.py))."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`routine.yml`: wrapper with immediate compose-up"
msgstr "`routine.yml`: iesaiņojums ar tūlītēju kompo-up"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`routine/backup/base.sh` (+ per-host routines in [`routine/backup/`](routine/backup/))"
msgstr "`routine/backup/base.sh` (+ uz host rutīnas in [`routine/backup/`](routine/backup/))"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`run_after:` entries are role names, not service keys."
msgstr "`run_after:` ieraksti ir lomu nosaukumi, nevis servisa atslēgas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`run_after:` from `meta/services.yml.<entity>.run_after` is an ordering hint only (see [base.md](role/services/base.md)); it MUST NOT pull roles into the include set."
msgstr "`run_after:` no `meta/services.yml.<entity>.run_after` ir tikai pasūtīšanas padoms (skatīt [base.md](role/services/base.md)); tas nedrīkst pull lomas iekļaut komplektu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`run_after:` walk"
msgstr "`run_after:` staigāt"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`run_after:`, when present, is a non-empty list of role names."
msgstr "`run_after:`, ja ir, ir netukšs saraksts ar lomu nosaukumiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`run_after` Dependency Tests ⏭️"
msgstr "`run_after` Atkarības testi ️"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`run_after` Rules"
msgstr "`run_after` Noteikumi"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`run_after` and `lifecycle` 🌱"
msgstr "`run_after` kā arī `lifecycle` 🌱"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`run_once_web_app_mailu is defined` assertion failed in `sys-svc-mail`, indicating the service-loader did not preload Mailu in the keycloak-only deploy path."
msgstr "`run_once_web_app_mailu is defined` apgalvojums nav izpildīts `sys-svc-mail`, norādot, ka kravas saņēmējs nav iepriekš ielādēts Mailu Atslēgas aizslēga izvēršanas ceļā."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`runner_docker_base` defaults to `/mnt/docker`. Override via inventory `host_vars` for non-standard machines."
msgstr "`runner_docker_base` noklusētais `/mnt/docker`. Pārrakstīt, izmantojot inventāra `host_vars` nestandarta mašīnām."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`s3_prefix`: list, head and get through a dedicated read-only policy restricted to named buckets and prefixes;"
msgstr "`s3_prefix`: saraksts, vadītājs un saņemt caur īpašu lasāmu politiku, kas attiecas tikai uz nosauktiem spaiņiem un prefiksiem;"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`sandbox.allowUnsandboxedCommands: false`: MUST NOT use per-call escape hatches (e.g. `dangerouslyDisableSandbox`)."
msgstr "`sandbox.allowUnsandboxedCommands: false`: NEDRĪKST izmantot avārijas lūkas pēc izsaukuma (Piemēram, `dangerouslyDisableSandbox`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`sandbox.filesystem`: `allowWrite` bounds write scope; `denyRead` paths MUST NOT be read."
msgstr "`sandbox.filesystem`: `allowWrite` ierobežojumi rakstīšanas darbības joma; `denyRead` ceļus NEDRĪKST nolasīt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`sandbox.network`: outbound calls MUST go to hosts matching `allowedDomains`. Unix-socket connections are permitted only if `allowAllUnixSockets: true`; listening on local ports is permitted only if `allowLocalBinding: true`."
msgstr "`sandbox.network`: izejošie zvani jādodas uz saimniekiem saskaņošanas `allowedDomains`. Unix-socket savienojumi ir atļauta tikai tad, ja `allowAllUnixSockets: true`; klausīšanās vietējās ostās ir atļauta tikai tad, ja `allowLocalBinding: true`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`schedule`: cron-based periodic runs (UTC)."
msgstr "`schedule`: periodiskie braucieni, kuru pamatā ir hronoloģija (UTC)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`scope.sh` resolves whether a Pull Request is agents-only, documentation-only, or full scope"
msgstr "`scope.sh` atrisina jautājumu, vai “Pull” pieprasījums ir tikai aģenti, tikai dokumentācija vai pilna darbības joma"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`scripts/install/package.sh` builds and installs the local package for the current distro (Arch, Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora), so dependency resolution is performed by the distro package manager from package metadata."
msgstr "`scripts/install/package.sh` būvē un uzstāda vietējo pakotni pašreizējam distro (Arch, Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora), tāpēc atkarība izšķirtspēju veic distro paketes pārvaldnieks no paketes metadatiem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`scripts/meta/wait/mirrors.sh` waits for fork PRs until all required mirror images are available in GHCR before letting the deploy tests proceed. This is necessary because fork PRs cannot push images themselves; the `pull_request_target` event handles that."
msgstr "`scripts/meta/wait/mirrors.sh` Gaida dakšu PR, līdz GHCR ir pieejami visi nepieciešamie spoguļattēli, pirms atlaiž izvietošanas testus. Tas ir nepieciešams, jo dakšveida PR nevar virzīt attēlus paši; `pull_request_target` notikums rīkojas, ka."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`scripts/tests/deploy/local/exec/container.sh` is a direct-entry shell script example."
msgstr "`scripts/tests/deploy/local/exec/container.sh` ir tiešā ieraksta čaulas skripta piemērs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`scripts/tests/deploy/utils/filesystem/resolve.sh` serves a kind only when the **host kernel** carries it: `zfs` needs `/dev/zfs` or a `modinfo zfs` hit, the others need an entry in `/proc/filesystems` or a module. The distro images carry only the userland (`scripts/install/filesystem.sh`)."
msgstr "`scripts/tests/deploy/utils/filesystem/resolve.sh` izmanto tikai tad, ja **saimniekaugs** pārvadā: `zfs` vajadzības `/dev/zfs` vai a `modinfo zfs` hit, pārējie nepieciešams ieraksts `/proc/filesystems` vai modulis. Distro attēli satur tikai lietotāju zemi (`scripts/install/filesystem.sh`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`secrets.credentials.*` paths are populated by `apply_schema()` at `applications.<app>.secrets.credentials.<…>`, so the credential file obeys the same file-root rule as every other `meta/<topic>.yml`."
msgstr "`secrets.credentials.*` ceļus apdzīvo `apply_schema()` datums `applications.<app>.secrets.credentials.<…>`, tāpēc credential datne atbilst tam pašam faila root noteikumam kā visi citi `meta/<topic>.yml`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`selection.sh` requires the caller to supply the application set explicitly."
msgstr "`selection.sh` pieprasa, lai zvanītājs piegādātu tieši noteikto pieteikumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`selection.sh` requires:"
msgstr "`selection.sh` prasa:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`semaphoreui/semaphore` (Docker Hub + `ghcr.io`); pin a concrete stable `2.x` semver (no `:latest`)."
msgstr "`semaphoreui/semaphore` (Docker Hub + `ghcr.io`); pin betona stallis `2.x` semver (nav `:latest`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`server` Block Tests 🛡️"
msgstr "`server` Bloka testi 🛡️"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`service_key` MUST name an existing top-level service entry in the same `meta/services.yml`, and `port_key` MUST name an existing key under `services.<service_key>.ports.local`."
msgstr "`service_key` MUST nosaukt esošo augstākā līmeņa pakalpojumu ierakstu tajā pašā `meta/services.yml`, un `port_key` UZVĀRDS esošam taustiņam zem `services.<service_key>.ports.local`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`services.<engine>.enabled: true` + `shared: false` -> **embedded** sidecar (current behaviour), for single-host / opt-out."
msgstr "`services.<engine>.enabled: true` + `shared: false` - BAR **iegults** blakusvāģis (pašreizējā uzvedība;), par viena uzņēmēja / atteikšanās ."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`services.<engine>.enabled: true` + `shared: true` -> **central**: the consumer connects to the central engine over the shared cross-stack network using the `<engine>` lookup and its own provisioned credentials."
msgstr "`services.<engine>.enabled: true` + `shared: true` - BAR **centrālā**: patērētājs pieslēdzas centrālajam dzinējam, izmantojot kopīgo pārrobežu tīklu, izmantojot `<engine>` atsauksme un tās nodrošinātās pilnvaras."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`services.code.flavor` picks one of `code-oss`, `vscodium` or `vscode`. The three builds conflict at package level, so the role removes the other two before installing the chosen one."
msgstr "`services.code.flavor` izvēlas vienu no `code-oss`, `vscodium` vai `vscode`. Trīs veido konfliktu paketes līmenī, tāpēc loma noņem pārējos divus pirms uzstādīšanas izvēlēto vienu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`services.libretranslate`: image and version"
msgstr "`services.libretranslate`: attēls un versija"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`services.matomo`: enable analytics"
msgstr "`services.matomo`: dod iespēju analītiski"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`services.matrix.conferencing.element_call` and `services.matrix.conferencing.jitsi` toggle MDAD's Element Call / Jitsi stacks (ansible flavor only). Both default to true."
msgstr "`services.matrix.conferencing.element_call` kā arī `services.matrix.conferencing.jitsi` Pārslēgt MDAD elementu izsaukumu / Jitsi stekus (tikai garša). Abi noklusējuma taisnība."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`services.openwebui.embedding_model`, `.image_model`, `.speech_to_text_model` and `.text_to_speech_model` route embeddings, images, speech recognition and speech synthesis through the gateway; an embedding model set here also replaces the sentence-transformer the image otherwise downloads from Hugging Face on first start"
msgstr "`services.openwebui.embedding_model`, `.image_model`, `.speech_to_text_model` kā arī `.text_to_speech_model` maršrutu iegultnes, attēli, runas atpazīšana un runas sintēze caur vārteju; iegultais modelis šeit arī aizstāj teikumu transformatoru attēlu citādi lejupielādē no Hagging Face pirmajā startā"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`services.redis`: enable Redis backend"
msgstr "`services.redis`: ieslēgt Redis aizmugure"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`services.s1.flavor` selects which implementation answers that contract. `laya` runs [Laya](https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya), the default; `torch` and `onnx` run [jeff](https://github.com/logan-markewich/jeff) over a GLiFormer encoder, which is what the role carried before. Neither upstream ships a container image, so the role builds one and bakes the checkpoints into it. Baking keeps the deploy free of a download at container start, which is the failure mode a sibling role's model pull already hit."
msgstr "`services.s1.flavor` izvēlas, kura īstenošana atbild uz minēto līgumu. `laya` iet [Laya](https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya), saistību neizpilde; `torch` kā arī `onnx` palaist [jeff](https://github.com/logan-markewich/jeff) virs GLiFormer kodētājs, kas ir tas, ko loma veikta pirms. Nevienam no augšējiem kuģiem nav konteinera attēla, tāpēc tas veido vienu un tajā ieliek kontrolpunktus. Cepšana uztur izvietot bez lejupielādes pie konteinera startu, kas ir neveiksmes režīmā māsa loma modelis velk jau hit."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`services.volume-2-local.snapshot_mode` (declared in `meta/services.yml`, overridable per host from the inventory) decides whether a run uses baudolo's `--snapshot` mode. **Quote the value** — YAML reads a bare `off`/`no`/`false` as a boolean, and the deploy asserts on the result."
msgstr "`services.volume-2-local.snapshot_mode` (deklarēti `meta/services.yml`, maināms uz resursdatoru no inventāra) izlemt, vai palaist izmanto baudolo s `--snapshot` režīms. **Citēt vērtību** — YAML skan tukša `off`/`no`/`false` kā boolean, un izvietošana apgalvo par rezultātu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`set hostname to {{ inventory_hostname }}`   Applies the desired hostname."
msgstr "`set hostname to {{ inventory_hostname }}` Piemēro vēlamo datora nosaukumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`setdefault` is the operator-override contract: exporting a key changes it and the change persists. That persistence is why it MUST NOT carry a value an environment declares for a single run. [Makefile](../../Makefile) exports `BASH_ENV`, so every make recipe sources `.env` — a value adopted once is re-exported into every later recipe and into every container that mounts the repo, and a per-run decision has silently become a property of the machine."
msgstr "`setdefault` ir operatora/pārņēmēja līgums: eksports galvenās izmaiņas to un izmaiņas turpinās. Šī noturība ir iemesls, kāpēc tai NEDRĪKST būt vērtīgai videi, kas deklarēta vienam braucienam. [Makefile](../../Makefile) eksports `BASH_ENV`, tāpēc katru padarīt receptes avoti `.env` — vienu reizi pieņemta vērtība tiek atkārtoti eksportēta katrā vēlākā receptē un katrā konteinerā, kas nostiprina repo, un lēmums pēc kārtas ir klusi kļuvis par mašīnas īpašumu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`settings.BASEROW_OPENAI_BASE_URL` reaches the OpenAI client at `backend/src/baserow/core/generative_ai/generative_ai_model_types.py:288`, but the only two surfaces that ever send a prompt live in `baserow_premium` and both open with `LicenseHandler.raise_if_user_doesnt_have_feature(PREMIUM, request.user, workspace)`: `AsyncGenerateAIFieldValuesView` and `GenerateFormulaWithAIView` (`premium/backend/src/baserow_premium/api/fields/views.py`). An unlicensed deployment configures the endpoint and can never reach it"
msgstr "`settings.BASEROW_OPENAI_BASE_URL` sasniedz OpenAI klientu `backend/src/baserow/core/generative_ai/generative_ai_model_types.py:288`, bet tikai divas virsmas, kas jebkad sūtīt uzvedni dzīvot `baserow_premium` un abus atvērt ar `LicenseHandler.raise_if_user_doesnt_have_feature(PREMIUM, request.user, workspace)`: `AsyncGenerateAIFieldValuesView` kā arī `GenerateFormulaWithAIView` (`premium/backend/src/baserow_premium/api/fields/views.py`). Nelicencēta izvietošana konfigurē galapunktu un nekad nevar sasniegt to"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`shared` MUST mean that other Infinito.Nexus roles MAY discover and consume the MCP endpoint through the applications lookup."
msgstr "`shared` Jānozīmē, ka Infinito.Nexus lomas MAI atklāt un patērēt MCP beigu punktu caur pieteikumu lookup."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`size-gb` (positional)"
msgstr "`size-gb` (pozicionāls)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`skipped` counts as passed, so an empty chunk never blocks the chain. After fixing what broke a sweep, `resume_from_chunk` re-enters at that index instead of re-running the green chunks. Both are inputs on `entry-manual-steer.yml`; the other entry points take the defaults. A retrigger carries the source run's `chunk_gate` over unless `infinito administration deploy ci trigger --chunk-gate false` overrides it; the `i8ciallon` alias is `i8ciall` with that override, for sweeps that should report every chunk before anyone looks."
msgstr "`skipped` skaitīt kā pagājis, tāpēc tukšs gabals nekad bloķē ķēdi. Pēc noteikšanas, kas lauza slaucīšana, `resume_from_chunk` Atgriežas pēc šī indeksa, nevis atkārtoti vada zaļos gabalus. Abi ir dati par `entry-manual-steer.yml`; pārējie ieejas punkti veikt noklusējuma. Retrigers nes avota palaisto `chunk_gate` virs `infinito administration deploy ci trigger --chunk-gate false` aizstāj to; `i8ciallon` aizstājvārdu `i8ciall` ar šo atslēgu, par slaucīšanu, kas ziņot katru gabalu, pirms kāds izskatās."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`socket.connect` time to the resolved address on `:443`"
msgstr "`socket.connect` laiks līdz adresei `:443`"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`socket.getaddrinfo` resolution time + returned addresses"
msgstr "`socket.getaddrinfo` Noregulējuma laiks + sūtītās adreses"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`socket.gethostname()` with a `local` fallback for sandboxed hosts that fail the syscall."
msgstr "`socket.gethostname()` ar `local` rezerves smilšu kastes saimniekiem, kas neizdosies syscall."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`source_url` and `notes` MUST carry the upstream provenance of the surface. They live in the role because the role owns them; the audit artifact derives its provenance columns from here and MUST NOT keep a second copy. Version numbers do not belong here: the deployed version already lives in `meta/services.yml`, and a second copy in `meta/mcp.yml` records only when somebody last looked, which nothing enforces and no consumer reads."
msgstr "`source_url` kā arī `notes` JĀVEIC virsmas pirmavots. Viņi dzīvo lomu, jo loma pieder viņiem; audita artifact iegūst tās pirmavota slejas no šejienes un NEDRĪKST paturēt otru kopiju. Versijas numuri nepieder šeit: izvērstā versija jau dzīvo `meta/services.yml`, un otrais eksemplārs `meta/mcp.yml` ieraksti tikai tad, kad kāds pēdējo reizi izskatījās, kas nekas improvizē un neviens patērētājs lasa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`source` (required) MUST be one of `upstream` (installed from the app's own registry), `bundled` (ships with the image), `vendored` (committed under `roles/<role>/files/`), or `built` (compiled/zipped during the play, e.g. the Joomla OIDC plugin)."
msgstr "`source` (nepieciešams) Jābūt vienam no `upstream` (instalēta no paša lietotnes reģistra), `bundled` (kuģi ar attēlu), `vendored` (saistības piešķirtas saskaņā ar `roles/<role>/files/`), vai `built` (spēles laikā apkopota/zipped, piemēram, Joomla OIDC spraudnis)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`sources`  — pick the right loader for a log path, CSV path, or URL."
msgstr "`sources` — izvēlieties pareizo ielādētāju žurnāla ceļam, CSV ceļam vai URL."

